---
source: xtask/src/tests.rs
expression: json_v2
---
{
  "annotations": [
    {
      "comment": "This pertains to the high-level server implementation, as the\nauthority of the data being sent is transparent to h3.\n",
      "id": "8843f05493cadb1a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Where multiple tenants share space on the same server, that server MUST ensure that tenants are not able to push representations of resources that they do not have authority over.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/10.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be enforced by the user, as h3 may not be able to\ndetermine the nature of the content.\n",
      "id": "79eb79f93938496c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Implementations communicating on a secure channel MUST NOT compress content that includes both confidential and attacker-controlled data unless separate compression contexts are used for each source of data.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/10.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is up to the user to decide.\n",
      "id": "244041e7aff572a3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Compression MUST NOT be used if the source of data cannot be reliably determined.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/10.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "38928d3bb7612f7a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "If an entry is present in only one registry, every effort SHOULD be made to avoid assigning the corresponding value to an unrelated operation.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "2fbe4bd25f5fc64f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "Expert reviewers MAY reject unrelated registrations that would conflict with the same value in the corresponding registry.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "cd9cd268ec86e812",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following field: Frame Type:  A name or label for the frame type.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "d2dad16d0d77680e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "Specifications of frame types MUST include a description of the frame layout and its semantics, including any parts of the frame that are conditionally present.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "5d6ff86b8878eacb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe) MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "83e4295d21417b1f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "If an entry is present in only one registry, every effort SHOULD be made to avoid assigning the corresponding value to an unrelated operation.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "6a3a99106bbab454",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "Expert reviewers MAY reject unrelated registrations that would conflict with the same value in the corresponding registry.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "e3a1c102e5f4d29d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following fields: Setting Name:  A symbolic name for the setting.  Specifying a setting name is optional.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "70eee5eb6c38b250",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Default:  The value of the setting unless otherwise indicated.  A default SHOULD be the most restrictive possible value.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "bc3ec3bb6a5b0ad0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe) MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "102e356af49f054c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Use of values that are registered in the \"HTTP/2 Error Code\" registry is discouraged, and expert reviewers MAY reject such registrations.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "fda8e3e12e46b03c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "Permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following field: Name:  A name for the error code.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "0a2c0a33fca49024",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe) MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "3a5c239049088071",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following fields: Stream Type:  A name or label for the stream type.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "30be05c14c3a81c5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "Specifications for permanent registrations MUST include a description of the stream type, including the layout and semantics of the stream contents.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to IANA registration.\n",
      "id": "ce69f635e6db5cf0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe) MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/11.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Connection establishment is handled by the user and the QUIC\ncomponent.\n",
      "id": "8f5cc95dc3bae598",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "On receipt of an Alt-Svc record indicating HTTP/3 support, a client MAY attempt to establish a QUIC connection to the indicated host and port; if this connection is successful, the client can send HTTP requests using the mapping described in this document.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement pertains to the high-level implementation.\n",
      "id": "dac660f5663d9ad9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Prior to making requests for an origin whose scheme is not \"https\", the client MUST ensure the server is willing to serve that scheme.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be enforced by the TLS implementation, as h3 does not\ninspect certificate messages.\n",
      "id": "dfc838f7590c0779",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Upon receiving a server certificate in the TLS handshake, the client MUST verify that the certificate is an acceptable match for the URI's origin server using the process described in Section 4.3.4 of [HTTP].",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be enforced by the TLS implementation, as h3 does not\ninspect certificate messages.\n",
      "id": "e2ee7236b371c76c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "If the certificate cannot be verified with respect to the URI's origin server, the client MUST NOT consider the server authoritative for that origin.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not need to do anything specific, as this is only a\ndescription of the expected behavior of a HTTP/3 client.\n",
      "id": "34b58a268408d27b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "A client MAY attempt access to a resource with an \"https\" URI by resolving the host identifier to an IP address, establishing a QUIC connection to that address on the indicated port (including validation of the server certificate as described above), and sending an HTTP/3 request message targeting the URI to the server over that secured connection.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Downgrading should be handled by other components of the\nimplementation, as h3 is meant to be a dedicated QUIC-based HTTP\nimplementation.\n",
      "id": "154fdca498c2b9e7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Connectivity problems (e.g., blocking UDP) can result in a failure to establish a QUIC connection; clients SHOULD attempt to use TCP-based versions of HTTP in this case.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not constrain which port the server will be listening on.  It\nis up to the user to decide.\n\nThe alt-svc advertisement should be handled by the user, as h3 only\nhandles QUIC traffic.\n",
      "id": "811bf3793e2d1aae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "Servers MAY serve HTTP/3 on any UDP port; an alternative service advertisement always includes an explicit port, and URIs contain either an explicit port or a default port associated with the scheme.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is a suggestion of future spec development.\n",
      "id": "1a874b2288112738",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The use of other QUIC transport versions with HTTP/3 MAY be defined by future specifications.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This pertains to the TLS implementation, as h3 does not inspect TLS\nmessages.\n",
      "id": "b0b43cffa07e1951",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "HTTP/3 clients MUST support a mechanism to indicate the target host to the server during the TLS handshake.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This pertains to the TLS implementation, as h3 does not inspect TLS\nmessages.\n",
      "id": "7ed4f3e1c8051678",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "If the server is identified by a domain name ([DNS-TERMS]), clients MUST send the Server Name Indication (SNI; [RFC6066]) TLS extension unless an alternative mechanism to indicate the target host is used.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not handle protocol negotiation.\n",
      "id": "9722d4b6cd4d23c9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "During connection establishment, HTTP/3 support is indicated by selecting the ALPN token \"h3\" in the TLS handshake.  Support for other application-layer protocols MAY be offered in the same handshake.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not have to do anything specific, as we cannot anticipate when\nwill the client decide to reuse a connection.\n",
      "id": "50b363d64d35f3cb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Once a connection to a server endpoint exists, this connection MAY be reused for requests with multiple different URI authority components.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be handled by the user, as h3 does not inspect certificate\nmessages.\n",
      "id": "67755f575792f798",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "To use an existing connection for a new origin, clients MUST validate the certificate presented by the server for the new origin server using the process described in Section 4.3.4 of [HTTP].",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be handled by the user, as h3 does not inspect certificate\nmessages.\n",
      "id": "3c63c8996ac19e56",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "If the certificate is not acceptable with regard to the new origin for any reason, the connection MUST NOT be reused and a new connection SHOULD be established for the new origin.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be handled by the user, as h3 does not inspect certificate\nmessages.\n",
      "id": "5c5f1b7d4937246c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "If the reason the certificate cannot be verified might apply to other origins already associated with the connection, the client SHOULD revalidate the server certificate for those origins.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This pertains to the user of h3.\n",
      "id": "bc521c3f72fccb87",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "A client MAY open multiple HTTP/3 connections to the same IP address and UDP port using different transport or TLS configurations but SHOULD avoid creating multiple connections with the same configuration.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does enable the user to cancel requests.  It is up to the user to\ndecide when to do it.\n",
      "id": "5d13852330d291f5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Once a request stream has been opened, the request MAY be cancelled by either endpoint.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should handle this, as h3 should not know anything about\nrequest processing.\n",
      "id": "9a4e0b9cd235406e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "When possible, it is RECOMMENDED that servers send an HTTP response with an appropriate status code rather than cancelling a request it has already begun processing.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should handle this, as h3 should not know anything about\nrequest processing.\n",
      "id": "09997605f7fee804",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "When the server cancels a request without performing any application processing, the request is considered \"rejected\".  The server SHOULD abort its response stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_REJECTED.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should handle this, as h3 should not know anything about\nrequest processing.\n",
      "id": "444d262187815c5a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT use the H3_REQUEST_REJECTED error code for requests that were partially or fully processed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should initiate this, as h3 should not know anything about\nrequest processing.\n",
      "id": "f74eed5caa4c207f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "When a server abandons a response after partial processing, it SHOULD abort its response stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should initiate this, as h3 should not decide when to cancel\nrequests.\n",
      "id": "773c8f59a2bf704f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "Client SHOULD use the error code H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED to cancel requests.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should initiate this, as h3 should not know anything about\nrequest processing.\n",
      "id": "d1089b9ac03a1a22",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of this error code, a server MAY abruptly terminate the response using the error code H3_REQUEST_REJECTED if no processing was performed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It should be up to the user to decide.\n",
      "id": "54e953d5f6214084",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "If a stream is cancelled after receiving a complete response, the client MAY ignore the cancellation and use the response.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be left to the user to decide.\n",
      "id": "23e4ceced9ad2c50",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "Only idempotent actions such as GET, PUT, or DELETE can be safely retried; a client SHOULD NOT automatically retry a request with a non-idempotent method unless it has some means to know that the request semantics are idempotent independent of the method or some means to detect that the original request was never applied.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 is not meant to be used for intermediaries.\n",
      "id": "c6514c2cf7d76f34",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Intermediaries that process HTTP requests or responses (i.e., any intermediary not acting as a tunnel) MUST NOT forward a malformed request or response.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be initiated by the user, as h3 cannot determine when the\nreceived message is enough.\n",
      "id": "4b3441c4371f4708",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Because some messages are large or unbounded, endpoints SHOULD begin processing partial HTTP messages once enough of the message has been received to make progress.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This should be initiated by the user, as h3 cannot determine if the\nremainder of the request is needed.\n",
      "id": "9f03ce1c48c6b506",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "When the server does not need to receive the remainder of the request, it MAY abort reading the request stream, send a complete response, and cleanly close the sending part of the stream.  The error code H3_NO_ERROR SHOULD be used when requesting that the client stop sending on the request stream.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not discard complete responses, but h3 has no control over\nwhether the user will do.\n",
      "id": "abd168bdf347d103",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT discard complete responses as a result of having their request terminated abruptly, though clients can always discard responses at their discretion for other reasons.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not need to do anything specific.\n",
      "id": "229cc781768e1add",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "If the server sends a partial or complete response but does not abort reading the request, clients SHOULD continue sending the content of the request and close the stream normally.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Users of h3 should close the stream for sending after sending a final response. As documented in the server docs.\n",
      "id": "9a19dbda80c954ce",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "After sending a final response, the server MUST close the stream for sending.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Users of h3 should close the stream for sending after sending a request. As documented in the client docs.\n",
      "id": "039237dc11ab56df",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "After sending a request, a client MUST close the stream for sending.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 is not meant to be used for intermediaries.\n",
      "id": "038f9728e5720649",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An intermediary transforming an HTTP/1.x message to HTTP/3 MUST remove connection-specific header fields as discussed in Section 7.6.1 of [HTTP], or their messages will be treated by other HTTP/3 endpoints as malformed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 is not meant to be used for intermediaries.\n",
      "id": "994569ba9197e917",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "To ensure that the HTTP/1.1 request line can be reproduced accurately, this pseudo-header field MUST be omitted when translating from an HTTP/1.1 request that has a request target in a method-specific form; see Section 7.1 of [HTTP].",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 is not meant to be used for intermediaries.\n",
      "id": "264f7037765bda63",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "An intermediary that converts an HTTP/3 request to HTTP/1.1 MUST create a Host field if one is not present in a request by copying the value of the :authority pseudo-header field.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 is not meant to be used for handling proxy.\n",
      "id": "5d5ab129b252cd77",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "TCP connections that remain half closed in a single direction are not invalid, but are often handled poorly by servers, so clients SHOULD NOT close a stream for sending while they still expect to receive data from the target of the CONNECT.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 is not meant to be used for handling proxy.\n",
      "id": "0cd6d9763d340643",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "In all these cases, if the underlying TCP implementation permits it, the proxy SHOULD send a TCP segment with the RST bit set.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 is not aware of connection establishment details.\n",
      "id": "9545dd682d896865",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "If the client has not yet validated the connection for the origin indicated by the pushed request, it MUST perform the same verification process it would do before sending a request for that origin on the connection; see Section 3.3.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 is not aware of connection establishment details.\n",
      "id": "9bfbb874977e1978",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "If this verification fails, the client MUST NOT consider the server authoritative for that origin.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For maximum flexibility, this should be left to the user to decide.\n",
      "id": "bd90c5bd74959934",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "These associations do not affect the operation of the protocol, but they MAY be considered by user agents when deciding how to use pushed resources.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not handle caching.\n",
      "id": "35299ebdb9ec904a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Pushed responses that are not cacheable MUST NOT be stored by any HTTP cache.  They MAY be made available to the application separately.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is a suggestion for API gateways.\n",
      "id": "676f7861eaadf717",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A gateway MAY maintain connections in anticipation of need rather than incur the latency cost of connection establishment to servers.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is left to the user to decide.\n",
      "id": "7147ea3f04c9a852",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The server sends a client- initiated bidirectional stream ID; the client sends a push ID. Requests or pushes with the indicated identifier or greater are rejected (Section 4.1.1) by the sender of the GOAWAY.  This identifier MAY be zero if no requests or pushes were processed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is left to the user to decide.\n",
      "id": "39fb0466f2c001c9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Clients MAY establish a new connection to send additional requests.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should initiate this, as h3 is unable to anticipate when to\nclose a connection.\n",
      "id": "1b35b5cd3a0ac1fd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD send a GOAWAY frame when the closing of a connection is known in advance, even if the advance notice is small, so that the remote peer can know whether or not a request has been partially processed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should decide how to handle this, as h3 should not know\nanything about message processing.\n",
      "id": "ff551e5570d0bebc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "Once all accepted requests and pushes have been processed, the endpoint can permit the connection to become idle, or it MAY initiate an immediate closure of the connection.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not need to do anything specific.\n",
      "id": "1e960f1fcbdb1e28",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "If a connection terminates without a GOAWAY frame, clients MUST assume that any request that was sent, whether in whole or in part, might have been processed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "h3 does not handle flow control credit acquiring.\n",
      "id": "541ad082d250c7a6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Because the contents of the control stream are used to manage the behavior of other streams, endpoints SHOULD provide enough flow- control credit to keep the peer's control stream from becoming blocked.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should ensure that the transport parameters satisfy the\nrequirements, as h3 does not handle connection establishment.\n",
      "id": "929a9831180c6e4b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Each endpoint needs to create at least one unidirectional stream for the HTTP control stream.  QPACK requires two additional unidirectional streams, and other extensions might require further streams.  Therefore, the transport parameters sent by both clients and servers MUST allow the peer to create at least three unidirectional streams.  These transport parameters SHOULD also provide at least 1,024 bytes of flow-control credit to each unidirectional stream.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The user should ensure that the order is correct, as h3 does not\nhandle protocol negotiations.\n",
      "id": "87d08f4178de733a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Extensions that could change the semantics of existing protocol components MUST be negotiated before being used.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The requirement applies to extension specifications.\n",
      "id": "e774e62d373ef48f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 13,
      "quote": "If a setting is used for extension negotiation, the default value MUST be defined in such a fashion that the extension is disabled if the setting is omitted.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/exception/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "EXCEPTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2c3439932dd7160b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An endpoint can use the SETTINGS_MAX_FIELD_SECTION_SIZE (Section 4.2.2) setting to advise peers of limits that might apply on the size of field sections.  This setting is only advisory, so endpoints MAY choose to send field sections that exceed this limit and risk having the request or response being treated as malformed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/10.5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.5.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "86b69ab907faa922",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A client that accepts server push SHOULD limit the number of push IDs it issues at a time.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/10.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "33643dd014b3cc10",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "All these features -- i.e., server push, unknown protocol elements, field compression -- have legitimate uses.  These features become a burden only when they are used unnecessarily or to excess. An endpoint that does not monitor such behavior exposes itself to a risk of denial-of-service attack.  Implementations SHOULD track the use of these features and set limits on their use.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/10.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "a7baf8f46c2bba31",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY treat activity that is suspicious as a connection error of type H3_EXCESSIVE_LOAD, but false positives will result in disrupting valid connections and requests.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/10.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "874937aef87606e1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An implementation MUST ensure that the length of a frame exactly matches the length of the fields it contains.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/10.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.8",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "2b4637c2dbad23de",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The use of 0-RTT with HTTP/3 creates an exposure to replay attack. The anti-replay mitigations in [HTTP-REPLAY] MUST be applied when using HTTP/3 with 0-RTT.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/10.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.9",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "c05f9bb66633d6f0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT use the H3_REQUEST_REJECTED error code, except when a server has requested closure of the request stream with this error code.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "21b61582afaa49b2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "However, if a stream is cancelled after receiving a partial response, the response SHOULD NOT be used.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d77203ea5c22b11",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Malformed requests or responses that are detected MUST be treated as a stream error of type H3_MESSAGE_ERROR.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "07d77cb2772190fb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "For malformed requests, a server MAY send an HTTP response indicating the error prior to closing or resetting the stream.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae45c1ef790dbcb4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 15,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT accept a malformed response.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "1c811c4e432c1061",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "On a given stream, receipt of multiple requests or receipt of an additional HTTP response following a final HTTP response MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "b7f775c5bed91079",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "A server MAY send one or more PUSH_PROMISE frames before, after, or interleaved with the frames of a response message.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "e91783aefa3abe47",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "PUSH_PROMISE frames are not permitted on push streams; a pushed response that includes PUSH_PROMISE frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "129731d03f8564af",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 23,
      "quote": "Frames of unknown types (Section 9), including reserved frames (Section 7.2.8) MAY be sent on a request or push stream before, after, or interleaved with other frames described in this section.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "e71ca63cef5bea63",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "Transfer codings (see Section 7 of [HTTP/1.1]) are not defined for HTTP/3; the Transfer-Encoding header field MUST NOT be used.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "ee1ec4cb47ec300d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "A response MAY consist of multiple messages when and only when one or more interim responses (1xx; see Section 15.2 of [HTTP]) precede a final response to the same request.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "1891d709199d726d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "Unless using the CONNECT method (see Section 4.4), clients MUST NOT make stream closure dependent on receiving a response to their request.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef28ae30620cc27d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "If a decompressed field section contains multiple cookie field lines, these MUST be concatenated into a single byte string using the two-byte delimiter of \"; \" (ASCII 0x3b, 0x20) before being passed into a context other than HTTP/2 or HTTP/3, such as an HTTP/1.1 connection, or a generic HTTP server application.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2b738c956851a80",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT generate an HTTP/3 field section containing connection-specific fields; any message containing connection-specific fields MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "782ff75662e89bdb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "The only exception to this is the TE header field, which MAY be present in an HTTP/3 request header; when it is, it MUST NOT contain any value other than \"trailers\".",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "e89001de40cdf7de",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "The authority MUST NOT include the deprecated userinfo subcomponent for URIs of scheme \"http\" or \"https\".",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa64821aefbf0478",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "Clients that generate HTTP/3 requests directly SHOULD use the :authority pseudo-header field instead of the Host header field.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "e11dc69b20d7ff73",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST treat a request or response that contains undefined or invalid pseudo-header fields as malformed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "99f249dcc9984c19",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "Any request or response that contains a pseudo-header field that appears in a header section after a regular header field MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "66d8ef675b611bea",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A CONNECT request MUST be constructed as follows: *  The :method pseudo-header field is set to \"CONNECT\" *  The :scheme and :path pseudo-header fields are omitted *  The :authority pseudo-header field contains the host and port to connect to (equivalent to the authority-form of the request-target of CONNECT requests; see Section 7.1 of [HTTP]).",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "8f5206c085faae96",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "Once the CONNECT method has completed, only DATA frames are permitted to be sent on the stream.  Extension frames MAY be used if specifically permitted by the definition of the extension.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "efdcd18798ec2b85",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "Receipt of any other known frame type MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "dbdb7a28fe6b5d97",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "TCP connections that remain half closed in a single direction are not invalid, but are often handled poorly by servers, so clients SHOULD NOT close a stream for sending while they still expect to receive data from the target of the CONNECT.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "303fcbfb4ce5cbfe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "Correspondingly, if a proxy detects an error with the stream or the QUIC connection, it MUST close the TCP connection.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "e024cbb81716d1f7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "If the proxy detects that the client has reset the stream or aborted reading from the stream, it MUST close the TCP connection.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "0b73150c4a626288",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "If the stream is reset or reading is aborted by the client, a proxy SHOULD perform the same operation on the other direction in order to ensure that both directions of the stream are cancelled.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "c08f2e7f14e8c95d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "Since CONNECT creates a tunnel to an arbitrary server, proxies that support CONNECT SHOULD restrict its use to a set of known ports or a list of safe request targets; see Section 9.3.6 of [HTTP] for more details.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "4aea915772f9467c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A server SHOULD use push IDs sequentially, beginning from zero.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "3f8c923fddd55fae",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a push stream as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR when no MAX_PUSH_ID frame has been sent or when the stream references a push ID that is greater than the maximum push ID.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "86b1c83651993d81",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "When the same push ID is promised on multiple request streams, the decompressed request field sections MUST contain the same fields in the same order, and both the name and the value in each field MUST be identical.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "f02554c204c37449",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "Not all requests can be pushed.  A server MAY push requests that have the following properties: *  cacheable; see Section 9.2.3 of [HTTP] *  safe; see Section 9.2.1 of [HTTP] *  does not include request content or a trailer section",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "720172d9f8579ac6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "The server MUST include a value in the :authority pseudo-header field for which the server is authoritative.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "ced3057b9411537b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD send a CANCEL_PUSH frame upon receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame carrying a request that is not cacheable, is not known to be safe, that indicates the presence of request content, or for which it does not consider the server authoritative.  Any corresponding responses MUST NOT be used or cached.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "358a46b22aeff46b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "The server SHOULD send PUSH_PROMISE frames prior to sending HEADERS or DATA frames that reference the promised responses.  This reduces the chance that a client requests a resource that will be pushed by the server.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "cccafca9f37a1473",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD abort reading and discard data already read from push streams if no corresponding PUSH_PROMISE frame is processed in a reasonable amount of time.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "fd68e7ecd1b6ec12",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "HTTP/3 implementations will need to open a new HTTP/3 connection for new requests if the existing connection has been idle for longer than the idle timeout negotiated during the QUIC handshake, and they SHOULD do so if approaching the idle timeout; see Section 10.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "b9b5c07d4a2ae2ce",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD NOT actively keep connections open.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "8742e659c73da5d7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Upon sending a GOAWAY frame, the endpoint SHOULD explicitly cancel (see Sections 4.1.1 and 7.2.3) any requests or pushes that have identifiers greater than or equal to the one indicated, in order to clean up transport state for the affected streams.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "89ca04fd06b61b4d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "The endpoint SHOULD continue to do so as more requests or pushes arrive.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "27a78194fb95fb17",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 18,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT initiate new requests or promise new pushes on the connection after receipt of a GOAWAY frame from the peer.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "ac0936dc967dfae2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "Servers MAY reject individual requests on streams below the indicated ID if these requests were not processed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "028226bce4cf92f5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "An endpoint that completes a graceful shutdown SHOULD use the H3_NO_ERROR error code when closing the connection.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "9f399b02cae8ef04",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Before closing the connection, a GOAWAY frame MAY be sent to allow the client to retry some requests.  Including the GOAWAY frame in the same packet as the QUIC CONNECTION_CLOSE frame improves the chances of the frame being received by clients.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "16748f744ef535ea",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Only servers can push; if a server receives a client-initiated push stream, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "2a5a38baee16cb1c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "A client SHOULD NOT abort reading on a push stream prior to reading the push stream header, as this could lead to disagreement between client and server on which push IDs have already been consumed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "7ed8b66fae5bb4e3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "Each push ID MUST only be used once in a push stream header.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "3d0b4269ae724adb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 22,
      "quote": "If a client detects that a push stream header includes a push ID that was used in another push stream header, the client MUST treat this as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "7ea5ead0fb376cee",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Implementations MAY send stream types before knowing whether the peer supports them.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc3c52623fb627bc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "However, stream types that could modify the state or semantics of existing protocol components, including QPACK or other extensions, MUST NOT be sent until the peer is known to support them.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "cf404173f3d69e6e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST tolerate unidirectional streams being closed or reset prior to the reception of the unidirectional stream header.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "97dd0d49cb4a22b4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Each frame's payload MUST contain exactly the fields identified in its description.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "31dfc2149798bdea",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "When a client sends a CANCEL_PUSH frame, it is indicating that it does not wish to receive the promised resource.  The server SHOULD abort sending the resource, but the mechanism to do so depends on the state of the corresponding push stream.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "c089db5974cc128d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "If the push stream is open, the server SHOULD abruptly terminate that stream.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "b987bccb1c3bcce3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "If the push stream has already ended, the server MAY still abruptly terminate the stream or MAY take no action.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "54e31c15cefea0c5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "Regardless of whether a push stream has been opened, a server SHOULD send a CANCEL_PUSH frame when it determines that promise will not be fulfilled.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb24f6635a30a258",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "A client SHOULD NOT send a CANCEL_PUSH frame when it has already received a corresponding push stream.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "b4834482e1d1791a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "A push stream could arrive after a client has sent a CANCEL_PUSH frame, because a server might not have processed the CANCEL_PUSH.  The client SHOULD abort reading the stream with an error code of H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "4ffd7eaa78d1bbf3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An HTTP implementation MUST NOT send frames or requests that would be invalid based on its current understanding of the peer's settings.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "08d201ec21920899",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "Each endpoint SHOULD use these initial values to send messages before the peer's SETTINGS frame has arrived, as packets carrying the settings can be lost or delayed.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "13a3f5f671281dfc",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD NOT wait indefinitely for SETTINGS to arrive before sending requests, but they SHOULD process received datagrams in order to increase the likelihood of processing SETTINGS before sending the first request.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "dde1ba7ea396b557",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "A client MUST comply with stored settings -- or default values if no values are stored -- when attempting 0-RTT.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "9a93f56f6b3ab4ab",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Once a server has provided new settings, clients MUST comply with those values.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "ac6a49b4fe4aa581",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 38,
      "quote": "If the server cannot determine that the settings remembered by a client are compatible with its current settings, it MUST NOT accept 0-RTT data. Remembered settings are compatible if a client complying with those settings would not violate the server's current settings.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "49b278483a4a4ddf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "A server MAY accept 0-RTT and subsequently provide different settings in its SETTINGS frame.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "31b0a0dc47201e44",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "If 0-RTT data is accepted by the server, its SETTINGS frame MUST NOT reduce any limits or alter any values that might be violated by the client with its 0-RTT data.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "b37d6718768eacd6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "The server MUST include all settings that differ from their default values.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "5b680e8cab9bf130",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "If a server accepts 0-RTT but then sends settings that are not compatible with the previously specified settings, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "e26e277c06529ec1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "If a server accepts 0-RTT but then sends a SETTINGS frame that omits a setting value that the client understands (apart from reserved setting identifiers) that was previously specified to have a non-default value, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "bdbe0b7692bcbc80",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT use a push ID that is larger than the client has provided in a MAX_PUSH_ID frame (Section 7.2.7).",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3466282e5a98052",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "A server MAY use the same push ID in multiple PUSH_PROMISE frames. If so, the decompressed request header sets MUST contain the same fields in the same order, and both the name and the value in each field MUST be exact matches.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "8992c704681d1fc5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 17,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD compare the request header sections for resources promised multiple times.  If a client receives a push ID that has already been promised and detects a mismatch, it MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_GENERAL_PROTOCOL_ERROR.  If the decompressed field sections match exactly, the client SHOULD associate the pushed content with each stream on which a PUSH_PROMISE frame was received.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "f8c4334a132ba7bb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "Allowing duplicate references to the same push ID is primarily to reduce duplication caused by concurrent requests.  A server SHOULD avoid reusing a push ID over a long period.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "b875f5625dcf7a81",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT send a PUSH_PROMISE frame.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "8b84ef0f629acf5e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT send a MAX_PUSH_ID frame.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "9c073bf0cd7af5a7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider these frames to have any meaning upon receipt.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.8",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "6a62c1f0188770dd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "Frame types that were used in HTTP/2 where there is no corresponding HTTP/3 frame have also been reserved (Section 11.2.1).  These frame types MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/7.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.8",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "5ab253e959d92da5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Error codes of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N are reserved to exercise the requirement that unknown error codes be treated as equivalent to H3_NO_ERROR (Section 9). Implementations SHOULD select an error code from this space with some probability when they would have sent H3_NO_ERROR.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "5c12a40ffb17c5d8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY choose to treat a stream error as a connection error under certain circumstances, closing the entire connection in response to a condition on a single stream.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "4dc96cf241cb05ea",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 10,
      "quote": "Because new error codes can be defined without negotiation (see Section 9), use of an error code in an unexpected context or receipt of an unknown error code MUST be treated as equivalent to H3_NO_ERROR.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "dd71538ccf82aeeb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 3,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST ignore unknown or unsupported values in all extensible protocol elements.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "33e867e6195b6ec1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 9,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST discard data or abort reading on unidirectional streams that have unknown or unsupported types.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "04da51f1046d8115",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 16,
      "quote": "However, where a known frame type is required to be in a specific location, such as the SETTINGS frame as the first frame of the control stream (see Section 6.2.1), an unknown frame type does not satisfy that requirement and SHOULD be treated as an error.",
      "source": "ci/compliance/specs/rfc9114/todo/9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "8916abea85d3039b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD NOT open more than one HTTP/3 connection to a given IP address and UDP port, where the IP address and port might be derived from a URI, a selected alternative service ([ALTSVC]), a configured proxy, or name resolution of any of these.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/builder.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cb12f70787f05ff1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "A client MUST send only a single request on a given stream.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "143c974b69c022c9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 158,
      "quote": "Characters in field names MUST be converted to lowercase prior to their encoding.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "1ed478530bea41e7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 163,
      "quote": "To allow for better compression efficiency, the Cookie header field ([COOKIES]) MAY be split into separate field lines, each with one or more cookie-pairs, before compression.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "aac35d0072a33069",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 172,
      "quote": "An implementation that has received this parameter SHOULD NOT send an HTTP message header that exceeds the indicated size, as the peer will likely refuse to process it.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "60e6ed5289074edf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 369,
      "quote": "When a 0-RTT QUIC connection is being used, the initial value of each server setting is the value used in the previous session.  Clients SHOULD store the settings the server provided in the HTTP/3 connection where resumption information was provided, but they MAY opt not to store settings in certain cases (e.g., if the session ticket is received before the SETTINGS frame).",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "7635202f3f0c45bd",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 378,
      "quote": "A client MUST comply with stored settings -- or default values if no values are stored -- when attempting 0-RTT.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "729c8396fa58f230",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 384,
      "quote": "Once a server has provided new settings, clients MUST comply with those values.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "897bb33be841db66",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 395,
      "quote": "The GOAWAY frame is always sent on the control stream.  In the server-to-client direction, it carries a QUIC stream ID for a client- initiated bidirectional stream encoded as a variable-length integer. A client MUST treat receipt of a GOAWAY frame containing a stream ID of any other type as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ea684161a5cd041f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 413,
      "quote": "If a PUSH_PROMISE frame is received on the control stream, the client MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c00ef4d1aa6c1783",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 417,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat the receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6e7b93ade4715c5b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 444,
      "quote": "Clients MUST treat receipt of a server-initiated bidirectional stream as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR unless such an extension has been negotiated.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "af947b3312e8881b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame that contains a larger push ID than the client has advertised as a connection error of H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "b0bdc393917f18af",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "If a client receives a push ID that has already been promised and detects a mismatch, it MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_GENERAL_PROTOCOL_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "8c45568e99e5e40d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "An HTTP/3 implementation MAY impose a limit on the maximum size of the message header it will accept on an individual HTTP message.",
      "source": "h3/src/client/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "972e00ceedb47b89",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 200,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD cancel requests by abruptly terminating any directions of a stream that are still open.  To do so, an implementation resets the sending parts of streams and aborts reading on the receiving parts of streams; see Section 2.4 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "h3/src/client/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "4f46a80a95d00cf3",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "Setting identifiers of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N are reserved to exercise the requirement that unknown identifiers be ignored.  Such settings have no defined meaning.  Endpoints SHOULD include at least one such setting in their SETTINGS frame.",
      "source": "h3/src/config.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f1edb8e39f9b72c4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "Setting identifiers that were defined in [HTTP/2] where there is no corresponding HTTP/3 setting have also been reserved (Section 11.2.2).  These reserved settings MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/config.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "36a7ba5d130866cb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 185,
      "quote": "After the QUIC connection is established, a SETTINGS frame MUST be sent by each endpoint as the initial frame of their respective HTTP control stream.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "773cfa903518d745",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 190,
      "quote": "Each side MUST initiate a single control stream at the beginning of the connection and send its SETTINGS frame as the first frame on this stream.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "843eb908926b1928",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 195,
      "quote": "A SETTINGS frame MUST be sent as the first frame of each control stream (see Section 6.2.1) by each peer, and it MUST NOT be sent subsequently.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8b76f01b92a5ecb5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 200,
      "quote": "SETTINGS frames MUST NOT be sent on any stream other than the control stream.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "546b7a87040177d8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 205,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT require any data to be received from the peer prior to sending the SETTINGS frame; settings MUST be sent as soon as the transport is ready to send data.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "565c62c557d9ae10",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 241,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD create the HTTP control stream as well as the unidirectional streams required by mandatory extensions (such as the QPACK encoder and decoder streams) first, and then create additional",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "09797e0976f1cec5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 266,
      "quote": "The sender MUST NOT close the control stream, and the receiver MUST NOT request that the sender close the control stream.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c608fa513980f3d6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 315,
      "quote": "When either endpoint chooses to close the HTTP/3 connection, the terminating endpoint SHOULD first send a GOAWAY frame (Section 5.2) so that both endpoints can reliably determine whether previously sent frames have been processed and gracefully complete or terminate any necessary remaining tasks.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8e144963ca398ab5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 378,
      "quote": "As certain stream types can affect connection state, a recipient SHOULD NOT discard data from incoming unidirectional streams prior to reading the stream type.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "bccc3bb13f4df6ed",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 389,
      "quote": "Only one control stream per peer is permitted; receipt of a second stream claiming to be a control stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a82a88395533696a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 423,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider these streams to have any meaning upon receipt.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "858c14a846b1c5e5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 455,
      "quote": "If either control stream is closed at any point, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_CLOSED_CRITICAL_STREAM.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "10e0aad18f02481e",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 463,
      "quote": "A receiver MAY treat the presence of duplicate setting identifiers as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "3feabd0b82a65f9d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 468,
      "quote": "Setting identifiers that were defined in [HTTP/2] where there is no corresponding HTTP/3 setting have also been reserved (Section 11.2.2).  These reserved settings MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "2e2d1f6c8ed7c956",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 478,
      "quote": "An implementation MUST ignore any parameter with an identifier it does not understand.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "b44801fce652a220",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 483,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider such settings to have any meaning upon receipt.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "dad341cf81c770d1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 495,
      "quote": "If a CANCEL_PUSH frame is received that references a push ID greater than currently allowed on the connection, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "983e21485bb62cf6",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 504,
      "quote": "If the first frame of the control stream is any other frame type, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_MISSING_SETTINGS.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "105732f2a501910c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 515,
      "quote": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f27bcb12af817198",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 519,
      "quote": "DATA frames MUST be associated with an HTTP request or response.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.1",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "f1ce87baefb820d7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 523,
      "quote": "If a DATA frame is received on a control stream, the recipient MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a19a0b93e1b1f89c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 528,
      "quote": "If a HEADERS frame is received on a control stream, the recipient MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ee3f92379086f8d9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 532,
      "quote": "If an endpoint receives a second SETTINGS frame on the control stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e0f5b6514483050b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 545,
      "quote": "Frame types of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N are reserved to exercise the requirement that unknown types be ignored (Section 9).  These frames have no semantics, and they MAY be sent on any stream where frames are allowed to be sent.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.8",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2b3dad25aa371980",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 568,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send multiple GOAWAY frames indicating different identifiers, but the identifier in each frame MUST NOT be greater than the identifier in any previous frame, since clients might already have retried unprocessed requests on another HTTP connection.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "37249656d1256a73",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 574,
      "quote": "Like the server, the client MAY send subsequent GOAWAY frames so long as the specified push ID is no greater than any previously sent value.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "651af02c785ac082",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 580,
      "quote": "Receiving a GOAWAY containing a larger identifier than previously received MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "0f9d426b8614b5c2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 629,
      "quote": "Stream types of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N are reserved to exercise the requirement that unknown types be ignored.  These streams have no semantics, and they can be sent when application-layer padding is desired.  They MAY also be sent on connections where no data is currently being transferred.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "28dc3f082f79aec9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 679,
      "quote": "When sending a reserved stream type, the implementation MAY either terminate the stream cleanly or reset it.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a39778e49e6f8aa9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 770,
      "quote": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c93f88531bd194a5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 774,
      "quote": "Receiving a CANCEL_PUSH frame on a stream other than the control stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "45f132d0b684c910",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 779,
      "quote": "If an endpoint receives a SETTINGS frame on a different stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6aafaca728703ff4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 784,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat a GOAWAY frame on a stream other than the control stream as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "914110a0b4a72190",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 788,
      "quote": "The MAX_PUSH_ID frame is always sent on the control stream.  Receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame on any other stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "306624ff47699005",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 820,
      "quote": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "09648c1ad784e409",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 824,
      "quote": "Receiving a CANCEL_PUSH frame on a stream other than the control stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "71589630b7ec019c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 829,
      "quote": "If an endpoint receives a SETTINGS frame on a different stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "fabbbf6484ec8332",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 834,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat a GOAWAY frame on a stream other than the control stream as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.6",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c8cf666193c12086",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 838,
      "quote": "The MAX_PUSH_ID frame is always sent on the control stream.  Receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame on any other stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "140c8ea9449ead60",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 861,
      "quote": "An HTTP/3 implementation MAY impose a limit on the maximum size of the message header it will accept on an individual HTTP message.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a96942e4936082a5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 903,
      "quote": "Characters in field names MUST be converted to lowercase prior to their encoding.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "98a2c8732b1b674b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 916,
      "quote": "An implementation that has received this parameter SHOULD NOT send an HTTP message header that exceeds the indicated size, as the peer will likely refuse to process it.",
      "source": "h3/src/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "48cadc7f78352a1a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 410,
      "quote": "When a stream terminates cleanly, if the last frame on the stream was truncated, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/error.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "2923e04c99a175b7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 424,
      "quote": "A frame payload that contains additional bytes after the identified fields or a frame payload that terminates before the end of the identified fields MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/error.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "080ed16d5c8b27a4",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 430,
      "quote": "In particular, redundant length encodings MUST be verified to be self-consistent; see Section 10.8.",
      "source": "h3/src/error.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e2a9bef52dbc6894",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "",
      "source": "h3/src/ext.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9297",
      "target_section": "section-2.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "51e9a81064a7de3b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 408,
      "quote": "Setting identifiers that were defined in [HTTP/2] where there is no corresponding HTTP/3 setting have also been reserved (Section 11.2.2).  These reserved settings MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/frame.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "983c14c5ad06dd24",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 487,
      "quote": "The same setting identifier MUST NOT occur more than once in the SETTINGS frame.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/frame.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2848050c34e3914",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 528,
      "quote": "Setting identifiers that were defined in [HTTP/2] where there is no corresponding HTTP/3 setting have also been reserved (Section 11.2.2).  These reserved settings MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/frame.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ed29a04aacb827eb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 538,
      "quote": "Setting identifiers that were defined in [HTTP/2] where there is no corresponding HTTP/3 setting have also been reserved (Section 11.2.2).  These reserved settings MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/frame.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c8e60f567f9df812",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "Pseudo-header fields MUST NOT appear in trailer sections.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "de1750e4714dc753",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "If the :scheme pseudo-header field identifies a scheme that has a mandatory authority component (including \"http\" and \"https\"), the request MUST contain either an :authority pseudo-header field or a Host header field.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cecde5ca5a5abd79",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "If the scheme does not have a mandatory authority component and none is provided in the request target, the request MUST NOT contain the :authority pseudo-header or Host header fields.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "5622b67f51e8cb9f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 87,
      "quote": "If both fields are present, they MUST contain the same value.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5d1ce05ea29a1ef",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "If these fields are present, they MUST NOT be empty.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e6abb03fd1b9995",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "For responses, a single \":status\" pseudo-header field is defined that carries the HTTP status code; see Section 15 of [HTTP].  This pseudo- header field MUST be included in all responses; otherwise, the response is malformed (see Section 4.1.2).",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c74c9c50205d3303",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "All pseudo-header fields MUST appear in the header section before regular header fields.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3216127f35d63a7c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 268,
      "quote": "Requests or responses containing invalid field names MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3a5dc0bb622406b9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 272,
      "quote": "Any request or response that contains a character not permitted in a field value MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b729b3509f09344",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 277,
      "quote": "A request or response containing uppercase characters in field names MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "9b907e03506d4946",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 293,
      "quote": "If these fields are present, they MUST NOT be empty.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "898bd589152bc2f7",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 331,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT generate pseudo-header fields other than those defined in this document.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6242ec1559958390",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 361,
      "quote": "This pseudo-header field MUST NOT be empty for \"http\" or \"https\" URIs; \"http\" or \"https\" URIs that do not contain a path component MUST include a value of / (ASCII 0x2f).",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d234484c8cf6049f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 388,
      "quote": "Pseudo-header fields defined for requests MUST NOT appear in responses; pseudo-header fields defined for responses MUST NOT appear in requests.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "8d126729cd4603ac",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 394,
      "quote": "All HTTP/3 requests MUST include exactly one value for the :method, :scheme, and :path pseudo-header fields, unless the request is a CONNECT request; see Section 4.4.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "53c778fe586c0116",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 411,
      "quote": "Pseudo-header fields defined for requests MUST NOT appear in responses; pseudo-header fields defined for responses MUST NOT appear in requests.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ab4a7ffa8e703ed9",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 489,
      "quote": "If the :scheme pseudo-header field identifies a scheme that has a mandatory authority component (including \"http\" and \"https\"), the request MUST contain either an :authority pseudo-header field or a Host header field.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "374c24af7b19c80c",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 505,
      "quote": "If these fields are present, they MUST NOT be empty.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d575b4688d74572b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 520,
      "quote": "If these fields are present, they MUST NOT be empty.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "1ca7c4223fb0b61b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 537,
      "quote": "If the :scheme pseudo-header field identifies a scheme that has a mandatory authority component (including \"http\" and \"https\"), the request MUST contain either an :authority pseudo-header field or a Host header field.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ca7a02aa78fb62f5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 553,
      "quote": "If the :scheme pseudo-header field identifies a scheme that has a mandatory authority component (including \"http\" and \"https\"), the request MUST contain either an :authority pseudo-header field or a Host header field.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "02e1ba6383ea3d38",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 570,
      "quote": "If both fields are present, they MUST contain the same value.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "0c6b181ed519bbd2",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 583,
      "quote": "If both fields are present, they MUST contain the same value.",
      "source": "h3/src/proto/headers.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "9ef770b6d32df7df",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 170,
      "quote": "If a client-initiated stream terminates without enough of the HTTP message to provide a complete response, the server SHOULD abort its response stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_INCOMPLETE.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "d1f51608fc71ec38",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 182,
      "quote": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "6e2018074798db64",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 186,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat the receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "72462b497145a408",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 191,
      "quote": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "210ac9f69a6c2a71",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 244,
      "quote": "An HTTP/3 implementation MAY impose a limit on the maximum size of the message header it will accept on an individual HTTP message.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "1bf83164abb38258",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 380,
      "quote": "If a server receives a CANCEL_PUSH frame for a push ID that has not yet been mentioned by a PUSH_PROMISE frame, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "954d0359f0f0f1fe",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 386,
      "quote": "A MAX_PUSH_ID frame cannot reduce the maximum push ID; receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame that contains a smaller value than previously received MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ad30eff7fcc7c93",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 394,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat the receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ef894b18943771a5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 477,
      "quote": "In order to permit these streams to open, an HTTP/3 server SHOULD configure non- zero minimum values for the number of permitted streams and the initial stream flow-control window.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "6fc4a692ab701b13",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 484,
      "quote": "So as to not unnecessarily limit parallelism, at least 100 request streams SHOULD be permitted at a time.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "783d43089342d53f",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "Malformed requests or responses that are detected MUST be treated as a stream error of type H3_MESSAGE_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "cf06c9475a6228c0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "Malformed requests or responses that are detected MUST be treated as a stream error of type H3_MESSAGE_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "e13088c54983c40d",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "An implementation that has received this parameter SHOULD NOT send an HTTP message header that exceeds the indicated size, as the peer will likely refuse to process it.",
      "source": "h3/src/server/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5f65f3a0123a693",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD cancel requests by abruptly terminating any directions of a stream that are still open.  To do so, an implementation resets the sending parts of streams and aborts reading on the receiving parts of streams; see Section 2.4 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "h3/src/server/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "TODO"
    },
    {
      "id": "50758fba273e450a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 298,
      "quote": "Recipients of unknown stream types MUST either abort reading of the stream or discard incoming data without further processing.",
      "source": "h3/src/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "22749977fe15683b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 303,
      "quote": "If reading is aborted, the recipient SHOULD use the H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR error code or a reserved error code (Section 8.1).",
      "source": "h3/src/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "CITATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "4b75efbe32111810",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 308,
      "quote": "The recipient MUST NOT consider unknown stream types to be a connection error of any kind.",
      "source": "h3/src/stream.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "IMPLICATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "36ade4f8d02da995",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 189,
      "quote": "After the QUIC connection is established, a SETTINGS frame MUST be sent by each endpoint as the initial frame of their respective HTTP control stream.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a802244752edaddf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 239,
      "quote": "After the QUIC connection is established, a SETTINGS frame MUST be sent by each endpoint as the initial frame of their respective HTTP control stream.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "bf8cbc51ae2c49b8",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 306,
      "quote": "Clients MUST treat receipt of a server-initiated bidirectional stream as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR unless such an extension has been negotiated.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "d952c61069f2c29b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 349,
      "quote": "Only one control stream per peer is permitted; receipt of a second stream claiming to be a control stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "461113cfc19caa06",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 393,
      "quote": "If either control stream is closed at any point, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_CLOSED_CRITICAL_STREAM.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "6a499abebe930a04",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 452,
      "quote": "If the first frame of the control stream is any other frame type, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_MISSING_SETTINGS.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "e3c6a671d11a47c1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 488,
      "quote": "If a DATA frame is received on a control stream, the recipient MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "107c5e17f53007c1",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 581,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a GOAWAY frame containing a stream ID of any other type as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/connection.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "909829cd8705162b",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 289,
      "quote": "An HTTP/3 implementation MAY impose a limit on the maximum size of the message header it will accept on an individual HTTP message.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "113dbeee5ecff698",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 347,
      "quote": "An HTTP/3 implementation MAY impose a limit on the maximum size of the message header it will accept on an individual HTTP message.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8577519434330a1c",
