      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "672e1d7e7756e16a",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1157,
      "quote": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8fdf87bd66f79665",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1172,
      "quote": "Receiving a CANCEL_PUSH frame on a stream other than the control stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "ceb5a3b172d93adf",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1178,
      "quote": "If an endpoint receives a SETTINGS frame on a different stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "8dea253ace587866",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1184,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat a GOAWAY frame on a stream other than the control stream as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.6",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "a799fa2bf14d7ceb",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1189,
      "quote": "The MAX_PUSH_ID frame is always sent on the control stream.  Receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame on any other stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "f803acd8bc4e6be5",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1297,
      "quote": "A frame payload that contains additional bytes after the identified fields or a frame payload that terminates before the end of the identified fields MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_ERROR.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "243c6cdcb0818cd0",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1317,
      "quote": "In particular, redundant length encodings MUST be verified to be self-consistent; see Section 10.8.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "812f1e756ada4c64",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1340,
      "quote": "In particular, redundant length encodings MUST be verified to be self-consistent; see Section 10.8.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "id": "18f6421b67326e57",
      "level": "Auto",
      "line": 1390,
      "quote": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "h3/src/tests/request.rs",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "TEST"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Requests or responses containing invalid field names MUST be treated\nas malformed.\n",
      "id": "b00ea8d3a3983a35",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "Requests or responses containing invalid field names MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any request or response that contains a\ncharacter not permitted in a field value MUST be treated as\nmalformed.\n",
      "id": "ab50585e50f008cc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "Any request or response that contains a character not permitted in a field value MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Where multiple tenants share space on the same server, that server\nMUST ensure that tenants are not able to push representations of\nresources that they do not have authority over.\n",
      "id": "6618ea9abe2850f3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "Where multiple tenants share space on the same server, that server MUST ensure that tenants are not able to push representations of resources that they do not have authority over.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This setting is only advisory, so\nendpoints MAY choose to send field sections that exceed this limit\nand risk having the request or response being treated as malformed.\n",
      "id": "16c88b859a586492",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 30,
      "quote": "This setting is only advisory, so endpoints MAY choose to send field sections that exceed this limit and risk having the request or response being treated as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client that accepts server push SHOULD limit the number\nof push IDs it issues at a time.\n",
      "id": "3cc98ad8fb02ba5e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "A client that accepts server push SHOULD limit the number of push IDs it issues at a time.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD track the\nuse of these features and set limits on their use.\n",
      "id": "fff8299c267e67dd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD track the use of these features and set limits on their use.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY\ntreat activity that is suspicious as a connection error of type\nH3_EXCESSIVE_LOAD, but false positives will result in disrupting\nvalid connections and requests.\n",
      "id": "30435513d440a425",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY treat activity that is suspicious as a connection error of type H3_EXCESSIVE_LOAD, but false positives will result in disrupting valid connections and requests.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations communicating on a secure channel MUST NOT compress\ncontent that includes both confidential and attacker-controlled data\nunless separate compression contexts are used for each source of\ndata.\n",
      "id": "21823b164e17aacf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "Implementations communicating on a secure channel MUST NOT compress content that includes both confidential and attacker-controlled data unless separate compression contexts are used for each source of data.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Compression MUST NOT be used if the source of data cannot be\nreliably determined.\n",
      "id": "a194991955a45aff",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Compression MUST NOT be used if the source of data cannot be reliably determined.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An implementation MUST ensure that the length of a\nframe exactly matches the length of the fields it contains.\n",
      "id": "b142a05de43183ab",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 11,
      "quote": "An implementation MUST ensure that the length of a frame exactly matches the length of the fields it contains.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The anti-replay mitigations in [HTTP-REPLAY] MUST be applied when\nusing HTTP/3 with 0-RTT.\n",
      "id": "5669030a63845ea1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 12,
      "quote": "The anti-replay mitigations in [HTTP-REPLAY] MUST be applied when using HTTP/3 with 0-RTT.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-10.9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-10.9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an entry is present in\nonly one registry, every effort SHOULD be made to avoid assigning the\ncorresponding value to an unrelated operation.\n",
      "id": "dc593cff92109e95",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 66,
      "quote": "If an entry is present in only one registry, every effort SHOULD be made to avoid assigning the corresponding value to an unrelated operation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Expert reviewers MAY\nreject unrelated registrations that would conflict with the same\nvalue in the corresponding registry.\n",
      "id": "c2dc09c81ad996e8",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 74,
      "quote": "Expert reviewers MAY reject unrelated registrations that would conflict with the same value in the corresponding registry.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent\nregistrations in this registry MUST include the following field:\n",
      "id": "096132a5c58e3b8f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following field:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Specifications of frame types MUST include a description of the frame\nlayout and its semantics, including any parts of the frame that are\nconditionally present.\n",
      "id": "89c93d2581c06224",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Specifications of frame types MUST include a description of the frame layout and its semantics, including any parts of the frame that are conditionally present.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer\nvalues of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe)\nMUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of\nassigned values.\n",
      "id": "6ec25ca053820271",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 97,
      "quote": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe) MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an entry is present in only one registry, every\neffort SHOULD be made to avoid assigning the corresponding value to\nan unrelated operation.\n",
      "id": "759b4ce0dda185a8",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "If an entry is present in only one registry, every effort SHOULD be made to avoid assigning the corresponding value to an unrelated operation.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Expert reviewers MAY reject unrelated\nregistrations that would conflict with the same value in the\ncorresponding registry.\n",
      "id": "fb055d725135fceb",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "Expert reviewers MAY reject unrelated registrations that would conflict with the same value in the corresponding registry.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent\nregistrations in this registry MUST include the following fields:\n",
      "id": "2c04635e729dfcae",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following fields:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\ndefault SHOULD be the most restrictive possible value.\n",
      "id": "e04bee38d4e7a32c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 82,
      "quote": "A default SHOULD be the most restrictive possible value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer\nvalues of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe)\nMUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of\nassigned values.\n",
      "id": "a3845b8fd1708627",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe) MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Use of values that are registered in the \"HTTP/2 Error Code\" registry\nis discouraged, and expert reviewers MAY reject such registrations.\n",
      "id": "d4fd7430fbe2c4c3",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "Use of values that are registered in the \"HTTP/2 Error Code\" registry is discouraged, and expert reviewers MAY reject such registrations.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Permanent registrations in\nthis registry MUST include the following field:\n",
      "id": "01051a80bd783957",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "Permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following field:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer\nvalues of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe)\nMUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of\nassigned values.\n",
      "id": "0f5362612bfe2296",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe) MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent\nregistrations in this registry MUST include the following fields:\n",
      "id": "f636c659de02009b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent registrations in this registry MUST include the following fields:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Specifications for permanent registrations MUST include a description\nof the stream type, including the layout and semantics of the stream\ncontents.\n",
      "id": "4245ef3af964e5bf",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Specifications for permanent registrations MUST include a description of the stream type, including the layout and semantics of the stream contents.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer\nvalues of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe)\nMUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of\nassigned values.\n",
      "id": "147e3d8a2c356e17",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 58,
      "quote": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe) MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of assigned values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-11.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-11.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On receipt of an Alt-Svc record indicating HTTP/3 support, a client\nMAY attempt to establish a QUIC connection to the indicated host and\nport; if this connection is successful, the client can send HTTP\nrequests using the mapping described in this document.\n",
      "id": "66c2ed8bdaf9064d",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "On receipt of an Alt-Svc record indicating HTTP/3 support, a client MAY attempt to establish a QUIC connection to the indicated host and port; if this connection is successful, the client can send HTTP requests using the mapping described in this document.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Prior to making requests for an origin whose scheme is not \"https\",\nthe client MUST ensure the server is willing to serve that scheme.\n",
      "id": "1cbbe669c3ba2d63",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "Prior to making requests for an origin whose scheme is not \"https\", the client MUST ensure the server is willing to serve that scheme.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receiving a\nserver certificate in the TLS handshake, the client MUST verify that\nthe certificate is an acceptable match for the URI's origin server\nusing the process described in Section 4.3.4 of [HTTP].\n",
      "id": "7afe765dea465088",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 39,
      "quote": "Upon receiving a server certificate in the TLS handshake, the client MUST verify that the certificate is an acceptable match for the URI's origin server using the process described in Section 4.3.4 of [HTTP].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the\ncertificate cannot be verified with respect to the URI's origin\nserver, the client MUST NOT consider the server authoritative for\nthat origin.\n",
      "id": "a6c16dadde40bbb0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "If the certificate cannot be verified with respect to the URI's origin server, the client MUST NOT consider the server authoritative for that origin.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MAY attempt access to a resource with an \"https\" URI by\nresolving the host identifier to an IP address, establishing a QUIC\nconnection to that address on the indicated port (including\nvalidation of the server certificate as described above), and sending\nan HTTP/3 request message targeting the URI to the server over that\nsecured connection.\n",
      "id": "e29093aeb8d8cb70",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "A client MAY attempt access to a resource with an \"https\" URI by resolving the host identifier to an IP address, establishing a QUIC connection to that address on the indicated port (including validation of the server certificate as described above), and sending an HTTP/3 request message targeting the URI to the server over that secured connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Connectivity problems (e.g., blocking UDP) can result in a failure to\nestablish a QUIC connection; clients SHOULD attempt to use TCP-based\nversions of HTTP in this case.\n",
      "id": "09136c7e1c936c36",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "Connectivity problems (e.g., blocking UDP) can result in a failure to establish a QUIC connection; clients SHOULD attempt to use TCP-based versions of HTTP in this case.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY serve HTTP/3 on any UDP port; an alternative service\nadvertisement always includes an explicit port, and URIs contain\neither an explicit port or a default port associated with the scheme.\n",
      "id": "044f6306fc277fcb",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "Servers MAY serve HTTP/3 on any UDP port; an alternative service advertisement always includes an explicit port, and URIs contain either an explicit port or a default port associated with the scheme.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The use\nof other QUIC transport versions with HTTP/3 MAY be defined by future\nspecifications.\n",
      "id": "23b575586e5e0855",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 28,
      "quote": "The use of other QUIC transport versions with HTTP/3 MAY be defined by future specifications.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "HTTP/3 clients MUST support a mechanism to indicate the\ntarget host to the server during the TLS handshake.\n",
      "id": "594fb71ec747d430",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "HTTP/3 clients MUST support a mechanism to indicate the target host to the server during the TLS handshake.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server is\nidentified by a domain name ([DNS-TERMS]), clients MUST send the\nServer Name Indication (SNI; [RFC6066]) TLS extension unless an\nalternative mechanism to indicate the target host is used.\n",
      "id": "9bbfb0020a6f5e50",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "If the server is identified by a domain name ([DNS-TERMS]), clients MUST send the Server Name Indication (SNI; [RFC6066]) TLS extension unless an alternative mechanism to indicate the target host is used.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Support for\nother application-layer protocols MAY be offered in the same\nhandshake.\n",
      "id": "bb7ec493b35315e6",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Support for other application-layer protocols MAY be offered in the same handshake.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After the QUIC connection is\nestablished, a SETTINGS frame MUST be sent by each endpoint as the\ninitial frame of their respective HTTP control stream.\n",
      "id": "d83a6d8d60117059",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "After the QUIC connection is established, a SETTINGS frame MUST be sent by each endpoint as the initial frame of their respective HTTP control stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a connection to a server endpoint exists, this connection MAY be\nreused for requests with multiple different URI authority components.\n",
      "id": "9609ed5de4037687",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 52,
      "quote": "Once a connection to a server endpoint exists, this connection MAY be reused for requests with multiple different URI authority components.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To use an existing connection for a new origin, clients MUST validate\nthe certificate presented by the server for the new origin server\nusing the process described in Section 4.3.4 of [HTTP].\n",
      "id": "13b8ba85bff7698c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "To use an existing connection for a new origin, clients MUST validate the certificate presented by the server for the new origin server using the process described in Section 4.3.4 of [HTTP].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the certificate is not acceptable with regard to the new origin\nfor any reason, the connection MUST NOT be reused and a new\nconnection SHOULD be established for the new origin.\n",
      "id": "f5300f4e0aadf957",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "If the certificate is not acceptable with regard to the new origin for any reason, the connection MUST NOT be reused and a new connection SHOULD be established for the new origin.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the reason\nthe certificate cannot be verified might apply to other origins\nalready associated with the connection, the client SHOULD revalidate\nthe server certificate for those origins.\n",
      "id": "44c924b4a40190ea",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "If the reason the certificate cannot be verified might apply to other origins already associated with the connection, the client SHOULD revalidate the server certificate for those origins.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD NOT open more than one HTTP/3 connection to a given IP\naddress and UDP port, where the IP address and port might be derived\nfrom a URI, a selected alternative service ([ALTSVC]), a configured\nproxy, or name resolution of any of these.\n",
      "id": "6e55d38ff737813e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD NOT open more than one HTTP/3 connection to a given IP address and UDP port, where the IP address and port might be derived from a URI, a selected alternative service ([ALTSVC]), a configured proxy, or name resolution of any of these.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MAY open\nmultiple HTTP/3 connections to the same IP address and UDP port using\ndifferent transport or TLS configurations but SHOULD avoid creating\nmultiple connections with the same configuration.\n",
      "id": "b3cc558f9172f182",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "A client MAY open multiple HTTP/3 connections to the same IP address and UDP port using different transport or TLS configurations but SHOULD avoid creating multiple connections with the same configuration.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When either endpoint chooses to close the HTTP/3\nconnection, the terminating endpoint SHOULD first send a GOAWAY frame\n(Section 5.2) so that both endpoints can reliably determine whether\npreviously sent frames have been processed and gracefully complete or\nterminate any necessary remaining tasks.\n",
      "id": "b3a70630a72369a1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 102,
      "quote": "When either endpoint chooses to close the HTTP/3 connection, the terminating endpoint SHOULD first send a GOAWAY frame (Section 5.2) so that both endpoints can reliably determine whether previously sent frames have been processed and gracefully complete or terminate any necessary remaining tasks.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-3.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-3.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a request stream has been opened, the request MAY be cancelled\nby either endpoint.\n",
      "id": "25d3e78e36ed698b",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Once a request stream has been opened, the request MAY be cancelled by either endpoint.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When possible, it is RECOMMENDED that servers\nsend an HTTP response with an appropriate status code rather than\ncancelling a request it has already begun processing.\n",
      "id": "3f2bc185878995c4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "When possible, it is RECOMMENDED that servers send an HTTP response with an appropriate status code rather than cancelling a request it has already begun processing.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD cancel requests by abruptly terminating any\ndirections of a stream that are still open.\n",
      "id": "f00070e37b2117bf",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 65,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD cancel requests by abruptly terminating any directions of a stream that are still open.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server SHOULD\nabort its response stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_REJECTED.\n",
      "id": "30b2e9c3c56d7673",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "The server SHOULD abort its response stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_REJECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MUST NOT use the H3_REQUEST_REJECTED error code for requests\nthat were partially or fully processed.\n",
      "id": "3bbf6106d16ec8f8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 79,
      "quote": "Servers MUST NOT use the H3_REQUEST_REJECTED error code for requests that were partially or fully processed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a server abandons a\nresponse after partial processing, it SHOULD abort its response\nstream with the error code H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED.\n",
      "id": "2a58cc21bab37356",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "When a server abandons a response after partial processing, it SHOULD abort its response stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Client SHOULD use the error code H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED to cancel\nrequests.\n",
      "id": "02d2782c009ea56b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 94,
      "quote": "Client SHOULD use the error code H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED to cancel requests.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon receipt of this error code, a server MAY abruptly\nterminate the response using the error code H3_REQUEST_REJECTED if no\nprocessing was performed.\n",
      "id": "7c08634f5452864c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "Upon receipt of this error code, a server MAY abruptly terminate the response using the error code H3_REQUEST_REJECTED if no processing was performed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT use the\nH3_REQUEST_REJECTED error code, except when a server has requested\nclosure of the request stream with this error code.\n",
      "id": "d78f5dc2973a2404",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT use the H3_REQUEST_REJECTED error code, except when a server has requested closure of the request stream with this error code.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a stream is cancelled after receiving a complete response, the\nclient MAY ignore the cancellation and use the response.\n",
      "id": "1a11a9450b0f6fd1",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "If a stream is cancelled after receiving a complete response, the client MAY ignore the cancellation and use the response.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, if\na stream is cancelled after receiving a partial response, the\nresponse SHOULD NOT be used.\n",
      "id": "45e532ec5e0afa6b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 124,
      "quote": "However, if a stream is cancelled after receiving a partial response, the response SHOULD NOT be used.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Only idempotent actions such as GET,\nPUT, or DELETE can be safely retried; a client SHOULD NOT\nautomatically retry a request with a non-idempotent method unless it\nhas some means to know that the request semantics are idempotent\nindependent of the method or some means to detect that the original\nrequest was never applied.\n",
      "id": "9c1911dee0590fea",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "Only idempotent actions such as GET, PUT, or DELETE can be safely retried; a client SHOULD NOT automatically retry a request with a non-idempotent method unless it has some means to know that the request semantics are idempotent independent of the method or some means to detect that the original request was never applied.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Intermediaries that process HTTP requests or responses (i.e., any\nintermediary not acting as a tunnel) MUST NOT forward a malformed\nrequest or response.\n",
      "id": "a47d73f6439ca20d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Intermediaries that process HTTP requests or responses (i.e., any intermediary not acting as a tunnel) MUST NOT forward a malformed request or response.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Malformed requests or responses that are\ndetected MUST be treated as a stream error of type H3_MESSAGE_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "45d8732afb217228",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Malformed requests or responses that are detected MUST be treated as a stream error of type H3_MESSAGE_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For malformed requests, a server MAY send an HTTP response indicating\nthe error prior to closing or resetting the stream.\n",
      "id": "f4090f231fc43317",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "For malformed requests, a server MAY send an HTTP response indicating the error prior to closing or resetting the stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT\naccept a malformed response.\n",
      "id": "6e5624f0ba898279",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT accept a malformed response.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A\nclient MUST send only a single request on a given stream.\n",
      "id": "bdd4e5372c910a10",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "A client MUST send only a single request on a given stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "On a given stream, receipt of multiple requests or receipt of an\nadditional HTTP response following a final HTTP response MUST be\ntreated as malformed.\n",
      "id": "243672a1a1a852e1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "On a given stream, receipt of multiple requests or receipt of an additional HTTP response following a final HTTP response MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a\nconnection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "9312ce862123c9f0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY send one or more PUSH_PROMISE frames before, after, or\ninterleaved with the frames of a response message.\n",
      "id": "959c1fb65ab1ab22",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "A server MAY send one or more PUSH_PROMISE frames before, after, or interleaved with the frames of a response message.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "PUSH_PROMISE frames are not permitted on push streams;\na pushed response that includes PUSH_PROMISE frames MUST be treated\nas a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "c598184fccb799a5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "PUSH_PROMISE frames are not permitted on push streams; a pushed response that includes PUSH_PROMISE frames MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Frames of unknown types (Section 9), including reserved frames\n(Section 7.2.8) MAY be sent on a request or push stream before,\nafter, or interleaved with other frames described in this section.\n",
      "id": "197cd7f19098d184",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "Frames of unknown types (Section 9), including reserved frames (Section 7.2.8) MAY be sent on a request or push stream before, after, or interleaved with other frames described in this section.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Transfer codings (see Section 7 of [HTTP/1.1]) are not defined for\nHTTP/3; the Transfer-Encoding header field MUST NOT be used.\n",
      "id": "0ebba0f6d59dc263",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 143,
      "quote": "Transfer codings (see Section 7 of [HTTP/1.1]) are not defined for HTTP/3; the Transfer-Encoding header field MUST NOT be used.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A response MAY consist of multiple messages when and only when one or\nmore interim responses (1xx; see Section 15.2 of [HTTP]) precede a\nfinal response to the same request.\n",
      "id": "c6f166d8d3e8e227",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "A response MAY consist of multiple messages when and only when one or more interim responses (1xx; see Section 15.2 of [HTTP]) precede a final response to the same request.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After sending a request, a client MUST\nclose the stream for sending.\n",
      "id": "3bd013753d37014f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 158,
      "quote": "After sending a request, a client MUST close the stream for sending.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Unless using the CONNECT method (see\nSection 4.4), clients MUST NOT make stream closure dependent on\nreceiving a response to their request.\n",
      "id": "931a1b4963a733c3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 165,
      "quote": "Unless using the CONNECT method (see Section 4.4), clients MUST NOT make stream closure dependent on receiving a response to their request.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After sending a final\nresponse, the server MUST close the stream for sending.\n",
      "id": "11b3f372f12df786",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 173,
      "quote": "After sending a final response, the server MUST close the stream for sending.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because some messages are large or unbounded, endpoints\nSHOULD begin processing partial HTTP messages once enough of the\nmessage has been received to make progress.\n",
      "id": "b2581a73d7789d74",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 180,
      "quote": "Because some messages are large or unbounded, endpoints SHOULD begin processing partial HTTP messages once enough of the message has been received to make progress.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a client-initiated\nstream terminates without enough of the HTTP message to provide a\ncomplete response, the server SHOULD abort its response stream with\nthe error code H3_REQUEST_INCOMPLETE.\n",
      "id": "9e6790b9ab9295bc",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 188,
      "quote": "If a client-initiated stream terminates without enough of the HTTP message to provide a complete response, the server SHOULD abort its response stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_INCOMPLETE.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the server does\nnot need to receive the remainder of the request, it MAY abort\nreading the request stream, send a complete response, and cleanly\nclose the sending part of the stream.\n",
      "id": "b01c93918cdd8284",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 197,
      "quote": "When the server does not need to receive the remainder of the request, it MAY abort reading the request stream, send a complete response, and cleanly close the sending part of the stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The error code H3_NO_ERROR\nSHOULD be used when requesting that the client stop sending on the\nrequest stream.\n",
      "id": "905af24366f31e49",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 206,
      "quote": "The error code H3_NO_ERROR SHOULD be used when requesting that the client stop sending on the request stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST NOT discard complete responses as a\nresult of having their request terminated abruptly, though clients\ncan always discard responses at their discretion for other reasons.\n",
      "id": "0be3149683672a4c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 214,
      "quote": "Clients MUST NOT discard complete responses as a result of having their request terminated abruptly, though clients can always discard responses at their discretion for other reasons.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the server sends a partial or complete response but does not abort\nreading the request, clients SHOULD continue sending the content of\nthe request and close the stream normally.\n",
      "id": "96c811bcccc5f69f",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 222,
      "quote": "If the server sends a partial or complete response but does not abort reading the request, clients SHOULD continue sending the content of the request and close the stream normally.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To allow for better compression efficiency, the Cookie header field\n([COOKIES]) MAY be split into separate field lines, each with one or\nmore cookie-pairs, before compression.\n",
      "id": "81108cd4c584f78c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "To allow for better compression efficiency, the Cookie header field ([COOKIES]) MAY be split into separate field lines, each with one or more cookie-pairs, before compression.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a decompressed field\nsection contains multiple cookie field lines, these MUST be\nconcatenated into a single byte string using the two-byte delimiter\nof \"; \" (ASCII 0x3b, 0x20) before being passed into a context other\nthan HTTP/2 or HTTP/3, such as an HTTP/1.1 connection, or a generic\nHTTP server application.\n",
      "id": "b656c7fab3c4f044",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "If a decompressed field section contains multiple cookie field lines, these MUST be concatenated into a single byte string using the two-byte delimiter of \"; \" (ASCII 0x3b, 0x20) before being passed into a context other than HTTP/2 or HTTP/3, such as an HTTP/1.1 connection, or a generic HTTP server application.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An HTTP/3 implementation MAY impose a limit on the maximum size of\nthe message header it will accept on an individual HTTP message.\n",
      "id": "1f160585e275be6f",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 25,
      "quote": "An HTTP/3 implementation MAY impose a limit on the maximum size of the message header it will accept on an individual HTTP message.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An implementation that\nhas received this parameter SHOULD NOT send an HTTP message header\nthat exceeds the indicated size, as the peer will likely refuse to\nprocess it.\n",
      "id": "5f45b81e80200f23",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "An implementation that has received this parameter SHOULD NOT send an HTTP message header that exceeds the indicated size, as the peer will likely refuse to process it.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Characters in field names MUST be\nconverted to lowercase prior to their encoding.\n",
      "id": "f73c6c385c95906f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "Characters in field names MUST be converted to lowercase prior to their encoding.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A request or\nresponse containing uppercase characters in field names MUST be\ntreated as malformed.\n",
      "id": "7b354958868c096b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "A request or response containing uppercase characters in field names MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MUST NOT generate\nan HTTP/3 field section containing connection-specific fields; any\nmessage containing connection-specific fields MUST be treated as\nmalformed.\n",
      "id": "e1305508ecd287a6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 51,
      "quote": "An endpoint MUST NOT generate an HTTP/3 field section containing connection-specific fields; any message containing connection-specific fields MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The only exception to this is the TE header field, which MAY be\npresent in an HTTP/3 request header; when it is, it MUST NOT contain\nany value other than \"trailers\".\n",
      "id": "f86026918614c17e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "The only exception to this is the TE header field, which MAY be present in an HTTP/3 request header; when it is, it MUST NOT contain any value other than \"trailers\".",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An intermediary transforming an HTTP/1.x message to HTTP/3 MUST\nremove connection-specific header fields as discussed in\nSection 7.6.1 of [HTTP], or their messages will be treated by other\nHTTP/3 endpoints as malformed.\n",
      "id": "b7ac758053f3afc6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 68,
      "quote": "An intermediary transforming an HTTP/1.x message to HTTP/3 MUST remove connection-specific header fields as discussed in Section 7.6.1 of [HTTP], or their messages will be treated by other HTTP/3 endpoints as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The authority MUST NOT include the\ndeprecated userinfo subcomponent for URIs of scheme \"http\" or\n\"https\".\n",
      "id": "71e843de46315c6b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "The authority MUST NOT include the deprecated userinfo subcomponent for URIs of scheme \"http\" or \"https\".",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To ensure that the HTTP/1.1 request line can be reproduced\naccurately, this pseudo-header field MUST be omitted when\ntranslating from an HTTP/1.1 request that has a request target in\na method-specific form; see Section 7.1 of [HTTP].\n",
      "id": "a2e749ca67995c2e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "To ensure that the HTTP/1.1 request line can be reproduced accurately, this pseudo-header field MUST be omitted when translating from an HTTP/1.1 request that has a request target in a method-specific form; see Section 7.1 of [HTTP].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients that\ngenerate HTTP/3 requests directly SHOULD use the :authority\npseudo-header field instead of the Host header field.\n",
      "id": "0e5b98975d85b1fa",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "Clients that generate HTTP/3 requests directly SHOULD use the :authority pseudo-header field instead of the Host header field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An\nintermediary that converts an HTTP/3 request to HTTP/1.1 MUST\ncreate a Host field if one is not present in a request by copying\nthe value of the :authority pseudo-header field.\n",
      "id": "9c50b5c78993039f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "An intermediary that converts an HTTP/3 request to HTTP/1.1 MUST create a Host field if one is not present in a request by copying the value of the :authority pseudo-header field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This pseudo-header field MUST NOT be empty for \"http\" or \"https\"\nURIs; \"http\" or \"https\" URIs that do not contain a path component\nMUST include a value of / (ASCII 0x2f).\n",
      "id": "7c7b5c747d9f4366",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "This pseudo-header field MUST NOT be empty for \"http\" or \"https\" URIs; \"http\" or \"https\" URIs that do not contain a path component MUST include a value of / (ASCII 0x2f).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All HTTP/3 requests MUST include exactly one value for the :method,\n:scheme, and :path pseudo-header fields, unless the request is a\nCONNECT request; see Section 4.4.\n",
      "id": "a06510c05ad3949e",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 109,
      "quote": "All HTTP/3 requests MUST include exactly one value for the :method, :scheme, and :path pseudo-header fields, unless the request is a CONNECT request; see Section 4.4.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the :scheme pseudo-header field identifies a scheme that has a\nmandatory authority component (including \"http\" and \"https\"), the\nrequest MUST contain either an :authority pseudo-header field or a\nHost header field.\n",
      "id": "5945c2613a18a727",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "If the :scheme pseudo-header field identifies a scheme that has a mandatory authority component (including \"http\" and \"https\"), the request MUST contain either an :authority pseudo-header field or a Host header field.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If these fields are present, they MUST NOT be\nempty.\n",
      "id": "a0aa459c036f241b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 126,
      "quote": "If these fields are present, they MUST NOT be empty.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If both fields are present, they MUST contain the same value.\n",
      "id": "99cc61f43adc2975",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "If both fields are present, they MUST contain the same value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the scheme does not have a mandatory authority component and none\nis provided in the request target, the request MUST NOT contain the\n:authority pseudo-header or Host header fields.\n",
      "id": "cc8a88128bf701af",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 139,
      "quote": "If the scheme does not have a mandatory authority component and none is provided in the request target, the request MUST NOT contain the :authority pseudo-header or Host header fields.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This pseudo-\nheader field MUST be included in all responses; otherwise, the\nresponse is malformed (see Section 4.1.2).\n",
      "id": "4a9d0778f4b32d32",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "This pseudo- header field MUST be included in all responses; otherwise, the response is malformed (see Section 4.1.2).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT\ngenerate pseudo-header fields other than those defined in this\ndocument.\n",
      "id": "30f2de88dab0e604",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT generate pseudo-header fields other than those defined in this document.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Pseudo-header fields defined for requests MUST NOT appear\nin responses; pseudo-header fields defined for responses MUST NOT\nappear in requests.\n",
      "id": "b7660f78996da429",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "Pseudo-header fields defined for requests MUST NOT appear in responses; pseudo-header fields defined for responses MUST NOT appear in requests.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Pseudo-header fields MUST NOT appear in trailer\nsections.\n",
      "id": "7657964fb6c4e5ee",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "Pseudo-header fields MUST NOT appear in trailer sections.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST treat a request or response that contains\nundefined or invalid pseudo-header fields as malformed.\n",
      "id": "9e4476dc3f6f6bde",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 50,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST treat a request or response that contains undefined or invalid pseudo-header fields as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "All pseudo-header fields MUST appear in the header section before\nregular header fields.\n",
      "id": "d308d2ad102394d9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 57,
      "quote": "All pseudo-header fields MUST appear in the header section before regular header fields.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any request or response that contains a\npseudo-header field that appears in a header section after a regular\nheader field MUST be treated as malformed.\n",
      "id": "c6a9bec131c3a693",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "Any request or response that contains a pseudo-header field that appears in a header section after a regular header field MUST be treated as malformed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A CONNECT request MUST be constructed as follows:\n",
      "id": "c382a6578e58d953",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "A CONNECT request MUST be constructed as follows:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Extension frames MAY be used if\nspecifically permitted by the definition of the extension.\n",
      "id": "d339a8ff6854278a",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "Extension frames MAY be used if specifically permitted by the definition of the extension.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt\nof any other known frame type MUST be treated as a connection error\nof type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "1bad7beeb08c4e8c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 91,
      "quote": "Receipt of any other known frame type MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "TCP connections that remain half closed in a single\ndirection are not invalid, but are often handled poorly by servers,\nso clients SHOULD NOT close a stream for sending while they still\nexpect to receive data from the target of the CONNECT.\n",
      "id": "50f3b7149ecc4744",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "TCP connections that remain half closed in a single direction are not invalid, but are often handled poorly by servers, so clients SHOULD NOT close a stream for sending while they still expect to receive data from the target of the CONNECT.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Correspondingly, if a proxy detects an error with the stream or the\nQUIC connection, it MUST close the TCP connection.\n",
      "id": "d1a7d45e72284b37",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "Correspondingly, if a proxy detects an error with the stream or the QUIC connection, it MUST close the TCP connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the proxy\ndetects that the client has reset the stream or aborted reading from\nthe stream, it MUST close the TCP connection.\n",
      "id": "e5dbb9a0a122f725",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 115,
      "quote": "If the proxy detects that the client has reset the stream or aborted reading from the stream, it MUST close the TCP connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the stream is reset\nor reading is aborted by the client, a proxy SHOULD perform the same\noperation on the other direction in order to ensure that both\ndirections of the stream are cancelled.\n",
      "id": "f261ef65c7e50d5e",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 123,
      "quote": "If the stream is reset or reading is aborted by the client, a proxy SHOULD perform the same operation on the other direction in order to ensure that both directions of the stream are cancelled.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In all these cases, if the\nunderlying TCP implementation permits it, the proxy SHOULD send a TCP\nsegment with the RST bit set.\n",
      "id": "98a763004456cdd4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "In all these cases, if the underlying TCP implementation permits it, the proxy SHOULD send a TCP segment with the RST bit set.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Since CONNECT creates a tunnel to an arbitrary server, proxies that\nsupport CONNECT SHOULD restrict its use to a set of known ports or a\nlist of safe request targets; see Section 9.3.6 of [HTTP] for more\ndetails.\n",
      "id": "84dbeba805fcd43b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 140,
      "quote": "Since CONNECT creates a tunnel to an arbitrary server, proxies that support CONNECT SHOULD restrict its use to a set of known ports or a list of safe request targets; see Section 9.3.6 of [HTTP] for more details.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server SHOULD use push IDs sequentially, beginning from\nzero.\n",
      "id": "3915aa352e28b6f6",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 110,
      "quote": "A server SHOULD use push IDs sequentially, beginning from zero.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST treat receipt of a push stream as a connection\nerror of type H3_ID_ERROR when no MAX_PUSH_ID frame has been sent or\nwhen the stream references a push ID that is greater than the maximum\npush ID.\n",
      "id": "6fa3cba172cfcd91",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 117,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a push stream as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR when no MAX_PUSH_ID frame has been sent or when the stream references a push ID that is greater than the maximum push ID.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the\nsame push ID is promised on multiple request streams, the\ndecompressed request field sections MUST contain the same fields in\nthe same order, and both the name and the value in each field MUST be\nidentical.\n",
      "id": "8f171b2462f982d9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 126,
      "quote": "When the same push ID is promised on multiple request streams, the decompressed request field sections MUST contain the same fields in the same order, and both the name and the value in each field MUST be identical.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY push requests that have\nthe following properties:\n",
      "id": "a0f4588830b09416",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "A server MAY push requests that have the following properties:",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST include a value in the :authority pseudo-header field\nfor which the server is authoritative.\n",
      "id": "8a1daf82c968aff2",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 143,
      "quote": "The server MUST include a value in the :authority pseudo-header field for which the server is authoritative.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the client has not yet\nvalidated the connection for the origin indicated by the pushed\nrequest, it MUST perform the same verification process it would do\nbefore sending a request for that origin on the connection; see\nSection 3.3.\n",
      "id": "1dd090f4f97d5522",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "If the client has not yet validated the connection for the origin indicated by the pushed request, it MUST perform the same verification process it would do before sending a request for that origin on the connection; see Section 3.3.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If this verification fails, the client MUST NOT\nconsider the server authoritative for that origin.\n",
      "id": "e23ff005728bc4e3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 160,
      "quote": "If this verification fails, the client MUST NOT consider the server authoritative for that origin.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD send a CANCEL_PUSH frame upon receipt of a\nPUSH_PROMISE frame carrying a request that is not cacheable, is not\nknown to be safe, that indicates the presence of request content, or\nfor which it does not consider the server authoritative.\n",
      "id": "8dc17250b246db1c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 167,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD send a CANCEL_PUSH frame upon receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame carrying a request that is not cacheable, is not known to be safe, that indicates the presence of request content, or for which it does not consider the server authoritative.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any\ncorresponding responses MUST NOT be used or cached.\n",
      "id": "dc64f94bbee6efda",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 176,
      "quote": "Any corresponding responses MUST NOT be used or cached.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These\nassociations do not affect the operation of the protocol, but they\nMAY be considered by user agents when deciding how to use pushed\nresources.\n",
      "id": "7db5bc9707bd2c6e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 183,
      "quote": "These associations do not affect the operation of the protocol, but they MAY be considered by user agents when deciding how to use pushed resources.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server SHOULD send PUSH_PROMISE frames\nprior to sending HEADERS or DATA frames that reference the promised\nresponses.\n",
      "id": "af8f0f31c7b03064",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 192,
      "quote": "The server SHOULD send PUSH_PROMISE frames prior to sending HEADERS or DATA frames that reference the promised responses.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD abort reading and discard data\nalready read from push streams if no corresponding PUSH_PROMISE frame\nis processed in a reasonable amount of time.\n",
      "id": "7384cd29aa90ccfe",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 200,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD abort reading and discard data already read from push streams if no corresponding PUSH_PROMISE frame is processed in a reasonable amount of time.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Pushed responses that are not cacheable MUST NOT be stored by any\nHTTP cache.\n",
      "id": "32d11c18786fbb46",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 208,
      "quote": "Pushed responses that are not cacheable MUST NOT be stored by any HTTP cache.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "They MAY be made available to the application\nseparately.\n",
      "id": "70efdf5f37739da8",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 215,
      "quote": "They MAY be made available to the application separately.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-4.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-4.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "HTTP/3 implementations will need to open a new HTTP/3\nconnection for new requests if the existing connection has been idle\nfor longer than the idle timeout negotiated during the QUIC\nhandshake, and they SHOULD do so if approaching the idle timeout; see\nSection 10.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].\n",
      "id": "484a3ce8aed2bbe4",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "HTTP/3 implementations will need to open a new HTTP/3 connection for new requests if the existing connection has been idle for longer than the idle timeout negotiated during the QUIC handshake, and they SHOULD do so if approaching the idle timeout; see Section 10.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A gateway MAY\nmaintain connections in anticipation of need rather than incur the\nlatency cost of connection establishment to servers.\n",
      "id": "0757089a86ff30f3",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "A gateway MAY maintain connections in anticipation of need rather than incur the latency cost of connection establishment to servers.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD\nNOT actively keep connections open.\n",
      "id": "36a7691ff29c54d0",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD NOT actively keep connections open.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This\nidentifier MAY be zero if no requests or pushes were processed.\n",
      "id": "2a1a535d36c7ec57",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 101,
      "quote": "This identifier MAY be zero if no requests or pushes were processed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Upon sending a GOAWAY frame, the endpoint\nSHOULD explicitly cancel (see Sections 4.1.1 and 7.2.3) any requests\nor pushes that have identifiers greater than or equal to the one\nindicated, in order to clean up transport state for the affected\nstreams.\n",
      "id": "38689b3da54dd596",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "Upon sending a GOAWAY frame, the endpoint SHOULD explicitly cancel (see Sections 4.1.1 and 7.2.3) any requests or pushes that have identifiers greater than or equal to the one indicated, in order to clean up transport state for the affected streams.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The endpoint SHOULD continue to do so as more requests or\npushes arrive.\n",
      "id": "b4f5a0cc325e48dd",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 118,
      "quote": "The endpoint SHOULD continue to do so as more requests or pushes arrive.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT initiate new requests or promise new pushes on the\nconnection after receipt of a GOAWAY frame from the peer.\n",
      "id": "e540cc43e0208525",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT initiate new requests or promise new pushes on the connection after receipt of a GOAWAY frame from the peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients\nMAY establish a new connection to send additional requests.\n",
      "id": "f67941570f8ce6ed",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 132,
      "quote": "Clients MAY establish a new connection to send additional requests.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers MAY reject individual requests on streams below the\nindicated ID if these requests were not processed.\n",
      "id": "547e8fbd6f356e2e",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 139,
      "quote": "Servers MAY reject individual requests on streams below the indicated ID if these requests were not processed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Servers SHOULD send a GOAWAY frame when the closing of a connection\nis known in advance, even if the advance notice is small, so that the\nremote peer can know whether or not a request has been partially\nprocessed.\n",
      "id": "93f2dc64ea33b50c",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 146,
      "quote": "Servers SHOULD send a GOAWAY frame when the closing of a connection is known in advance, even if the advance notice is small, so that the remote peer can know whether or not a request has been partially processed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY send multiple GOAWAY frames indicating different\nidentifiers, but the identifier in each frame MUST NOT be greater\nthan the identifier in any previous frame, since clients might\nalready have retried unprocessed requests on another HTTP connection.\n",
      "id": "2535b50626e41c9c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 155,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY send multiple GOAWAY frames indicating different identifiers, but the identifier in each frame MUST NOT be greater than the identifier in any previous frame, since clients might already have retried unprocessed requests on another HTTP connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receiving a GOAWAY containing a larger identifier than previously\nreceived MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "aad84fe8f12682b8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 164,
      "quote": "Receiving a GOAWAY containing a larger identifier than previously received MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Like the server,\nthe client MAY send subsequent GOAWAY frames so long as the specified\npush ID is no greater than any previously sent value.\n",
      "id": "0094b17a6c3cef22",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 171,
      "quote": "Like the server, the client MAY send subsequent GOAWAY frames so long as the specified push ID is no greater than any previously sent value.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once all accepted requests and pushes have been processed, the\nendpoint can permit the connection to become idle, or it MAY initiate\nan immediate closure of the connection.\n",
      "id": "e2f6749361cc7cca",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 179,
      "quote": "Once all accepted requests and pushes have been processed, the endpoint can permit the connection to become idle, or it MAY initiate an immediate closure of the connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint that completes a\ngraceful shutdown SHOULD use the H3_NO_ERROR error code when closing\nthe connection.\n",
      "id": "e356e28a9b617d41",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 187,
      "quote": "An endpoint that completes a graceful shutdown SHOULD use the H3_NO_ERROR error code when closing the connection.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Before closing the connection, a GOAWAY frame MAY be sent to allow\nthe client to retry some requests.\n",
      "id": "55286aab802a4d87",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 21,
      "quote": "Before closing the connection, a GOAWAY frame MAY be sent to allow the client to retry some requests.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a connection terminates without a GOAWAY frame, clients MUST\nassume that any request that was sent, whether in whole or in part,\nmight have been processed.\n",
      "id": "279b4eb96da49f6c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 14,
      "quote": "If a connection terminates without a GOAWAY frame, clients MUST assume that any request that was sent, whether in whole or in part, might have been processed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-5.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-5.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In order to\npermit these streams to open, an HTTP/3 server SHOULD configure non-\nzero minimum values for the number of permitted streams and the\ninitial stream flow-control window.\n",
      "id": "757a6ff85af25157",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 24,
      "quote": "In order to permit these streams to open, an HTTP/3 server SHOULD configure non- zero minimum values for the number of permitted streams and the initial stream flow-control window.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "So as to not unnecessarily limit\nparallelism, at least 100 request streams SHOULD be permitted at a\ntime.\n",
      "id": "16544e083447ce87",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "So as to not unnecessarily limit parallelism, at least 100 request streams SHOULD be permitted at a time.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients MUST treat\nreceipt of a server-initiated bidirectional stream as a connection\nerror of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR unless such an extension has\nbeen negotiated.\n",
      "id": "7df97886005961c4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Clients MUST treat receipt of a server-initiated bidirectional stream as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR unless such an extension has been negotiated.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each side MUST initiate a single control stream at the beginning of\nthe connection and send its SETTINGS frame as the first frame on this\nstream.\n",
      "id": "5c6a913d6dab89be",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 32,
      "quote": "Each side MUST initiate a single control stream at the beginning of the connection and send its SETTINGS frame as the first frame on this stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the first frame of the control stream is any other frame\ntype, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nH3_MISSING_SETTINGS.\n",
      "id": "49ab785e362ab475",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "If the first frame of the control stream is any other frame type, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_MISSING_SETTINGS.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Only one control stream per peer is permitted;\nreceipt of a second stream claiming to be a control stream MUST be\ntreated as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "cdc40201d195e03d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "Only one control stream per peer is permitted; receipt of a second stream claiming to be a control stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nsender MUST NOT close the control stream, and the receiver MUST NOT\nrequest that the sender close the control stream.\n",
      "id": "f52a0250cab812c8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 56,
      "quote": "The sender MUST NOT close the control stream, and the receiver MUST NOT request that the sender close the control stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If either control\nstream is closed at any point, this MUST be treated as a connection\nerror of type H3_CLOSED_CRITICAL_STREAM.\n",
      "id": "b6f13f7811745223",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 64,
      "quote": "If either control stream is closed at any point, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_CLOSED_CRITICAL_STREAM.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because the contents of the control stream are used to manage the\nbehavior of other streams, endpoints SHOULD provide enough flow-\ncontrol credit to keep the peer's control stream from becoming\nblocked.\n",
      "id": "5691356d09c4a182",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 72,
      "quote": "Because the contents of the control stream are used to manage the behavior of other streams, endpoints SHOULD provide enough flow- control credit to keep the peer's control stream from becoming blocked.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Only servers can push; if a server receives a client-initiated push\nstream, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nH3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "3990b3f46a171ff4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Only servers can push; if a server receives a client-initiated push stream, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client SHOULD NOT abort reading on a push stream prior to reading\nthe push stream header, as this could lead to disagreement between\nclient and server on which push IDs have already been consumed.\n",
      "id": "e0de61642e003a1b",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 45,
      "quote": "A client SHOULD NOT abort reading on a push stream prior to reading the push stream header, as this could lead to disagreement between client and server on which push IDs have already been consumed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each push ID MUST only be used once in a push stream header.\n",
      "id": "a4a6c565843a8ade",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "Each push ID MUST only be used once in a push stream header.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a\nclient detects that a push stream header includes a push ID that was\nused in another push stream header, the client MUST treat this as a\nconnection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "d64170d26820da2c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 59,
      "quote": "If a client detects that a push stream header includes a push ID that was used in another push stream header, the client MUST treat this as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "They MAY also be\nsent on connections where no data is currently being transferred.\n",
      "id": "28c9d02ce683de09",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 19,
      "quote": "They MAY also be sent on connections where no data is currently being transferred.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider these streams to have any meaning upon\nreceipt.\n",
      "id": "85b46f2a993db513",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider these streams to have any meaning upon receipt.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When sending a reserved stream type,\nthe implementation MAY either terminate the stream cleanly or reset\nit.\n",
      "id": "62016693af93c5ed",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 33,
      "quote": "When sending a reserved stream type, the implementation MAY either terminate the stream cleanly or reset it.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When resetting the stream, either the H3_NO_ERROR error code or\na reserved error code (Section 8.1) SHOULD be used.\n",
      "id": "33125ae624a6f02a",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "When resetting the stream, either the H3_NO_ERROR error code or a reserved error code (Section 8.1) SHOULD be used.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Therefore, the transport parameters sent by both clients\nand servers MUST allow the peer to create at least three\nunidirectional streams.\n",
      "id": "f041d2fe59a3ec7c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 73,
      "quote": "Therefore, the transport parameters sent by both clients and servers MUST allow the peer to create at least three unidirectional streams.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These transport parameters SHOULD also\nprovide at least 1,024 bytes of flow-control credit to each\nunidirectional stream.\n",
      "id": "2be1f4a755942aab",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "These transport parameters SHOULD also provide at least 1,024 bytes of flow-control credit to each unidirectional stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD create the HTTP control stream as well as the\nunidirectional streams required by mandatory extensions (such as the\nQPACK encoder and decoder streams) first, and then create additional\nstreams as allowed by their peer.\n",
      "id": "f9fffa36e5e586b3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD create the HTTP control stream as well as the unidirectional streams required by mandatory extensions (such as the QPACK encoder and decoder streams) first, and then create additional streams as allowed by their peer.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Recipients of unknown stream types MUST\neither abort reading of the stream or discard incoming data without\nfurther processing.\n",
      "id": "c0bd3dc16eff47d1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 98,
      "quote": "Recipients of unknown stream types MUST either abort reading of the stream or discard incoming data without further processing.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If reading is aborted, the recipient SHOULD use\nthe H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR error code or a reserved error code\n(Section 8.1).\n",
      "id": "ece28172445a589d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "If reading is aborted, the recipient SHOULD use the H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR error code or a reserved error code (Section 8.1).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The recipient MUST NOT consider unknown stream types\nto be a connection error of any kind.\n",
      "id": "830f8b47859906b0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 114,
      "quote": "The recipient MUST NOT consider unknown stream types to be a connection error of any kind.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "As certain stream types can affect connection state, a recipient\nSHOULD NOT discard data from incoming unidirectional streams prior to\nreading the stream type.\n",
      "id": "973a11615b6b3c68",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 121,
      "quote": "As certain stream types can affect connection state, a recipient SHOULD NOT discard data from incoming unidirectional streams prior to reading the stream type.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MAY send stream types before knowing whether the peer\nsupports them.\n",
      "id": "f78aaab67f13e2f0",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 129,
      "quote": "Implementations MAY send stream types before knowing whether the peer supports them.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, stream types that could modify the state or\nsemantics of existing protocol components, including QPACK or other\nextensions, MUST NOT be sent until the peer is known to support them.\n",
      "id": "0e083fc722fadb44",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 136,
      "quote": "However, stream types that could modify the state or semantics of existing protocol components, including QPACK or other extensions, MUST NOT be sent until the peer is known to support them.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver MUST tolerate unidirectional streams being\nclosed or reset prior to the reception of the unidirectional stream\nheader.\n",
      "id": "019770d70175fafb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 144,
      "quote": "A receiver MUST tolerate unidirectional streams being closed or reset prior to the reception of the unidirectional stream header.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-6.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-6.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each frame's payload MUST contain exactly the fields identified in\nits description.\n",
      "id": "4bffaa7b2c1c3152",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 37,
      "quote": "Each frame's payload MUST contain exactly the fields identified in its description.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A frame payload that contains additional bytes\nafter the identified fields or a frame payload that terminates before\nthe end of the identified fields MUST be treated as a connection\nerror of type H3_FRAME_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "42764cbfdaecb2b8",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 44,
      "quote": "A frame payload that contains additional bytes after the identified fields or a frame payload that terminates before the end of the identified fields MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In particular, redundant length\nencodings MUST be verified to be self-consistent; see Section 10.8.\n",
      "id": "e2c762004fc06a88",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 53,
      "quote": "In particular, redundant length encodings MUST be verified to be self-consistent; see Section 10.8.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a stream terminates cleanly, if the last frame on the stream was\ntruncated, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nH3_FRAME_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "0b7738d81d4a615a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "When a stream terminates cleanly, if the last frame on the stream was truncated, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "DATA frames MUST be associated with an HTTP request or response.\n",
      "id": "127152604cf3e41a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "DATA frames MUST be associated with an HTTP request or response.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If\na DATA frame is received on a control stream, the recipient MUST\nrespond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "7b602960014f50cc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "If a DATA frame is received on a control stream, the recipient MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a HEADERS frame is received on a control stream, the recipient\nMUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "3a850aca5d6d4bbd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "If a HEADERS frame is received on a control stream, the recipient MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server SHOULD\nabort sending the resource, but the mechanism to do so depends on the\nstate of the corresponding push stream.\n",
      "id": "4aec43ec1bda0329",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "The server SHOULD abort sending the resource, but the mechanism to do so depends on the state of the corresponding push stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the push stream is\nopen, the server SHOULD abruptly terminate that stream.\n",
      "id": "06fb5e7ed0f290d1",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "If the push stream is open, the server SHOULD abruptly terminate that stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the push\nstream has already ended, the server MAY still abruptly terminate the\nstream or MAY take no action.\n",
      "id": "ddbb733d9eaaef91",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 76,
      "quote": "If the push stream has already ended, the server MAY still abruptly terminate the stream or MAY take no action.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Regardless of\nwhether a push stream has been opened, a server SHOULD send a\nCANCEL_PUSH frame when it determines that promise will not be\nfulfilled.\n",
      "id": "31caab4fc1dbcade",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "Regardless of whether a push stream has been opened, a server SHOULD send a CANCEL_PUSH frame when it determines that promise will not be fulfilled.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client SHOULD NOT send a CANCEL_PUSH frame\nwhen it has already received a corresponding push stream.\n",
      "id": "f5487cf12913c622",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 93,
      "quote": "A client SHOULD NOT send a CANCEL_PUSH frame when it has already received a corresponding push stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The\nclient SHOULD abort reading the stream with an error code of\nH3_REQUEST_CANCELLED.\n",
      "id": "7eab7f35fb09bdf3",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 100,
      "quote": "The client SHOULD abort reading the stream with an error code of H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receiving a\nCANCEL_PUSH frame on a stream other than the control stream MUST be\ntreated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "e76ac93e327f9deb",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 108,
      "quote": "Receiving a CANCEL_PUSH frame on a stream other than the control stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a CANCEL_PUSH frame is received that\nreferences a push ID greater than currently allowed on the\nconnection, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nH3_ID_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "3d9ea830b4cdb36a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 116,
      "quote": "If a CANCEL_PUSH frame is received that references a push ID greater than currently allowed on the connection, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server receives a CANCEL_PUSH frame for a push\nID that has not yet been mentioned by a PUSH_PROMISE frame, this MUST\nbe treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "5bf7b51068068b54",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 125,
      "quote": "If a server receives a CANCEL_PUSH frame for a push ID that has not yet been mentioned by a PUSH_PROMISE frame, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.3.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.3",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints SHOULD include at least one such setting in their\nSETTINGS frame.\n",
      "id": "110359c950c5514d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 29,
      "quote": "Endpoints SHOULD include at least one such setting in their SETTINGS frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider such settings to have\nany meaning upon receipt.\n",
      "id": "1ff1049e2acf2dd5",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 36,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider such settings to have any meaning upon receipt.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These reserved settings MUST NOT be sent, and\ntheir receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nH3_SETTINGS_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "75abee02df644c35",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 43,
      "quote": "These reserved settings MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An HTTP implementation MUST NOT send frames or requests that would be\ninvalid based on its current understanding of the peer's settings.\n",
      "id": "ffd79ebc5a82d9bd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "An HTTP implementation MUST NOT send frames or requests that would be invalid based on its current understanding of the peer's settings.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each endpoint SHOULD use\nthese initial values to send messages before the peer's SETTINGS\nframe has arrived, as packets carrying the settings can be lost or\ndelayed.\n",
      "id": "432e5027f8762abe",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "Each endpoint SHOULD use these initial values to send messages before the peer's SETTINGS frame has arrived, as packets carrying the settings can be lost or delayed.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST NOT require any data to be received from\nthe peer prior to sending the SETTINGS frame; settings MUST be sent\nas soon as the transport is ready to send data.\n",
      "id": "5e6b147e55423fa0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT require any data to be received from the peer prior to sending the SETTINGS frame; settings MUST be sent as soon as the transport is ready to send data.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD\nNOT wait indefinitely for SETTINGS to arrive before sending requests,\nbut they SHOULD process received datagrams in order to increase the\nlikelihood of processing SETTINGS before sending the first request.\n",
      "id": "39adaf45ccc58747",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 86,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD NOT wait indefinitely for SETTINGS to arrive before sending requests, but they SHOULD process received datagrams in order to increase the likelihood of processing SETTINGS before sending the first request.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients\nSHOULD store the settings the server provided in the HTTP/3\nconnection where resumption information was provided, but they MAY\nopt not to store settings in certain cases (e.g., if the session\nticket is received before the SETTINGS frame).\n",
      "id": "9289dd1e0f49fe77",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 95,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD store the settings the server provided in the HTTP/3 connection where resumption information was provided, but they MAY opt not to store settings in certain cases (e.g., if the session ticket is received before the SETTINGS frame).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST comply\nwith stored settings -- or default values if no values are stored --\nwhen attempting 0-RTT.\n",
      "id": "64cca4e5efb0d987",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "A client MUST comply with stored settings -- or default values if no values are stored -- when attempting 0-RTT.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a server has provided new settings,\nclients MUST comply with those values.\n",
      "id": "cddeeae79b42ad02",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "Once a server has provided new settings, clients MUST comply with those values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the\nserver cannot determine that the settings remembered by a client are\ncompatible with its current settings, it MUST NOT accept 0-RTT data.\n",
      "id": "019ab9a277c307dc",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "If the server cannot determine that the settings remembered by a client are compatible with its current settings, it MUST NOT accept 0-RTT data.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY accept 0-RTT and subsequently provide different settings\nin its SETTINGS frame.\n",
      "id": "72b2dd5043f6ef94",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 128,
      "quote": "A server MAY accept 0-RTT and subsequently provide different settings in its SETTINGS frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If 0-RTT data is accepted by the server, its\nSETTINGS frame MUST NOT reduce any limits or alter any values that\nmight be violated by the client with its 0-RTT data.\n",
      "id": "a3a828590a6bd9e6",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 135,
      "quote": "If 0-RTT data is accepted by the server, its SETTINGS frame MUST NOT reduce any limits or alter any values that might be violated by the client with its 0-RTT data.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The server MUST\ninclude all settings that differ from their default values.\n",
      "id": "0ddddef0505cc5fd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 143,
      "quote": "The server MUST include all settings that differ from their default values.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a\nserver accepts 0-RTT but then sends settings that are not compatible\nwith the previously specified settings, this MUST be treated as a\nconnection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "fcf12e48eb6cefcd",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 150,
      "quote": "If a server accepts 0-RTT but then sends settings that are not compatible with the previously specified settings, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a server accepts\n0-RTT but then sends a SETTINGS frame that omits a setting value that\nthe client understands (apart from reserved setting identifiers) that\nwas previously specified to have a non-default value, this MUST be\ntreated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "2762ff8045d49714",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 159,
      "quote": "If a server accepts 0-RTT but then sends a SETTINGS frame that omits a setting value that the client understands (apart from reserved setting identifiers) that was previously specified to have a non-default value, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.2.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4.2",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A SETTINGS frame MUST be sent as the first frame of\neach control stream (see Section 6.2.1) by each peer, and it MUST NOT\nbe sent subsequently.\n",
      "id": "f4f78434a390d332",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 61,
      "quote": "A SETTINGS frame MUST be sent as the first frame of each control stream (see Section 6.2.1) by each peer, and it MUST NOT be sent subsequently.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an endpoint receives a second SETTINGS\nframe on the control stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a\nconnection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "ba37e1fbe330665a",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 69,
      "quote": "If an endpoint receives a second SETTINGS frame on the control stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "SETTINGS frames MUST NOT be sent on any stream other than the control\nstream.\n",
      "id": "0326ee95669b027b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 77,
      "quote": "SETTINGS frames MUST NOT be sent on any stream other than the control stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an endpoint receives a SETTINGS frame on a different\nstream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type\nH3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "12cfbf44692554a1",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 84,
      "quote": "If an endpoint receives a SETTINGS frame on a different stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The same setting identifier MUST NOT occur more than once in the\nSETTINGS frame.\n",
      "id": "53339c2a59192f3c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 92,
      "quote": "The same setting identifier MUST NOT occur more than once in the SETTINGS frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A receiver MAY treat the presence of duplicate\nsetting identifiers as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "004e5121caeeb077",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 99,
      "quote": "A receiver MAY treat the presence of duplicate setting identifiers as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An implementation MUST ignore any parameter with an identifier it\ndoes not understand.\n",
      "id": "3c9a2337b928bb98",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 106,
      "quote": "An implementation MUST ignore any parameter with an identifier it does not understand.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.4.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.4",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST NOT use a push ID that is larger than the client has\nprovided in a MAX_PUSH_ID frame (Section 7.2.7).\n",
      "id": "ddef3080399146ba",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 60,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT use a push ID that is larger than the client has provided in a MAX_PUSH_ID frame (Section 7.2.7).",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST treat\nreceipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame that contains a larger push ID than\nthe client has advertised as a connection error of H3_ID_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "a16190e5b336709d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame that contains a larger push ID than the client has advertised as a connection error of H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MAY use the same push ID in multiple PUSH_PROMISE frames.\n",
      "id": "a47aa454bbdef2fc",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 75,
      "quote": "A server MAY use the same push ID in multiple PUSH_PROMISE frames.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If so, the decompressed request header sets MUST contain the same\nfields in the same order, and both the name and the value in each\nfield MUST be exact matches.\n",
      "id": "27f4f80a52e71b41",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 81,
      "quote": "If so, the decompressed request header sets MUST contain the same fields in the same order, and both the name and the value in each field MUST be exact matches.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Clients SHOULD compare the request\nheader sections for resources promised multiple times.\n",
      "id": "21931cea7a58c819",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 89,
      "quote": "Clients SHOULD compare the request header sections for resources promised multiple times.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a client\nreceives a push ID that has already been promised and detects a\nmismatch, it MUST respond with a connection error of type\nH3_GENERAL_PROTOCOL_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "229fb775ebc4e8e9",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 96,
      "quote": "If a client receives a push ID that has already been promised and detects a mismatch, it MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_GENERAL_PROTOCOL_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the decompressed field sections match\nexactly, the client SHOULD associate the pushed content with each\nstream on which a PUSH_PROMISE frame was received.\n",
      "id": "54e5f27c49bf0f70",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 105,
      "quote": "If the decompressed field sections match exactly, the client SHOULD associate the pushed content with each stream on which a PUSH_PROMISE frame was received.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server SHOULD\navoid reusing a push ID over a long period.\n",
      "id": "98b391d596d52e3d",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 113,
      "quote": "A server SHOULD avoid reusing a push ID over a long period.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a PUSH_PROMISE frame is received on the control stream, the client\nMUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "c2058bd747e103f7",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 120,
      "quote": "If a PUSH_PROMISE frame is received on the control stream, the client MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST NOT send a PUSH_PROMISE frame.\n",
      "id": "ed53d52b7b2c9488",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 127,
      "quote": "A client MUST NOT send a PUSH_PROMISE frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST treat the\nreceipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame as a connection error of type\nH3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "a264e1afa211fa33",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 133,
      "quote": "A server MUST treat the receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.5.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.5",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST treat receipt of a GOAWAY frame containing a stream ID\nof any other type as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "411ae7d197b5e75f",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 35,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat receipt of a GOAWAY frame containing a stream ID of any other type as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST treat a GOAWAY frame on a stream other than\nthe control stream as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "bca37440c7c8dc9d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat a GOAWAY frame on a stream other than the control stream as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.6.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.6",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Receipt\nof a MAX_PUSH_ID frame on any other stream MUST be treated as a\nconnection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "647f128b19cf5ab3",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 41,
      "quote": "Receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame on any other stream MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A server MUST NOT send a MAX_PUSH_ID frame.\n",
      "id": "96610cfb897dfeab",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 49,
      "quote": "A server MUST NOT send a MAX_PUSH_ID frame.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A client MUST treat the\nreceipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame as a connection error of type\nH3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "d70507bb4dc8e33c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 55,
      "quote": "A client MUST treat the receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A MAX_PUSH_ID frame cannot reduce the maximum push\nID; receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame that contains a smaller value than\npreviously received MUST be treated as a connection error of type\nH3_ID_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "2b438eda7d19ed47",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 63,
      "quote": "A MAX_PUSH_ID frame cannot reduce the maximum push ID; receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame that contains a smaller value than previously received MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.7.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.7",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These frames have no semantics, and\nthey MAY be sent on any stream where frames are allowed to be sent.\n",
      "id": "49253564b73f9473",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 20,
      "quote": "These frames have no semantics, and they MAY be sent on any stream where frames are allowed to be sent.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Endpoints MUST\nNOT consider these frames to have any meaning upon receipt.\n",
      "id": "f9662646873fc86c",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 27,
      "quote": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider these frames to have any meaning upon receipt.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "These frame\ntypes MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a\nconnection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.\n",
      "id": "81557ad6ddd786b0",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "These frame types MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-7.2.8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-7.2.8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations SHOULD select an error code from this space with some\nprobability when they would have sent H3_NO_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "661faba88f31a532",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 67,
      "quote": "Implementations SHOULD select an error code from this space with some probability when they would have sent H3_NO_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-8.1.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-8.1",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An endpoint MAY choose to treat a stream error as a connection error\nunder certain circumstances, closing the entire connection in\nresponse to a condition on a single stream.\n",
      "id": "31df5bbeae17f51c",
      "level": "May",
      "line": 40,
      "quote": "An endpoint MAY choose to treat a stream error as a connection error under certain circumstances, closing the entire connection in response to a condition on a single stream.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because new error codes can be defined without negotiation (see\nSection 9), use of an error code in an unexpected context or receipt\nof an unknown error code MUST be treated as equivalent to\nH3_NO_ERROR.\n",
      "id": "f005fa2c08aa8cd4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 48,
      "quote": "Because new error codes can be defined without negotiation (see Section 9), use of an error code in an unexpected context or receipt of an unknown error code MUST be treated as equivalent to H3_NO_ERROR.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-8.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-8",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST ignore unknown or unsupported values in all\nextensible protocol elements.\n",
      "id": "fbee3adc4145ecde",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 47,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST ignore unknown or unsupported values in all extensible protocol elements.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Implementations MUST discard data or\nabort reading on unidirectional streams that have unknown or\nunsupported types.\n",
      "id": "81e9cbc8751f2cce",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 54,
      "quote": "Implementations MUST discard data or abort reading on unidirectional streams that have unknown or unsupported types.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "However, where a known frame type is required to be in\na specific location, such as the SETTINGS frame as the first frame of\nthe control stream (see Section 6.2.1), an unknown frame type does\nnot satisfy that requirement and SHOULD be treated as an error.\n",
      "id": "5c8f24fa1ff2b911",
      "level": "Should",
      "line": 62,
      "quote": "However, where a known frame type is required to be in a specific location, such as the SETTINGS frame as the first frame of the control stream (see Section 6.2.1), an unknown frame type does not satisfy that requirement and SHOULD be treated as an error.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Extensions that could change the semantics of existing protocol\ncomponents MUST be negotiated before being used.\n",
      "id": "66eab4393614241d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 71,
      "quote": "Extensions that could change the semantics of existing protocol components MUST be negotiated before being used.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a setting is used for extension negotiation, the default\nvalue MUST be defined in such a fashion that the extension is\ndisabled if the setting is omitted.\n",
      "id": "ba1f10f5ae72dca4",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 78,
      "quote": "If a setting is used for extension negotiation, the default value MUST be defined in such a fashion that the extension is disabled if the setting is omitted.",
      "source": "specs/www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114/section-9.toml",
      "target_path": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9114",
      "target_section": "section-9",
      "type": "SPEC"
    }
  ],
