            "   12. References",
            "     12.1.  Normative References",
            "     12.2.  Informative References",
            "   Appendix A.  Considerations for Transitioning from HTTP/2",
            "     A.1.  Streams",
            "     A.2.  HTTP Frame Types",
            "       A.2.1.  Prioritization Differences",
            "       A.2.2.  Field Compression Differences",
            "       A.2.3.  Flow-Control Differences",
            "       A.2.4.  Guidance for New Frame Type Definitions",
            "       A.2.5.  Comparison of HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 Frame Types",
            "     A.3.  HTTP/2 SETTINGS Parameters",
            "     A.4.  HTTP/2 Error Codes",
            "       A.4.1.  Mapping between HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 Errors",
            "   Acknowledgments",
            "   Index",
            "   Author's Address"
          ],
          "title": "Table of Contents"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP semantics ([HTTP]) are used for a broad range of services on the",
            "   Internet.  These semantics have most commonly been used with HTTP/1.1",
            "   and HTTP/2.  HTTP/1.1 has been used over a variety of transport and",
            "   session layers, while HTTP/2 has been used primarily with TLS over",
            "   TCP.  HTTP/3 supports the same semantics over a new transport",
            "   protocol: QUIC."
          ],
          "title": "Introduction"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1.1",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/1.1 ([HTTP/1.1]) uses whitespace-delimited text fields to convey",
            "   HTTP messages.  While these exchanges are human readable, using",
            "   whitespace for message formatting leads to parsing complexity and",
            "   excessive tolerance of variant behavior.",
            "",
            "   Because HTTP/1.1 does not include a multiplexing layer, multiple TCP",
            "   connections are often used to service requests in parallel.  However,",
            "   that has a negative impact on congestion control and network",
            "   efficiency, since TCP does not share congestion control across",
            "   multiple connections.",
            "",
            "   HTTP/2 ([HTTP/2]) introduced a binary framing and multiplexing layer",
            "   to improve latency without modifying the transport layer.  However,",
            "   because the parallel nature of HTTP/2's multiplexing is not visible",
            "   to TCP's loss recovery mechanisms, a lost or reordered packet causes",
            "   all active transactions to experience a stall regardless of whether",
            "   that transaction was directly impacted by the lost packet."
          ],
          "title": "Prior Versions of HTTP"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-1.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The QUIC transport protocol incorporates stream multiplexing and per-",
            "   stream flow control, similar to that provided by the HTTP/2 framing",
            "   layer.  By providing reliability at the stream level and congestion",
            "   control across the entire connection, QUIC has the capability to",
            "   improve the performance of HTTP compared to a TCP mapping.  QUIC also",
            "   incorporates TLS 1.3 ([TLS]) at the transport layer, offering",
            "   comparable confidentiality and integrity to running TLS over TCP,",
            "   with the improved connection setup latency of TCP Fast Open ([TFO]).",
            "",
            "   This document defines HTTP/3: a mapping of HTTP semantics over the",
            "   QUIC transport protocol, drawing heavily on the design of HTTP/2.",
            "   HTTP/3 relies on QUIC to provide confidentiality and integrity",
            "   protection of data; peer authentication; and reliable, in-order, per-",
            "   stream delivery.  While delegating stream lifetime and flow-control",
            "   issues to QUIC, a binary framing similar to the HTTP/2 framing is",
            "   used on each stream.  Some HTTP/2 features are subsumed by QUIC,",
            "   while other features are implemented atop QUIC.",
            "",
            "   QUIC is described in [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  For a full description of",
            "   HTTP/2, see [HTTP/2]."
          ],
          "title": "Delegation to QUIC"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/3 provides a transport for HTTP semantics using the QUIC",
            "   transport protocol and an internal framing layer similar to HTTP/2.",
            "",
            "   Once a client knows that an HTTP/3 server exists at a certain",
            "   endpoint, it opens a QUIC connection.  QUIC provides protocol",
            "   negotiation, stream-based multiplexing, and flow control.  Discovery",
            "   of an HTTP/3 endpoint is described in Section 3.1.",
            "",
            "   Within each stream, the basic unit of HTTP/3 communication is a frame",
            "   (Section 7.2).  Each frame type serves a different purpose.  For",
            "   example, HEADERS and DATA frames form the basis of HTTP requests and",
            "   responses (Section 4.1).  Frames that apply to the entire connection",
            "   are conveyed on a dedicated control stream.",
            "",
            "   Multiplexing of requests is performed using the QUIC stream",
            "   abstraction, which is described in Section 2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "   Each request-response pair consumes a single QUIC stream.  Streams",
            "   are independent of each other, so one stream that is blocked or",
            "   suffers packet loss does not prevent progress on other streams.",
            "",
            "   Server push is an interaction mode introduced in HTTP/2 ([HTTP/2])",
            "   that permits a server to push a request-response exchange to a client",
            "   in anticipation of the client making the indicated request.  This",
            "   trades off network usage against a potential latency gain.  Several",
            "   HTTP/3 frames are used to manage server push, such as PUSH_PROMISE,",
            "   MAX_PUSH_ID, and CANCEL_PUSH.",
            "",
            "   As in HTTP/2, request and response fields are compressed for",
            "   transmission.  Because HPACK ([HPACK]) relies on in-order",
            "   transmission of compressed field sections (a guarantee not provided",
            "   by QUIC), HTTP/3 replaces HPACK with QPACK ([QPACK]).  QPACK uses",
            "   separate unidirectional streams to modify and track field table",
            "   state, while encoded field sections refer to the state of the table",
            "   without modifying it."
          ],
          "title": "HTTP/3 Protocol Overview"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The following sections provide a detailed overview of the lifecycle",
            "   of an HTTP/3 connection:",
            "",
            "   *  \"Connection Setup and Management\" (Section 3) covers how an HTTP/3",
            "      endpoint is discovered and an HTTP/3 connection is established.",
            "",
            "   *  \"Expressing HTTP Semantics in HTTP/3\" (Section 4) describes how",
            "      HTTP semantics are expressed using frames.",
            "",
            "   *  \"Connection Closure\" (Section 5) describes how HTTP/3 connections",
            "      are terminated, either gracefully or abruptly.",
            "",
            "   The details of the wire protocol and interactions with the transport",
            "   are described in subsequent sections:",
            "",
            "   *  \"Stream Mapping and Usage\" (Section 6) describes the way QUIC",
            "      streams are used.",
            "",
            "   *  \"HTTP Framing Layer\" (Section 7) describes the frames used on most",
            "      streams.",
            "",
            "   *  \"Error Handling\" (Section 8) describes how error conditions are",
            "      handled and expressed, either on a particular stream or for the",
            "      connection as a whole.",
            "",
            "   Additional resources are provided in the final sections:",
            "",
            "   *  \"Extensions to HTTP/3\" (Section 9) describes how new capabilities",
            "      can be added in future documents.",
            "",
            "   *  A more detailed comparison between HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 can be found",
            "      in Appendix A."
          ],
          "title": "Document Organization"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The key words \"MUST\", \"MUST NOT\", \"REQUIRED\", \"SHALL\", \"SHALL NOT\",",
            "   \"SHOULD\", \"SHOULD NOT\", \"RECOMMENDED\", \"NOT RECOMMENDED\", \"MAY\", and",
            "   \"OPTIONAL\" in this document are to be interpreted as described in",
            "   BCP 14 [RFC2119] [RFC8174] when, and only when, they appear in all",
            "   capitals, as shown here.",
            "",
            "   This document uses the variable-length integer encoding from",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   The following terms are used:",
            "",
            "   abort:  An abrupt termination of a connection or stream, possibly due",
            "      to an error condition.",
            "",
            "   client:  The endpoint that initiates an HTTP/3 connection.  Clients",
            "      send HTTP requests and receive HTTP responses.",
            "",
            "   connection:  A transport-layer connection between two endpoints using",
            "      QUIC as the transport protocol.",
            "",
            "   connection error:  An error that affects the entire HTTP/3",
            "      connection.",
            "",
            "   endpoint:  Either the client or server of the connection.",
            "",
            "   frame:  The smallest unit of communication on a stream in HTTP/3,",
            "      consisting of a header and a variable-length sequence of bytes",
            "      structured according to the frame type.",
            "",
            "      Protocol elements called \"frames\" exist in both this document and",
            "      [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  Where frames from [QUIC-TRANSPORT] are",
            "      referenced, the frame name will be prefaced with \"QUIC\".  For",
            "      example, \"QUIC CONNECTION_CLOSE frames\".  References without this",
            "      preface refer to frames defined in Section 7.2.",
            "",
            "   HTTP/3 connection:  A QUIC connection where the negotiated",
            "      application protocol is HTTP/3.",
            "",
            "   peer:  An endpoint.  When discussing a particular endpoint, \"peer\"",
            "      refers to the endpoint that is remote to the primary subject of",
            "      discussion.",
            "",
            "   receiver:  An endpoint that is receiving frames.",
            "",
            "   sender:  An endpoint that is transmitting frames.",
            "",
            "   server:  The endpoint that accepts an HTTP/3 connection.  Servers",
            "      receive HTTP requests and send HTTP responses.",
            "",
            "   stream:  A bidirectional or unidirectional bytestream provided by the",
            "      QUIC transport.  All streams within an HTTP/3 connection can be",
            "      considered \"HTTP/3 streams\", but multiple stream types are defined",
            "      within HTTP/3.",
            "",
            "   stream error:  An application-level error on the individual stream.",
            "",
            "   The term \"content\" is defined in Section 6.4 of [HTTP].",
            "",
            "   Finally, the terms \"resource\", \"message\", \"user agent\", \"origin",
            "   server\", \"gateway\", \"intermediary\", \"proxy\", and \"tunnel\" are defined",
            "   in Section 3 of [HTTP].",
            "",
            "   Packet diagrams in this document use the format defined in",
            "   Section 1.3 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT] to illustrate the order and size of",
            "   fields."
          ],
          "title": "Conventions and Terminology"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Connection Setup and Management"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.1",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP relies on the notion of an authoritative response: a response",
            "   that has been determined to be the most appropriate response for that",
            "   request given the state of the target resource at the time of",
            "   response message origination by (or at the direction of) the origin",
            "   server identified within the target URI.  Locating an authoritative",
            "   server for an HTTP URI is discussed in Section 4.3 of [HTTP].",
            "",
            "   The \"https\" scheme associates authority with possession of a",
            "   certificate that the client considers to be trustworthy for the host",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   identified by the authority component of the URI.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dfc838f7590c0779",
                  "7afe765dea465088"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Upon receiving a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dfc838f7590c0779",
                  "7afe765dea465088"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "server certificate in the TLS handshake, the client MUST verify that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dfc838f7590c0779",
                  "7afe765dea465088"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the certificate is an acceptable match for the URI's origin server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dfc838f7590c0779",
                  "7afe765dea465088"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "using the process described in Section 4.3.4 of [HTTP]."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e2ee7236b371c76c",
                  "a6c16dadde40bbb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e2ee7236b371c76c",
                  "a6c16dadde40bbb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "certificate cannot be verified with respect to the URI's origin"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e2ee7236b371c76c",
                  "a6c16dadde40bbb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "server, the client MUST NOT consider the server authoritative for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e2ee7236b371c76c",
                  "a6c16dadde40bbb0"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "that origin."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "34b58a268408d27b",
                  "e29093aeb8d8cb70"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "A client MAY attempt access to a resource with an \"https\" URI by"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "34b58a268408d27b",
                  "e29093aeb8d8cb70"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "resolving the host identifier to an IP address, establishing a QUIC"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "34b58a268408d27b",
                  "e29093aeb8d8cb70"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "connection to that address on the indicated port (including"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "34b58a268408d27b",
                  "e29093aeb8d8cb70"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "validation of the server certificate as described above), and sending"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "34b58a268408d27b",
                  "e29093aeb8d8cb70"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "an HTTP/3 request message targeting the URI to the server over that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "34b58a268408d27b",
                  "e29093aeb8d8cb70"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "secured connection."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Unless some other mechanism is used to select"
              }
            ],
            "   HTTP/3, the token \"h3\" is used in the Application-Layer Protocol",
            "   Negotiation (ALPN; see [RFC7301]) extension during the TLS handshake.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "154fdca498c2b9e7",
                  "09136c7e1c936c36"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Connectivity problems (e.g., blocking UDP) can result in a failure to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "154fdca498c2b9e7",
                  "09136c7e1c936c36"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "establish a QUIC connection; clients SHOULD attempt to use TCP-based"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "154fdca498c2b9e7",
                  "09136c7e1c936c36"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "versions of HTTP in this case."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "811bf3793e2d1aae",
                  "044f6306fc277fcb"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Servers MAY serve HTTP/3 on any UDP port; an alternative service"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "811bf3793e2d1aae",
                  "044f6306fc277fcb"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "advertisement always includes an explicit port, and URIs contain"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "811bf3793e2d1aae",
                  "044f6306fc277fcb"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "either an explicit port or a default port associated with the scheme."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "7afe765dea465088",
            "7afe765dea465088",
            "7afe765dea465088",
            "7afe765dea465088",
            "a6c16dadde40bbb0",
            "a6c16dadde40bbb0",
            "a6c16dadde40bbb0",
            "a6c16dadde40bbb0",
            "e29093aeb8d8cb70",
            "e29093aeb8d8cb70",
            "e29093aeb8d8cb70",
            "e29093aeb8d8cb70",
            "e29093aeb8d8cb70",
            "e29093aeb8d8cb70",
            "09136c7e1c936c36",
            "09136c7e1c936c36",
            "09136c7e1c936c36",
            "044f6306fc277fcb",
            "044f6306fc277fcb",
            "044f6306fc277fcb"
          ],
          "title": "Discovering an HTTP/3 Endpoint"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.1.1",
          "lines": [
            "   An HTTP origin can advertise the availability of an equivalent HTTP/3",
            "   endpoint via the Alt-Svc HTTP response header field or the HTTP/2",
            "   ALTSVC frame ([ALTSVC]) using the \"h3\" ALPN token.",
            "",
            "   For example, an origin could indicate in an HTTP response that HTTP/3",
            "   was available on UDP port 50781 at the same hostname by including the",
            "   following header field:",
            "",
            "   Alt-Svc: h3=\":50781\"",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f5cc95dc3bae598",
                  "66c2ed8bdaf9064d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "On receipt of an Alt-Svc record indicating HTTP/3 support, a client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f5cc95dc3bae598",
                  "66c2ed8bdaf9064d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "MAY attempt to establish a QUIC connection to the indicated host and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f5cc95dc3bae598",
                  "66c2ed8bdaf9064d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "port; if this connection is successful, the client can send HTTP"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f5cc95dc3bae598",
                  "66c2ed8bdaf9064d"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "requests using the mapping described in this document."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "66c2ed8bdaf9064d",
            "66c2ed8bdaf9064d",
            "66c2ed8bdaf9064d",
            "66c2ed8bdaf9064d"
          ],
          "title": "HTTP Alternative Services"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.1.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Although HTTP is independent of the transport protocol, the \"http\"",
            "   scheme associates authority with the ability to receive TCP",
            "   connections on the indicated port of whatever host is identified",
            "   within the authority component.  Because HTTP/3 does not use TCP,",
            "   HTTP/3 cannot be used for direct access to the authoritative server",
            "   for a resource identified by an \"http\" URI.  However, protocol",
            "   extensions such as [ALTSVC] permit the authoritative server to",
            "   identify other services that are also authoritative and that might be",
            "   reachable over HTTP/3.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dac660f5663d9ad9",
                  "1cbbe669c3ba2d63"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Prior to making requests for an origin whose scheme is not \"https\","
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dac660f5663d9ad9",
                  "1cbbe669c3ba2d63"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the client MUST ensure the server is willing to serve that scheme."
              }
            ],
            "   For origins whose scheme is \"http\", an experimental method to",
            "   accomplish this is described in [RFC8164].  Other mechanisms might be",
            "   defined for various schemes in the future."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1cbbe669c3ba2d63",
            "1cbbe669c3ba2d63"
          ],
          "title": "Other Schemes"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   HTTP/3 relies on QUIC version 1 as the underlying transport.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a874b2288112738",
                  "23b575586e5e0855"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "The use"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a874b2288112738",
                  "23b575586e5e0855"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "of other QUIC transport versions with HTTP/3 MAY be defined by future"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1a874b2288112738",
                  "23b575586e5e0855"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "specifications."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   QUIC version 1 uses TLS version 1.3 or greater as its handshake",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   protocol.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b0b43cffa07e1951",
                  "594fb71ec747d430"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HTTP/3 clients MUST support a mechanism to indicate the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b0b43cffa07e1951",
                  "594fb71ec747d430"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "target host to the server during the TLS handshake."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ed4f3e1c8051678",
                  "9bbfb0020a6f5e50"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the server is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ed4f3e1c8051678",
                  "9bbfb0020a6f5e50"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "identified by a domain name ([DNS-TERMS]), clients MUST send the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ed4f3e1c8051678",
                  "9bbfb0020a6f5e50"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Server Name Indication (SNI; [RFC6066]) TLS extension unless an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ed4f3e1c8051678",
                  "9bbfb0020a6f5e50"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "alternative mechanism to indicate the target host is used."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   QUIC connections are established as described in [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9722d4b6cd4d23c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "During connection establishment, HTTP/3 support is indicated by"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9722d4b6cd4d23c9"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "selecting the ALPN token \"h3\" in the TLS handshake.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9722d4b6cd4d23c9",
                  "bb7ec493b35315e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Support for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9722d4b6cd4d23c9",
                  "bb7ec493b35315e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "other application-layer protocols MAY be offered in the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9722d4b6cd4d23c9",
                  "bb7ec493b35315e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "handshake."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   While connection-level options pertaining to the core QUIC protocol",
            "   are set in the initial crypto handshake, settings specific to HTTP/3",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   are conveyed in the SETTINGS frame.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "36a7ba5d130866cb",
                  "36ade4f8d02da995",
                  "a802244752edaddf",
                  "d83a6d8d60117059"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "After the QUIC connection is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "36a7ba5d130866cb",
                  "36ade4f8d02da995",
                  "a802244752edaddf",
                  "d83a6d8d60117059"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "established, a SETTINGS frame MUST be sent by each endpoint as the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "36a7ba5d130866cb",
                  "36ade4f8d02da995",
                  "a802244752edaddf",
                  "d83a6d8d60117059"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "initial frame of their respective HTTP control stream."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "23b575586e5e0855",
            "23b575586e5e0855",
            "23b575586e5e0855",
            "594fb71ec747d430",
            "594fb71ec747d430",
            "9bbfb0020a6f5e50",
            "9bbfb0020a6f5e50",
            "9bbfb0020a6f5e50",
            "9bbfb0020a6f5e50",
            "bb7ec493b35315e6",
            "bb7ec493b35315e6",
            "bb7ec493b35315e6",
            "d83a6d8d60117059",
            "d83a6d8d60117059",
            "d83a6d8d60117059"
          ],
          "title": "Connection Establishment"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-3.3",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/3 connections are persistent across multiple requests.  For best",
            "   performance, it is expected that clients will not close connections",
            "   until it is determined that no further communication with a server is",
            "   necessary (for example, when a user navigates away from a particular",
            "   web page) or until the server closes the connection.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50b363d64d35f3cb",
                  "9609ed5de4037687"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Once a connection to a server endpoint exists, this connection MAY be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50b363d64d35f3cb",
                  "9609ed5de4037687"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "reused for requests with multiple different URI authority components."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67755f575792f798",
                  "13b8ba85bff7698c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "To use an existing connection for a new origin, clients MUST validate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67755f575792f798",
                  "13b8ba85bff7698c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the certificate presented by the server for the new origin server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "67755f575792f798",
                  "13b8ba85bff7698c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "using the process described in Section 4.3.4 of [HTTP]."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This implies"
              }
            ],
            "   that clients will need to retain the server certificate and any",
            "   additional information needed to verify that certificate; clients",
            "   that do not do so will be unable to reuse the connection for",
            "   additional origins.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c63c8996ac19e56",
                  "f5300f4e0aadf957"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the certificate is not acceptable with regard to the new origin"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c63c8996ac19e56",
                  "f5300f4e0aadf957"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "for any reason, the connection MUST NOT be reused and a new"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3c63c8996ac19e56",
                  "f5300f4e0aadf957"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "connection SHOULD be established for the new origin."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c5f1b7d4937246c",
                  "44c924b4a40190ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the reason"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c5f1b7d4937246c",
                  "44c924b4a40190ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the certificate cannot be verified might apply to other origins"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c5f1b7d4937246c",
                  "44c924b4a40190ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "already associated with the connection, the client SHOULD revalidate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c5f1b7d4937246c",
                  "44c924b4a40190ea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the server certificate for those origins."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  For instance, if"
              }
            ],
            "   validation of a certificate fails because the certificate has expired",
            "   or been revoked, this might be used to invalidate all other origins",
            "   for which that certificate was used to establish authority.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8916abea85d3039b",
                  "6e55d38ff737813e"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "Clients SHOULD NOT open more than one HTTP/3 connection to a given IP"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8916abea85d3039b",
                  "6e55d38ff737813e"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "address and UDP port, where the IP address and port might be derived"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8916abea85d3039b",
                  "6e55d38ff737813e"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "from a URI, a selected alternative service ([ALTSVC]), a configured"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8916abea85d3039b",
                  "6e55d38ff737813e"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "proxy, or name resolution of any of these."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc521c3f72fccb87",
                  "b3cc558f9172f182"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "A client MAY open"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc521c3f72fccb87",
                  "b3cc558f9172f182"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "multiple HTTP/3 connections to the same IP address and UDP port using"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc521c3f72fccb87",
                  "b3cc558f9172f182"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "different transport or TLS configurations but SHOULD avoid creating"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc521c3f72fccb87",
                  "b3cc558f9172f182"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "multiple connections with the same configuration."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Servers are encouraged to maintain open HTTP/3 connections for as",
            "   long as possible but are permitted to terminate idle connections if",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   necessary.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c608fa513980f3d6",
                  "b3a70630a72369a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "When either endpoint chooses to close the HTTP/3"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c608fa513980f3d6",
                  "b3a70630a72369a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "connection, the terminating endpoint SHOULD first send a GOAWAY frame"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c608fa513980f3d6",
                  "b3a70630a72369a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(Section 5.2) so that both endpoints can reliably determine whether"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c608fa513980f3d6",
                  "b3a70630a72369a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "previously sent frames have been processed and gracefully complete or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c608fa513980f3d6",
                  "b3a70630a72369a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "terminate any necessary remaining tasks."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A server that does not wish clients to reuse HTTP/3 connections for a",
            "   particular origin can indicate that it is not authoritative for a",
            "   request by sending a 421 (Misdirected Request) status code in",
            "   response to the request; see Section 7.4 of [HTTP]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "9609ed5de4037687",
            "9609ed5de4037687",
            "13b8ba85bff7698c",
            "13b8ba85bff7698c",
            "13b8ba85bff7698c",
            "f5300f4e0aadf957",
            "f5300f4e0aadf957",
            "f5300f4e0aadf957",
            "44c924b4a40190ea",
            "44c924b4a40190ea",
            "44c924b4a40190ea",
            "44c924b4a40190ea",
            "6e55d38ff737813e",
            "6e55d38ff737813e",
            "6e55d38ff737813e",
            "6e55d38ff737813e",
            "b3cc558f9172f182",
            "b3cc558f9172f182",
            "b3cc558f9172f182",
            "b3cc558f9172f182",
            "b3a70630a72369a1",
            "b3a70630a72369a1",
            "b3a70630a72369a1",
            "b3a70630a72369a1",
            "b3a70630a72369a1"
          ],
          "title": "Connection Reuse"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Expressing HTTP Semantics in HTTP/3"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   A client sends an HTTP request on a request stream, which is a",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   client-initiated bidirectional QUIC stream; see Section 6.1.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "A"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cb12f70787f05ff1",
                  "bdd4e5372c910a10"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "client MUST send only a single request on a given stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  A server"
              }
            ],
            "   sends zero or more interim HTTP responses on the same stream as the",
            "   request, followed by a single final HTTP response, as detailed below.",
            "   See Section 15 of [HTTP] for a description of interim and final HTTP",
            "   responses.",
            "",
            "   Pushed responses are sent on a server-initiated unidirectional QUIC",
            "   stream; see Section 6.2.2.  A server sends zero or more interim HTTP",
            "   responses, followed by a single final HTTP response, in the same",
            "   manner as a standard response.  Push is described in more detail in",
            "   Section 4.6.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c811c4e432c1061",
                  "243672a1a1a852e1"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "On a given stream, receipt of multiple requests or receipt of an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c811c4e432c1061",
                  "243672a1a1a852e1"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "additional HTTP response following a final HTTP response MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1c811c4e432c1061",
                  "243672a1a1a852e1"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "treated as malformed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   An HTTP message (request or response) consists of:",
            "",
            "   1.  the header section, including message control data, sent as a",
            "       single HEADERS frame,",
            "",
            "   2.  optionally, the content, if present, sent as a series of DATA",
            "       frames, and",
            "",
            "   3.  optionally, the trailer section, if present, sent as a single",
            "       HEADERS frame.",
            "",
            "   Header and trailer sections are described in Sections 6.3 and 6.5 of",
            "   [HTTP]; the content is described in Section 6.4 of [HTTP].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "105732f2a501910c",
                  "a39778e49e6f8aa9",
                  "306624ff47699005",
                  "d1f51608fc71ec38",
                  "72462b497145a408",
                  "672e1d7e7756e16a",
                  "18f6421b67326e57",
                  "9312ce862123c9f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Receipt of an invalid sequence of frames MUST be treated as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "105732f2a501910c",
                  "a39778e49e6f8aa9",
                  "306624ff47699005",
                  "d1f51608fc71ec38",
                  "72462b497145a408",
                  "672e1d7e7756e16a",
                  "18f6421b67326e57",
                  "9312ce862123c9f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  In particular, a DATA"
              }
            ],
            "   frame before any HEADERS frame, or a HEADERS or DATA frame after the",
            "   trailing HEADERS frame, is considered invalid.  Other frame types,",
            "   especially unknown frame types, might be permitted subject to their",
            "   own rules; see Section 9.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7f775c5bed91079",
                  "959c1fb65ab1ab22"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A server MAY send one or more PUSH_PROMISE frames before, after, or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b7f775c5bed91079",
                  "959c1fb65ab1ab22"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "interleaved with the frames of a response message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  These"
              }
            ],
            "   PUSH_PROMISE frames are not part of the response; see Section 4.6 for",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   more details.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e91783aefa3abe47",
                  "c598184fccb799a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "PUSH_PROMISE frames are not permitted on push streams;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e91783aefa3abe47",
                  "c598184fccb799a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "a pushed response that includes PUSH_PROMISE frames MUST be treated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e91783aefa3abe47",
                  "c598184fccb799a5"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "129731d03f8564af",
                  "197cd7f19098d184"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Frames of unknown types (Section 9), including reserved frames"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "129731d03f8564af",
                  "197cd7f19098d184"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "(Section 7.2.8) MAY be sent on a request or push stream before,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "129731d03f8564af",
                  "197cd7f19098d184"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "after, or interleaved with other frames described in this section."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The HEADERS and PUSH_PROMISE frames might reference updates to the",
            "   QPACK dynamic table.  While these updates are not directly part of",
            "   the message exchange, they must be received and processed before the",
            "   message can be consumed.  See Section 4.2 for more details.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e71ca63cef5bea63",
                  "0ebba0f6d59dc263"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Transfer codings (see Section 7 of [HTTP/1.1]) are not defined for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e71ca63cef5bea63",
                  "0ebba0f6d59dc263"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "HTTP/3; the Transfer-Encoding header field MUST NOT be used."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee1ec4cb47ec300d",
                  "c6f166d8d3e8e227"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A response MAY consist of multiple messages when and only when one or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee1ec4cb47ec300d",
                  "c6f166d8d3e8e227"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "more interim responses (1xx; see Section 15.2 of [HTTP]) precede a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee1ec4cb47ec300d",
                  "c6f166d8d3e8e227"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "final response to the same request."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Interim responses do not contain"
              }
            ],
            "   content or trailer sections.",
            "",
            "   An HTTP request/response exchange fully consumes a client-initiated",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   bidirectional QUIC stream.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "039237dc11ab56df",
                  "3bd013753d37014f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "After sending a request, a client MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "039237dc11ab56df",
                  "3bd013753d37014f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "close the stream for sending."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1891d709199d726d",
                  "931a1b4963a733c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Unless using the CONNECT method (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1891d709199d726d",
                  "931a1b4963a733c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Section 4.4), clients MUST NOT make stream closure dependent on"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1891d709199d726d",
                  "931a1b4963a733c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "receiving a response to their request."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a19dbda80c954ce",
                  "11b3f372f12df786"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "After sending a final"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a19dbda80c954ce",
                  "11b3f372f12df786"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "response, the server MUST close the stream for sending."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  At this"
              }
            ],
            "   point, the QUIC stream is fully closed.",
            "",
            "   When a stream is closed, this indicates the end of the final HTTP",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   message.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b3441c4371f4708",
                  "b2581a73d7789d74"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Because some messages are large or unbounded, endpoints"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b3441c4371f4708",
                  "b2581a73d7789d74"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "SHOULD begin processing partial HTTP messages once enough of the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b3441c4371f4708",
                  "b2581a73d7789d74"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "message has been received to make progress."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ef770b6d32df7df",
                  "9e6790b9ab9295bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If a client-initiated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ef770b6d32df7df",
                  "9e6790b9ab9295bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "stream terminates without enough of the HTTP message to provide a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ef770b6d32df7df",
                  "9e6790b9ab9295bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "complete response, the server SHOULD abort its response stream with"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9ef770b6d32df7df",
                  "9e6790b9ab9295bc"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the error code H3_REQUEST_INCOMPLETE."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A server can send a complete response prior to the client sending an",
            "   entire request if the response does not depend on any portion of the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   request that has not been sent and received.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f03ce1c48c6b506",
                  "b01c93918cdd8284"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "When the server does"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f03ce1c48c6b506",
                  "b01c93918cdd8284"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "not need to receive the remainder of the request, it MAY abort"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f03ce1c48c6b506",
                  "b01c93918cdd8284"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "reading the request stream, send a complete response, and cleanly"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f03ce1c48c6b506",
                  "b01c93918cdd8284"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "close the sending part of the stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f03ce1c48c6b506"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f03ce1c48c6b506",
                  "905af24366f31e49"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The error code H3_NO_ERROR"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f03ce1c48c6b506",
                  "905af24366f31e49"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "SHOULD be used when requesting that the client stop sending on the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f03ce1c48c6b506",
                  "905af24366f31e49"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "request stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abd168bdf347d103",
                  "0be3149683672a4c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT discard complete responses as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abd168bdf347d103",
                  "0be3149683672a4c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "result of having their request terminated abruptly, though clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "abd168bdf347d103",
                  "0be3149683672a4c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "can always discard responses at their discretion for other reasons."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "229cc781768e1add",
                  "96c811bcccc5f69f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If the server sends a partial or complete response but does not abort"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "229cc781768e1add",
                  "96c811bcccc5f69f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "reading the request, clients SHOULD continue sending the content of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "229cc781768e1add",
                  "96c811bcccc5f69f"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "the request and close the stream normally."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "bdd4e5372c910a10",
            "bdd4e5372c910a10",
            "243672a1a1a852e1",
            "243672a1a1a852e1",
            "243672a1a1a852e1",
            "9312ce862123c9f0",
            "9312ce862123c9f0",
            "959c1fb65ab1ab22",
            "959c1fb65ab1ab22",
            "c598184fccb799a5",
            "c598184fccb799a5",
            "c598184fccb799a5",
            "197cd7f19098d184",
            "197cd7f19098d184",
            "197cd7f19098d184",
            "0ebba0f6d59dc263",
            "0ebba0f6d59dc263",
            "c6f166d8d3e8e227",
            "c6f166d8d3e8e227",
            "c6f166d8d3e8e227",
            "3bd013753d37014f",
            "3bd013753d37014f",
            "931a1b4963a733c3",
            "931a1b4963a733c3",
            "931a1b4963a733c3",
            "11b3f372f12df786",
            "11b3f372f12df786",
            "b2581a73d7789d74",
            "b2581a73d7789d74",
            "b2581a73d7789d74",
            "9e6790b9ab9295bc",
            "9e6790b9ab9295bc",
            "9e6790b9ab9295bc",
            "9e6790b9ab9295bc",
            "b01c93918cdd8284",
            "b01c93918cdd8284",
            "b01c93918cdd8284",
            "b01c93918cdd8284",
            "905af24366f31e49",
            "905af24366f31e49",
            "905af24366f31e49",
            "0be3149683672a4c",
            "0be3149683672a4c",
            "0be3149683672a4c",
            "96c811bcccc5f69f",
            "96c811bcccc5f69f",
            "96c811bcccc5f69f"
          ],
          "title": "HTTP Message Framing"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.1",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d13852330d291f5",
                  "25d3e78e36ed698b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Once a request stream has been opened, the request MAY be cancelled"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d13852330d291f5",
                  "25d3e78e36ed698b"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "by either endpoint."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Clients cancel requests if the response is no"
              }
            ],
            "   longer of interest; servers cancel requests if they are unable to or",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   choose not to respond.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a4e0b9cd235406e",
                  "3f2bc185878995c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "When possible, it is RECOMMENDED that servers"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a4e0b9cd235406e",
                  "3f2bc185878995c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "send an HTTP response with an appropriate status code rather than"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a4e0b9cd235406e",
                  "3f2bc185878995c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "cancelling a request it has already begun processing."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "972e00ceedb47b89",
                  "c5f65f3a0123a693",
                  "f00070e37b2117bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Implementations SHOULD cancel requests by abruptly terminating any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "972e00ceedb47b89",
                  "c5f65f3a0123a693",
                  "f00070e37b2117bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "directions of a stream that are still open."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "972e00ceedb47b89",
                  "c5f65f3a0123a693"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "  To do so, an"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "972e00ceedb47b89",
                  "c5f65f3a0123a693"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "implementation resets the sending parts of streams and aborts reading"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "972e00ceedb47b89",
                  "c5f65f3a0123a693"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "on the receiving parts of streams; see Section 2.4 of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "972e00ceedb47b89",
                  "c5f65f3a0123a693"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "[QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09997605f7fee804"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "When the server cancels a request without performing any application"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09997605f7fee804"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "processing, the request is considered \"rejected\".  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09997605f7fee804",
                  "30b2e9c3c56d7673"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "The server SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09997605f7fee804",
                  "30b2e9c3c56d7673"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "abort its response stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_REJECTED."
              }
            ],
            "   In this context, \"processed\" means that some data from the stream was",
            "   passed to some higher layer of software that might have taken some",
            "   action as a result.  The client can treat requests rejected by the",
            "   server as though they had never been sent at all, thereby allowing",
            "   them to be retried later.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "444d262187815c5a",
                  "3bbf6106d16ec8f8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Servers MUST NOT use the H3_REQUEST_REJECTED error code for requests"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "444d262187815c5a",
                  "3bbf6106d16ec8f8"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "that were partially or fully processed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f74eed5caa4c207f",
                  "2a58cc21bab37356"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "When a server abandons a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f74eed5caa4c207f",
                  "2a58cc21bab37356"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "response after partial processing, it SHOULD abort its response"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f74eed5caa4c207f",
                  "2a58cc21bab37356"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "stream with the error code H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "773c8f59a2bf704f",
                  "02d2782c009ea56b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Client SHOULD use the error code H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED to cancel"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "773c8f59a2bf704f",
                  "02d2782c009ea56b"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "requests."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1089b9ac03a1a22",
                  "7c08634f5452864c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Upon receipt of this error code, a server MAY abruptly"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1089b9ac03a1a22",
                  "7c08634f5452864c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "terminate the response using the error code H3_REQUEST_REJECTED if no"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d1089b9ac03a1a22",
                  "7c08634f5452864c"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "processing was performed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c05f9bb66633d6f0",
                  "d78f5dc2973a2404"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT use the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c05f9bb66633d6f0",
                  "d78f5dc2973a2404"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "H3_REQUEST_REJECTED error code, except when a server has requested"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c05f9bb66633d6f0",
                  "d78f5dc2973a2404"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "closure of the request stream with this error code."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54e953d5f6214084",
                  "1a11a9450b0f6fd1"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "If a stream is cancelled after receiving a complete response, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54e953d5f6214084",
                  "1a11a9450b0f6fd1"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "client MAY ignore the cancellation and use the response."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21b61582afaa49b2",
                  "45e532ec5e0afa6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "However, if"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21b61582afaa49b2",
                  "45e532ec5e0afa6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "a stream is cancelled after receiving a partial response, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "21b61582afaa49b2",
                  "45e532ec5e0afa6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "response SHOULD NOT be used."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23e4ceced9ad2c50",
                  "9c1911dee0590fea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Only idempotent actions such as GET,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23e4ceced9ad2c50",
                  "9c1911dee0590fea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "PUT, or DELETE can be safely retried; a client SHOULD NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23e4ceced9ad2c50",
                  "9c1911dee0590fea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "automatically retry a request with a non-idempotent method unless it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23e4ceced9ad2c50",
                  "9c1911dee0590fea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "has some means to know that the request semantics are idempotent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23e4ceced9ad2c50",
                  "9c1911dee0590fea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "independent of the method or some means to detect that the original"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "23e4ceced9ad2c50",
                  "9c1911dee0590fea"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "request was never applied."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  See Section 9.2.2 of [HTTP] for more"
              }
            ],
            "   details."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "25d3e78e36ed698b",
            "25d3e78e36ed698b",
            "3f2bc185878995c4",
            "3f2bc185878995c4",
            "3f2bc185878995c4",
            "f00070e37b2117bf",
            "f00070e37b2117bf",
            "30b2e9c3c56d7673",
            "30b2e9c3c56d7673",
            "3bbf6106d16ec8f8",
            "3bbf6106d16ec8f8",
            "2a58cc21bab37356",
            "2a58cc21bab37356",
            "2a58cc21bab37356",
            "02d2782c009ea56b",
            "02d2782c009ea56b",
            "7c08634f5452864c",
            "7c08634f5452864c",
            "7c08634f5452864c",
            "d78f5dc2973a2404",
            "d78f5dc2973a2404",
            "d78f5dc2973a2404",
            "1a11a9450b0f6fd1",
            "1a11a9450b0f6fd1",
            "45e532ec5e0afa6b",
            "45e532ec5e0afa6b",
            "45e532ec5e0afa6b",
            "9c1911dee0590fea",
            "9c1911dee0590fea",
            "9c1911dee0590fea",
            "9c1911dee0590fea",
            "9c1911dee0590fea",
            "9c1911dee0590fea"
          ],
          "title": "Request Cancellation and Rejection"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.1.2",
          "lines": [
            "   A malformed request or response is one that is an otherwise valid",
            "   sequence of frames but is invalid due to:",
            "",
            "   *  the presence of prohibited fields or pseudo-header fields,",
            "",
            "   *  the absence of mandatory pseudo-header fields,",
            "",
            "   *  invalid values for pseudo-header fields,",
            "",
            "   *  pseudo-header fields after fields,",
            "",
            "   *  an invalid sequence of HTTP messages,",
            "",
            "   *  the inclusion of uppercase field names, or",
            "",
            "   *  the inclusion of invalid characters in field names or values.",
            "",
            "   A request or response that is defined as having content when it",
            "   contains a Content-Length header field (Section 8.6 of [HTTP]) is",
            "   malformed if the value of the Content-Length header field does not",
            "   equal the sum of the DATA frame lengths received.  A response that is",
            "   defined as never having content, even when a Content-Length is",
            "   present, can have a non-zero Content-Length header field even though",
            "   no content is included in DATA frames.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c6514c2cf7d76f34",
                  "a47d73f6439ca20d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Intermediaries that process HTTP requests or responses (i.e., any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c6514c2cf7d76f34",
                  "a47d73f6439ca20d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "intermediary not acting as a tunnel) MUST NOT forward a malformed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c6514c2cf7d76f34",
                  "a47d73f6439ca20d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "request or response."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9d77203ea5c22b11",
                  "783d43089342d53f",
                  "cf06c9475a6228c0",
                  "45d8732afb217228"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "Malformed requests or responses that are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9d77203ea5c22b11",
                  "783d43089342d53f",
                  "cf06c9475a6228c0",
                  "45d8732afb217228"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "detected MUST be treated as a stream error of type H3_MESSAGE_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "07d77cb2772190fb",
                  "f4090f231fc43317"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "For malformed requests, a server MAY send an HTTP response indicating"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "07d77cb2772190fb",
                  "f4090f231fc43317"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "the error prior to closing or resetting the stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae45c1ef790dbcb4",
                  "6e5624f0ba898279"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Clients MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ae45c1ef790dbcb4",
                  "6e5624f0ba898279"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "accept a malformed response."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Note that these requirements are"
              }
            ],
            "   intended to protect against several types of common attacks against",
            "   HTTP; they are deliberately strict because being permissive can",
            "   expose implementations to these vulnerabilities."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "a47d73f6439ca20d",
            "a47d73f6439ca20d",
            "a47d73f6439ca20d",
            "45d8732afb217228",
            "45d8732afb217228",
            "f4090f231fc43317",
            "f4090f231fc43317",
            "6e5624f0ba898279",
            "6e5624f0ba898279"
          ],
          "title": "Malformed Requests and Responses"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP messages carry metadata as a series of key-value pairs called",
            "   \"HTTP fields\"; see Sections 6.3 and 6.5 of [HTTP].  For a listing of",
            "   registered HTTP fields, see the \"Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP)",
            "   Field Name Registry\" maintained at <https://www.iana.org/assignments/",
            "   http-fields/>.  Like HTTP/2, HTTP/3 has additional considerations",
            "   related to the use of characters in field names, the Connection",
            "   header field, and pseudo-header fields.",
            "",
            "   Field names are strings containing a subset of ASCII characters.",
            "   Properties of HTTP field names and values are discussed in more",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   detail in Section 5.1 of [HTTP].  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "143c974b69c022c9",
                  "a96942e4936082a5",
                  "f73c6c385c95906f"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Characters in field names MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "143c974b69c022c9",
                  "a96942e4936082a5",
                  "f73c6c385c95906f"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "converted to lowercase prior to their encoding."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b729b3509f09344",
                  "7b354958868c096b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "A request or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b729b3509f09344",
                  "7b354958868c096b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "response containing uppercase characters in field names MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9b729b3509f09344",
                  "7b354958868c096b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "treated as malformed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   HTTP/3 does not use the Connection header field to indicate",
            "   connection-specific fields; in this protocol, connection-specific",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   metadata is conveyed by other means.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2b738c956851a80",
                  "e1305508ecd287a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "An endpoint MUST NOT generate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2b738c956851a80",
                  "e1305508ecd287a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "an HTTP/3 field section containing connection-specific fields; any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2b738c956851a80",
                  "e1305508ecd287a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "message containing connection-specific fields MUST be treated as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f2b738c956851a80",
                  "e1305508ecd287a6"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "malformed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "782ff75662e89bdb",
                  "f86026918614c17e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The only exception to this is the TE header field, which MAY be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "782ff75662e89bdb",
                  "f86026918614c17e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "present in an HTTP/3 request header; when it is, it MUST NOT contain"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "782ff75662e89bdb",
                  "f86026918614c17e"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "any value other than \"trailers\"."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "038f9728e5720649",
                  "b7ac758053f3afc6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "An intermediary transforming an HTTP/1.x message to HTTP/3 MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "038f9728e5720649",
                  "b7ac758053f3afc6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "remove connection-specific header fields as discussed in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "038f9728e5720649",
                  "b7ac758053f3afc6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Section 7.6.1 of [HTTP], or their messages will be treated by other"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "038f9728e5720649",
                  "b7ac758053f3afc6"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HTTP/3 endpoints as malformed."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f73c6c385c95906f",
            "f73c6c385c95906f",
            "7b354958868c096b",
            "7b354958868c096b",
            "7b354958868c096b",
            "e1305508ecd287a6",
            "e1305508ecd287a6",
            "e1305508ecd287a6",
            "e1305508ecd287a6",
            "f86026918614c17e",
            "f86026918614c17e",
            "f86026918614c17e",
            "b7ac758053f3afc6",
            "b7ac758053f3afc6",
            "b7ac758053f3afc6",
            "b7ac758053f3afc6"
          ],
          "title": "HTTP Fields"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   [QPACK] describes a variation of HPACK that gives an encoder some",
            "   control over how much head-of-line blocking can be caused by",
            "   compression.  This allows an encoder to balance compression",
            "   efficiency with latency.  HTTP/3 uses QPACK to compress header and",
            "   trailer sections, including the control data present in the header",
            "   section.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1ed478530bea41e7",
                  "81108cd4c584f78c"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "To allow for better compression efficiency, the Cookie header field"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1ed478530bea41e7",
                  "81108cd4c584f78c"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "([COOKIES]) MAY be split into separate field lines, each with one or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1ed478530bea41e7",
                  "81108cd4c584f78c"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "more cookie-pairs, before compression."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef28ae30620cc27d",
                  "b656c7fab3c4f044"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If a decompressed field"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef28ae30620cc27d",
                  "b656c7fab3c4f044"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "section contains multiple cookie field lines, these MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef28ae30620cc27d",
                  "b656c7fab3c4f044"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "concatenated into a single byte string using the two-byte delimiter"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef28ae30620cc27d",
                  "b656c7fab3c4f044"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "of \"; \" (ASCII 0x3b, 0x20) before being passed into a context other"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef28ae30620cc27d",
                  "b656c7fab3c4f044"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "than HTTP/2 or HTTP/3, such as an HTTP/1.1 connection, or a generic"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef28ae30620cc27d",
                  "b656c7fab3c4f044"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "HTTP server application."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "81108cd4c584f78c",
            "81108cd4c584f78c",
            "81108cd4c584f78c",
            "b656c7fab3c4f044",
            "b656c7fab3c4f044",
            "b656c7fab3c4f044",
            "b656c7fab3c4f044",
            "b656c7fab3c4f044",
            "b656c7fab3c4f044"
          ],
          "title": "Field Compression"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.2.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c45568e99e5e40d",
                  "140c8ea9449ead60",
                  "210ac9f69a6c2a71",
                  "909829cd8705162b",
                  "113dbeee5ecff698",
                  "8577519434330a1c",
                  "1f160585e275be6f"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "An HTTP/3 implementation MAY impose a limit on the maximum size of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8c45568e99e5e40d",
                  "140c8ea9449ead60",
                  "210ac9f69a6c2a71",
                  "909829cd8705162b",
                  "113dbeee5ecff698",
                  "8577519434330a1c",
                  "1f160585e275be6f"
                ],
                "status_id": 14,
                "text": "the message header it will accept on an individual HTTP message."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  A"
              }
            ],
            "   server that receives a larger header section than it is willing to",
            "   handle can send an HTTP 431 (Request Header Fields Too Large) status",
            "   code ([RFC6585]).  A client can discard responses that it cannot",
            "   process.  The size of a field list is calculated based on the",
            "   uncompressed size of fields, including the length of the name and",
            "   value in bytes plus an overhead of 32 bytes for each field.",
            "",
            "   If an implementation wishes to advise its peer of this limit, it can",
            "   be conveyed as a number of bytes in the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   SETTINGS_MAX_FIELD_SECTION_SIZE parameter.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aac35d0072a33069",
                  "98a2c8732b1b674b",
                  "e13088c54983c40d",
                  "58a9b1409e277019",
                  "aec4134015590c54",
                  "3a42d14f151b2efb",
                  "8bcd6518a41f034c",
                  "5f45b81e80200f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "An implementation that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aac35d0072a33069",
                  "98a2c8732b1b674b",
                  "e13088c54983c40d",
                  "58a9b1409e277019",
                  "aec4134015590c54",
                  "3a42d14f151b2efb",
                  "8bcd6518a41f034c",
                  "5f45b81e80200f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "has received this parameter SHOULD NOT send an HTTP message header"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aac35d0072a33069",
                  "98a2c8732b1b674b",
                  "e13088c54983c40d",
                  "58a9b1409e277019",
                  "aec4134015590c54",
                  "3a42d14f151b2efb",
                  "8bcd6518a41f034c",
                  "5f45b81e80200f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "that exceeds the indicated size, as the peer will likely refuse to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aac35d0072a33069",
                  "98a2c8732b1b674b",
                  "e13088c54983c40d",
                  "58a9b1409e277019",
                  "aec4134015590c54",
                  "3a42d14f151b2efb",
                  "8bcd6518a41f034c",
                  "5f45b81e80200f23"
                ],
                "status_id": 15,
                "text": "process it."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  However, an HTTP message can traverse one or more"
              }
            ],
            "   intermediaries before reaching the origin server; see Section 3.7 of",
            "   [HTTP].  Because this limit is applied separately by each",
            "   implementation that processes the message, messages below this limit",
            "   are not guaranteed to be accepted."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "1f160585e275be6f",
            "1f160585e275be6f",
            "5f45b81e80200f23",
            "5f45b81e80200f23",
            "5f45b81e80200f23",
            "5f45b81e80200f23"
          ],
          "title": "Header Size Constraints"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3",
          "lines": [
            "   Like HTTP/2, HTTP/3 employs a series of pseudo-header fields, where",
            "   the field name begins with the : character (ASCII 0x3a).  These",
            "   pseudo-header fields convey message control data; see Section 6.2 of",
            "   [HTTP].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   Pseudo-header fields are not HTTP fields.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "898bd589152bc2f7",
                  "30f2de88dab0e604"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "898bd589152bc2f7",
                  "30f2de88dab0e604"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "generate pseudo-header fields other than those defined in this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "898bd589152bc2f7",
                  "30f2de88dab0e604"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "document."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  However, an extension could negotiate a modification of"
              }
            ],
            "   this restriction; see Section 9.",
            "",
            "   Pseudo-header fields are only valid in the context in which they are",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   defined.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d234484c8cf6049f",
                  "53c778fe586c0116",
                  "b7660f78996da429"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Pseudo-header fields defined for requests MUST NOT appear"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d234484c8cf6049f",
                  "53c778fe586c0116",
                  "b7660f78996da429"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "in responses; pseudo-header fields defined for responses MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d234484c8cf6049f",
                  "53c778fe586c0116",
                  "b7660f78996da429"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "appear in requests."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c8e60f567f9df812",
                  "7657964fb6c4e5ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Pseudo-header fields MUST NOT appear in trailer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c8e60f567f9df812",
                  "7657964fb6c4e5ee"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "sections."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e11dc69b20d7ff73",
                  "9e4476dc3f6f6bde"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST treat a request or response that contains"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e11dc69b20d7ff73",
                  "9e4476dc3f6f6bde"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "undefined or invalid pseudo-header fields as malformed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c74c9c50205d3303",
                  "d308d2ad102394d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "All pseudo-header fields MUST appear in the header section before"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c74c9c50205d3303",
                  "d308d2ad102394d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "regular header fields."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99f249dcc9984c19",
                  "c6a9bec131c3a693"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Any request or response that contains a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99f249dcc9984c19",
                  "c6a9bec131c3a693"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "pseudo-header field that appears in a header section after a regular"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "99f249dcc9984c19",
                  "c6a9bec131c3a693"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "header field MUST be treated as malformed."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "30f2de88dab0e604",
            "30f2de88dab0e604",
            "30f2de88dab0e604",
            "b7660f78996da429",
            "b7660f78996da429",
            "b7660f78996da429",
            "7657964fb6c4e5ee",
            "7657964fb6c4e5ee",
            "9e4476dc3f6f6bde",
            "9e4476dc3f6f6bde",
            "d308d2ad102394d9",
            "d308d2ad102394d9",
            "c6a9bec131c3a693",
            "c6a9bec131c3a693",
            "c6a9bec131c3a693"
          ],
          "title": "HTTP Control Data"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The following pseudo-header fields are defined for requests:",
            "",
            "   \":method\":  Contains the HTTP method (Section 9 of [HTTP])",
            "",
            "   \":scheme\":  Contains the scheme portion of the target URI",
            "      (Section 3.1 of [URI]).",
            "",
            "      The :scheme pseudo-header is not restricted to URIs with scheme",
            "      \"http\" and \"https\".  A proxy or gateway can translate requests for",
            "      non-HTTP schemes, enabling the use of HTTP to interact with non-",
            "      HTTP services.",
            "",
            "      See Section 3.1.2 for guidance on using a scheme other than",
            "      \"https\".",
            "",
            "   \":authority\":  Contains the authority portion of the target URI",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      (Section 3.2 of [URI]).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e89001de40cdf7de",
                  "71e843de46315c6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The authority MUST NOT include the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e89001de40cdf7de",
                  "71e843de46315c6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "deprecated userinfo subcomponent for URIs of scheme \"http\" or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e89001de40cdf7de",
                  "71e843de46315c6b"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "\"https\"."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "994569ba9197e917",
                  "a2e749ca67995c2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "To ensure that the HTTP/1.1 request line can be reproduced"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "994569ba9197e917",
                  "a2e749ca67995c2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "accurately, this pseudo-header field MUST be omitted when"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "994569ba9197e917",
                  "a2e749ca67995c2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "translating from an HTTP/1.1 request that has a request target in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "994569ba9197e917",
                  "a2e749ca67995c2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "a method-specific form; see Section 7.1 of [HTTP]."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa64821aefbf0478",
                  "0e5b98975d85b1fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Clients that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa64821aefbf0478",
                  "0e5b98975d85b1fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "generate HTTP/3 requests directly SHOULD use the :authority"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "aa64821aefbf0478",
                  "0e5b98975d85b1fa"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "pseudo-header field instead of the Host header field."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "264f7037765bda63",
                  "9c50b5c78993039f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "An"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "264f7037765bda63",
                  "9c50b5c78993039f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "intermediary that converts an HTTP/3 request to HTTP/1.1 MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "264f7037765bda63",
                  "9c50b5c78993039f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "create a Host field if one is not present in a request by copying"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "264f7037765bda63",
                  "9c50b5c78993039f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "the value of the :authority pseudo-header field."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   \":path\":  Contains the path and query parts of the target URI (the",
            "      \"path-absolute\" production and optionally a ? character (ASCII",
            "      0x3f) followed by the \"query\" production; see Sections 3.3 and 3.4",
            "      of [URI].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6242ec1559958390",
                  "7c7b5c747d9f4366"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "This pseudo-header field MUST NOT be empty for \"http\" or \"https\""
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6242ec1559958390",
                  "7c7b5c747d9f4366"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "URIs; \"http\" or \"https\" URIs that do not contain a path component"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6242ec1559958390",
                  "7c7b5c747d9f4366"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "MUST include a value of / (ASCII 0x2f)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  An OPTIONS request that"
              }
            ],
            "      does not include a path component includes the value * (ASCII",
            "      0x2a) for the :path pseudo-header field; see Section 7.1 of",
            "      [HTTP].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d126729cd4603ac",
                  "a06510c05ad3949e"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "All HTTP/3 requests MUST include exactly one value for the :method,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d126729cd4603ac",
                  "a06510c05ad3949e"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": ":scheme, and :path pseudo-header fields, unless the request is a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8d126729cd4603ac",
                  "a06510c05ad3949e"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "CONNECT request; see Section 4.4."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de1750e4714dc753",
                  "ab4a7ffa8e703ed9",
                  "1ca7c4223fb0b61b",
                  "ca7a02aa78fb62f5",
                  "5945c2613a18a727"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the :scheme pseudo-header field identifies a scheme that has a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de1750e4714dc753",
                  "ab4a7ffa8e703ed9",
                  "1ca7c4223fb0b61b",
                  "ca7a02aa78fb62f5",
                  "5945c2613a18a727"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "mandatory authority component (including \"http\" and \"https\"), the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de1750e4714dc753",
                  "ab4a7ffa8e703ed9",
                  "1ca7c4223fb0b61b",
                  "ca7a02aa78fb62f5",
                  "5945c2613a18a727"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "request MUST contain either an :authority pseudo-header field or a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "de1750e4714dc753",
                  "ab4a7ffa8e703ed9",
                  "1ca7c4223fb0b61b",
                  "ca7a02aa78fb62f5",
                  "5945c2613a18a727"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Host header field."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5d1ce05ea29a1ef",
                  "9b907e03506d4946",
                  "374c24af7b19c80c",
                  "d575b4688d74572b",
                  "a0aa459c036f241b"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If these fields are present, they MUST NOT be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c5d1ce05ea29a1ef",
                  "9b907e03506d4946",
                  "374c24af7b19c80c",
                  "d575b4688d74572b",
                  "a0aa459c036f241b"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "empty."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5622b67f51e8cb9f",
                  "02e1ba6383ea3d38",
                  "0c6b181ed519bbd2",
                  "99cc61f43adc2975"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If both fields are present, they MUST contain the same value."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cecde5ca5a5abd79",
                  "cc8a88128bf701af"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If the scheme does not have a mandatory authority component and none"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cecde5ca5a5abd79",
                  "cc8a88128bf701af"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "is provided in the request target, the request MUST NOT contain the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cecde5ca5a5abd79",
                  "cc8a88128bf701af"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": ":authority pseudo-header or Host header fields."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   An HTTP request that omits mandatory pseudo-header fields or contains",
            "   invalid values for those pseudo-header fields is malformed.",
            "",
            "   HTTP/3 does not define a way to carry the version identifier that is",
            "   included in the HTTP/1.1 request line.  HTTP/3 requests implicitly",
            "   have a protocol version of \"3.0\"."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "71e843de46315c6b",
            "71e843de46315c6b",
            "71e843de46315c6b",
            "a2e749ca67995c2e",
            "a2e749ca67995c2e",
            "a2e749ca67995c2e",
            "a2e749ca67995c2e",
            "0e5b98975d85b1fa",
            "0e5b98975d85b1fa",
            "0e5b98975d85b1fa",
            "9c50b5c78993039f",
            "9c50b5c78993039f",
            "9c50b5c78993039f",
            "9c50b5c78993039f",
            "7c7b5c747d9f4366",
            "7c7b5c747d9f4366",
            "7c7b5c747d9f4366",
            "a06510c05ad3949e",
            "a06510c05ad3949e",
            "a06510c05ad3949e",
            "5945c2613a18a727",
            "5945c2613a18a727",
            "5945c2613a18a727",
            "5945c2613a18a727",
            "a0aa459c036f241b",
            "a0aa459c036f241b",
            "99cc61f43adc2975",
            "cc8a88128bf701af",
            "cc8a88128bf701af",
            "cc8a88128bf701af"
          ],
          "title": "Request Pseudo-Header Fields"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.3.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e6abb03fd1b9995"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "For responses, a single \":status\" pseudo-header field is defined that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e6abb03fd1b9995"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "carries the HTTP status code; see Section 15 of [HTTP].  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e6abb03fd1b9995",
                  "4a9d0778f4b32d32"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "This pseudo-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e6abb03fd1b9995",
                  "4a9d0778f4b32d32"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "header field MUST be included in all responses; otherwise, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5e6abb03fd1b9995",
                  "4a9d0778f4b32d32"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "response is malformed (see Section 4.1.2)."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   HTTP/3 does not define a way to carry the version or reason phrase",
            "   that is included in an HTTP/1.1 status line.  HTTP/3 responses",
            "   implicitly have a protocol version of \"3.0\"."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4a9d0778f4b32d32",
            "4a9d0778f4b32d32",
            "4a9d0778f4b32d32"
          ],
          "title": "Response Pseudo-Header Fields"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.4",
          "lines": [
            "   The CONNECT method requests that the recipient establish a tunnel to",
            "   the destination origin server identified by the request-target; see",
            "   Section 9.3.6 of [HTTP].  It is primarily used with HTTP proxies to",
            "   establish a TLS session with an origin server for the purposes of",
            "   interacting with \"https\" resources.",
            "",
            "   In HTTP/1.x, CONNECT is used to convert an entire HTTP connection",
            "   into a tunnel to a remote host.  In HTTP/2 and HTTP/3, the CONNECT",
            "   method is used to establish a tunnel over a single stream.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66d8ef675b611bea",
                  "c382a6578e58d953"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A CONNECT request MUST be constructed as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66d8ef675b611bea"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "*  The :method pseudo-header field is set to \"CONNECT\""
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66d8ef675b611bea"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "*  The :scheme and :path pseudo-header fields are omitted"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66d8ef675b611bea"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "*  The :authority pseudo-header field contains the host and port to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66d8ef675b611bea"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "connect to (equivalent to the authority-form of the request-target"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "66d8ef675b611bea"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "of CONNECT requests; see Section 7.1 of [HTTP])."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The request stream remains open at the end of the request to carry",
            "   the data to be transferred.  A CONNECT request that does not conform",
            "   to these restrictions is malformed.",
            "",
            "   A proxy that supports CONNECT establishes a TCP connection",
            "   ([RFC0793]) to the server identified in the :authority pseudo-header",
            "   field.  Once this connection is successfully established, the proxy",
            "   sends a HEADERS frame containing a 2xx series status code to the",
            "   client, as defined in Section 15.3 of [HTTP].",
            "",
            "   All DATA frames on the stream correspond to data sent or received on",
            "   the TCP connection.  The payload of any DATA frame sent by the client",
            "   is transmitted by the proxy to the TCP server; data received from the",
            "   TCP server is packaged into DATA frames by the proxy.  Note that the",
            "   size and number of TCP segments is not guaranteed to map predictably",
            "   to the size and number of HTTP DATA or QUIC STREAM frames.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f5206c085faae96"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Once the CONNECT method has completed, only DATA frames are permitted"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f5206c085faae96"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "to be sent on the stream.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f5206c085faae96",
                  "d339a8ff6854278a"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Extension frames MAY be used if"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8f5206c085faae96",
                  "d339a8ff6854278a"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "specifically permitted by the definition of the extension."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "efdcd18798ec2b85",
                  "1bad7beeb08c4e8c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Receipt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "efdcd18798ec2b85",
                  "1bad7beeb08c4e8c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "of any other known frame type MUST be treated as a connection error"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "efdcd18798ec2b85",
                  "1bad7beeb08c4e8c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The TCP connection can be closed by either peer.  When the client",
            "   ends the request stream (that is, the receive stream at the proxy",
            "   enters the \"Data Recvd\" state), the proxy will set the FIN bit on its",
            "   connection to the TCP server.  When the proxy receives a packet with",
            "   the FIN bit set, it will close the send stream that it sends to the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   client.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d5ab129b252cd77",
                  "dbdb7a28fe6b5d97",
                  "50f3b7149ecc4744"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "TCP connections that remain half closed in a single"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d5ab129b252cd77",
                  "dbdb7a28fe6b5d97",
                  "50f3b7149ecc4744"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "direction are not invalid, but are often handled poorly by servers,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d5ab129b252cd77",
                  "dbdb7a28fe6b5d97",
                  "50f3b7149ecc4744"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "so clients SHOULD NOT close a stream for sending while they still"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d5ab129b252cd77",
                  "dbdb7a28fe6b5d97",
                  "50f3b7149ecc4744"
                ],
                "status_id": 18,
                "text": "expect to receive data from the target of the CONNECT."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A TCP connection error is signaled by abruptly terminating the",
            "   stream.  A proxy treats any error in the TCP connection, which",
            "   includes receiving a TCP segment with the RST bit set, as a stream",
            "   error of type H3_CONNECT_ERROR.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "303fcbfb4ce5cbfe",
                  "d1a7d45e72284b37"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Correspondingly, if a proxy detects an error with the stream or the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "303fcbfb4ce5cbfe",
                  "d1a7d45e72284b37"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "QUIC connection, it MUST close the TCP connection."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e024cbb81716d1f7",
                  "e5dbb9a0a122f725"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If the proxy"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e024cbb81716d1f7",
                  "e5dbb9a0a122f725"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "detects that the client has reset the stream or aborted reading from"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e024cbb81716d1f7",
                  "e5dbb9a0a122f725"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "the stream, it MUST close the TCP connection."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b73150c4a626288",
                  "f261ef65c7e50d5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "If the stream is reset"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b73150c4a626288",
                  "f261ef65c7e50d5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "or reading is aborted by the client, a proxy SHOULD perform the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b73150c4a626288",
                  "f261ef65c7e50d5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "operation on the other direction in order to ensure that both"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0b73150c4a626288",
                  "f261ef65c7e50d5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "directions of the stream are cancelled."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0cd6d9763d340643",
                  "98a763004456cdd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "In all these cases, if the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0cd6d9763d340643",
                  "98a763004456cdd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "underlying TCP implementation permits it, the proxy SHOULD send a TCP"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0cd6d9763d340643",
                  "98a763004456cdd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "segment with the RST bit set."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c08f2e7f14e8c95d",
                  "84dbeba805fcd43b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Since CONNECT creates a tunnel to an arbitrary server, proxies that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c08f2e7f14e8c95d",
                  "84dbeba805fcd43b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "support CONNECT SHOULD restrict its use to a set of known ports or a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c08f2e7f14e8c95d",
                  "84dbeba805fcd43b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "list of safe request targets; see Section 9.3.6 of [HTTP] for more"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c08f2e7f14e8c95d",
                  "84dbeba805fcd43b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "details."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "c382a6578e58d953",
            "d339a8ff6854278a",
            "d339a8ff6854278a",
            "1bad7beeb08c4e8c",
            "1bad7beeb08c4e8c",
            "1bad7beeb08c4e8c",
            "50f3b7149ecc4744",
            "50f3b7149ecc4744",
            "50f3b7149ecc4744",
            "50f3b7149ecc4744",
            "d1a7d45e72284b37",
            "d1a7d45e72284b37",
            "e5dbb9a0a122f725",
            "e5dbb9a0a122f725",
            "e5dbb9a0a122f725",
            "f261ef65c7e50d5e",
            "f261ef65c7e50d5e",
            "f261ef65c7e50d5e",
            "f261ef65c7e50d5e",
            "98a763004456cdd4",
            "98a763004456cdd4",
            "98a763004456cdd4",
            "84dbeba805fcd43b",
            "84dbeba805fcd43b",
            "84dbeba805fcd43b",
            "84dbeba805fcd43b"
          ],
          "title": "The CONNECT Method"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.5",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/3 does not support the HTTP Upgrade mechanism (Section 7.8 of",
            "   [HTTP]) or the 101 (Switching Protocols) informational status code",
            "   (Section 15.2.2 of [HTTP])."
          ],
          "title": "HTTP Upgrade"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-4.6",
          "lines": [
            "   Server push is an interaction mode that permits a server to push a",
            "   request-response exchange to a client in anticipation of the client",
            "   making the indicated request.  This trades off network usage against",
            "   a potential latency gain.  HTTP/3 server push is similar to what is",
            "   described in Section 8.2 of [HTTP/2], but it uses different",
            "   mechanisms.",
            "",
            "   Each server push is assigned a unique push ID by the server.  The",
            "   push ID is used to refer to the push in various contexts throughout",
            "   the lifetime of the HTTP/3 connection.",
            "",
            "   The push ID space begins at zero and ends at a maximum value set by",
            "   the MAX_PUSH_ID frame.  In particular, a server is not able to push",
            "   until after the client sends a MAX_PUSH_ID frame.  A client sends",
            "   MAX_PUSH_ID frames to control the number of pushes that a server can",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   promise.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4aea915772f9467c",
                  "3915aa352e28b6f6"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "A server SHOULD use push IDs sequentially, beginning from"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4aea915772f9467c",
                  "3915aa352e28b6f6"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "zero."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f8c923fddd55fae",
                  "6fa3cba172cfcd91"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A client MUST treat receipt of a push stream as a connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f8c923fddd55fae",
                  "6fa3cba172cfcd91"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "error of type H3_ID_ERROR when no MAX_PUSH_ID frame has been sent or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f8c923fddd55fae",
                  "6fa3cba172cfcd91"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "when the stream references a push ID that is greater than the maximum"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3f8c923fddd55fae",
                  "6fa3cba172cfcd91"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "push ID."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The push ID is used in one or more PUSH_PROMISE frames that carry the",
            "   control data and header fields of the request message.  These frames",
            "   are sent on the request stream that generated the push.  This allows",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   the server push to be associated with a client request.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86b1c83651993d81",
                  "8f171b2462f982d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "When the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86b1c83651993d81",
                  "8f171b2462f982d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "same push ID is promised on multiple request streams, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86b1c83651993d81",
                  "8f171b2462f982d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "decompressed request field sections MUST contain the same fields in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86b1c83651993d81",
                  "8f171b2462f982d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "the same order, and both the name and the value in each field MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86b1c83651993d81",
                  "8f171b2462f982d9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "identical."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The push ID is then included with the push stream that ultimately",
            "   fulfills those promises.  The push stream identifies the push ID of",
            "   the promise that it fulfills, then contains a response to the",
            "   promised request as described in Section 4.1.",
            "",
            "   Finally, the push ID can be used in CANCEL_PUSH frames; see",
            "   Section 7.2.3.  Clients use this frame to indicate they do not wish",
            "   to receive a promised resource.  Servers use this frame to indicate",
            "   they will not be fulfilling a previous promise.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f02554c204c37449"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Not all requests can be pushed.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f02554c204c37449",
                  "a0f4588830b09416"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A server MAY push requests that have"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f02554c204c37449",
                  "a0f4588830b09416"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "the following properties:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f02554c204c37449"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "*  cacheable; see Section 9.2.3 of [HTTP]"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f02554c204c37449"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "*  safe; see Section 9.2.1 of [HTTP]"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f02554c204c37449"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "*  does not include request content or a trailer section"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "720172d9f8579ac6",
                  "8a1daf82c968aff2"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The server MUST include a value in the :authority pseudo-header field"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "720172d9f8579ac6",
                  "8a1daf82c968aff2"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "for which the server is authoritative."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9545dd682d896865",
                  "1dd090f4f97d5522"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If the client has not yet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9545dd682d896865",
                  "1dd090f4f97d5522"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "validated the connection for the origin indicated by the pushed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9545dd682d896865",
                  "1dd090f4f97d5522"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "request, it MUST perform the same verification process it would do"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9545dd682d896865",
                  "1dd090f4f97d5522"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "before sending a request for that origin on the connection; see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9545dd682d896865",
                  "1dd090f4f97d5522"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Section 3.3."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bfbb874977e1978",
                  "e23ff005728bc4e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If this verification fails, the client MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9bfbb874977e1978",
                  "e23ff005728bc4e3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "consider the server authoritative for that origin."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ced3057b9411537b",
                  "8dc17250b246db1c"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Clients SHOULD send a CANCEL_PUSH frame upon receipt of a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ced3057b9411537b",
                  "8dc17250b246db1c"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "PUSH_PROMISE frame carrying a request that is not cacheable, is not"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ced3057b9411537b",
                  "8dc17250b246db1c"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "known to be safe, that indicates the presence of request content, or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ced3057b9411537b",
                  "8dc17250b246db1c"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "for which it does not consider the server authoritative."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ced3057b9411537b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ced3057b9411537b",
                  "dc64f94bbee6efda"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ced3057b9411537b",
                  "dc64f94bbee6efda"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "corresponding responses MUST NOT be used or cached."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Each pushed response is associated with one or more client requests.",
            "   The push is associated with the request stream on which the",
            "   PUSH_PROMISE frame was received.  The same server push can be",
            "   associated with additional client requests using a PUSH_PROMISE frame",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   with the same push ID on multiple request streams.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd90c5bd74959934",
                  "7db5bc9707bd2c6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "These"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd90c5bd74959934",
                  "7db5bc9707bd2c6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "associations do not affect the operation of the protocol, but they"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd90c5bd74959934",
                  "7db5bc9707bd2c6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "MAY be considered by user agents when deciding how to use pushed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bd90c5bd74959934",
                  "7db5bc9707bd2c6e"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "resources."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Ordering of a PUSH_PROMISE frame in relation to certain parts of the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   response is important.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "358a46b22aeff46b",
                  "af8f0f31c7b03064"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "The server SHOULD send PUSH_PROMISE frames"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "358a46b22aeff46b",
                  "af8f0f31c7b03064"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "prior to sending HEADERS or DATA frames that reference the promised"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "358a46b22aeff46b",
                  "af8f0f31c7b03064"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "responses."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "358a46b22aeff46b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "  This reduces the chance that a client requests a resource"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "358a46b22aeff46b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "that will be pushed by the server."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Due to reordering, push stream data can arrive before the",
            "   corresponding PUSH_PROMISE frame.  When a client receives a new push",
            "   stream with an as-yet-unknown push ID, both the associated client",
            "   request and the pushed request header fields are unknown.  The client",
            "   can buffer the stream data in expectation of the matching",
            "   PUSH_PROMISE.  The client can use stream flow control (Section 4.1 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]) to limit the amount of data a server may commit to",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   the pushed stream.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cccafca9f37a1473",
                  "7384cd29aa90ccfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Clients SHOULD abort reading and discard data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cccafca9f37a1473",
                  "7384cd29aa90ccfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "already read from push streams if no corresponding PUSH_PROMISE frame"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cccafca9f37a1473",
                  "7384cd29aa90ccfe"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "is processed in a reasonable amount of time."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Push stream data can also arrive after a client has cancelled a push.",
            "   In this case, the client can abort reading the stream with an error",
            "   code of H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED.  This asks the server not to transfer",
            "   additional data and indicates that it will be discarded upon receipt.",
            "",
            "   Pushed responses that are cacheable (see Section 3 of [HTTP-CACHING])",
            "   can be stored by the client, if it implements an HTTP cache.  Pushed",
            "   responses are considered successfully validated on the origin server",
            "   (e.g., if the \"no-cache\" cache response directive is present; see",
            "   Section 5.2.2.4 of [HTTP-CACHING]) at the time the pushed response is",
            "   received.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35299ebdb9ec904a",
                  "32d11c18786fbb46"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Pushed responses that are not cacheable MUST NOT be stored by any"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35299ebdb9ec904a",
                  "32d11c18786fbb46"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "HTTP cache."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35299ebdb9ec904a"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35299ebdb9ec904a",
                  "70efdf5f37739da8"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "They MAY be made available to the application"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "35299ebdb9ec904a",
                  "70efdf5f37739da8"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "separately."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "3915aa352e28b6f6",
            "3915aa352e28b6f6",
            "6fa3cba172cfcd91",
            "6fa3cba172cfcd91",
            "6fa3cba172cfcd91",
            "6fa3cba172cfcd91",
            "8f171b2462f982d9",
            "8f171b2462f982d9",
            "8f171b2462f982d9",
            "8f171b2462f982d9",
            "8f171b2462f982d9",
            "a0f4588830b09416",
            "a0f4588830b09416",
            "8a1daf82c968aff2",
            "8a1daf82c968aff2",
            "1dd090f4f97d5522",
            "1dd090f4f97d5522",
            "1dd090f4f97d5522",
            "1dd090f4f97d5522",
            "1dd090f4f97d5522",
            "e23ff005728bc4e3",
            "e23ff005728bc4e3",
            "8dc17250b246db1c",
            "8dc17250b246db1c",
            "8dc17250b246db1c",
            "8dc17250b246db1c",
            "dc64f94bbee6efda",
            "dc64f94bbee6efda",
            "7db5bc9707bd2c6e",
            "7db5bc9707bd2c6e",
            "7db5bc9707bd2c6e",
            "7db5bc9707bd2c6e",
            "af8f0f31c7b03064",
            "af8f0f31c7b03064",
            "af8f0f31c7b03064",
            "7384cd29aa90ccfe",
            "7384cd29aa90ccfe",
            "7384cd29aa90ccfe",
            "32d11c18786fbb46",
            "32d11c18786fbb46",
            "70efdf5f37739da8",
            "70efdf5f37739da8"
          ],
          "title": "Server Push"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5",
          "lines": [
            "   Once established, an HTTP/3 connection can be used for many requests",
            "   and responses over time until the connection is closed.  Connection",
            "   closure can happen in any of several different ways."
          ],
          "title": "Connection Closure"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.1",
          "lines": [
            "   Each QUIC endpoint declares an idle timeout during the handshake.  If",
            "   the QUIC connection remains idle (no packets received) for longer",
            "   than this duration, the peer will assume that the connection has been",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   closed.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fd68e7ecd1b6ec12",
                  "484a3ce8aed2bbe4"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "HTTP/3 implementations will need to open a new HTTP/3"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fd68e7ecd1b6ec12",
                  "484a3ce8aed2bbe4"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "connection for new requests if the existing connection has been idle"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fd68e7ecd1b6ec12",
                  "484a3ce8aed2bbe4"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "for longer than the idle timeout negotiated during the QUIC"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fd68e7ecd1b6ec12",
                  "484a3ce8aed2bbe4"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "handshake, and they SHOULD do so if approaching the idle timeout; see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fd68e7ecd1b6ec12",
                  "484a3ce8aed2bbe4"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Section 10.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   HTTP clients are expected to request that the transport keep",
            "   connections open while there are responses outstanding for requests",
            "   or server pushes, as described in Section 10.1.2 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "   If the client is not expecting a response from the server, allowing",
            "   an idle connection to time out is preferred over expending effort",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   maintaining a connection that might not be needed.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "676f7861eaadf717",
                  "0757089a86ff30f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "A gateway MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "676f7861eaadf717",
                  "0757089a86ff30f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "maintain connections in anticipation of need rather than incur the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "676f7861eaadf717",
                  "0757089a86ff30f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "latency cost of connection establishment to servers."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b9b5c07d4a2ae2ce",
                  "36a7691ff29c54d0"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Servers SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b9b5c07d4a2ae2ce",
                  "36a7691ff29c54d0"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "NOT actively keep connections open."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "484a3ce8aed2bbe4",
            "484a3ce8aed2bbe4",
            "484a3ce8aed2bbe4",
            "484a3ce8aed2bbe4",
            "484a3ce8aed2bbe4",
            "0757089a86ff30f3",
            "0757089a86ff30f3",
            "0757089a86ff30f3",
            "36a7691ff29c54d0",
            "36a7691ff29c54d0"
          ],
          "title": "Idle Connections"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Even when a connection is not idle, either endpoint can decide to",
            "   stop using the connection and initiate a graceful connection close.",
            "   Endpoints initiate the graceful shutdown of an HTTP/3 connection by",
            "   sending a GOAWAY frame.  The GOAWAY frame contains an identifier that",
            "   indicates to the receiver the range of requests or pushes that were",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   or might be processed in this connection.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7147ea3f04c9a852"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "The server sends a client-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7147ea3f04c9a852"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "initiated bidirectional stream ID; the client sends a push ID."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7147ea3f04c9a852"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Requests or pushes with the indicated identifier or greater are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7147ea3f04c9a852"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "rejected (Section 4.1.1) by the sender of the GOAWAY.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7147ea3f04c9a852",
                  "2a1a535d36c7ec57"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "This"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7147ea3f04c9a852",
                  "2a1a535d36c7ec57"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "identifier MAY be zero if no requests or pushes were processed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The information in the GOAWAY frame enables a client and server to",
            "   agree on which requests or pushes were accepted prior to the shutdown",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   of the HTTP/3 connection.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8742e659c73da5d7",
                  "38689b3da54dd596"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Upon sending a GOAWAY frame, the endpoint"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8742e659c73da5d7",
                  "38689b3da54dd596"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "SHOULD explicitly cancel (see Sections 4.1.1 and 7.2.3) any requests"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8742e659c73da5d7",
                  "38689b3da54dd596"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "or pushes that have identifiers greater than or equal to the one"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8742e659c73da5d7",
                  "38689b3da54dd596"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "indicated, in order to clean up transport state for the affected"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8742e659c73da5d7",
                  "38689b3da54dd596"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "streams."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "89ca04fd06b61b4d",
                  "b4f5a0cc325e48dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "The endpoint SHOULD continue to do so as more requests or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "89ca04fd06b61b4d",
                  "b4f5a0cc325e48dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "pushes arrive."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "27a78194fb95fb17",
                  "e540cc43e0208525"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST NOT initiate new requests or promise new pushes on the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "27a78194fb95fb17",
                  "e540cc43e0208525"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "connection after receipt of a GOAWAY frame from the peer."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "39fb0466f2c001c9",
                  "f67941570f8ce6ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "39fb0466f2c001c9",
                  "f67941570f8ce6ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "MAY establish a new connection to send additional requests."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Some requests or pushes might already be in transit:",
            "",
            "   *  Upon receipt of a GOAWAY frame, if the client has already sent",
            "      requests with a stream ID greater than or equal to the identifier",
            "      contained in the GOAWAY frame, those requests will not be",
            "      processed.  Clients can safely retry unprocessed requests on a",
            "      different HTTP connection.  A client that is unable to retry",
            "      requests loses all requests that are in flight when the server",
            "      closes the connection.",
            "",
            "      Requests on stream IDs less than the stream ID in a GOAWAY frame",
            "      from the server might have been processed; their status cannot be",
            "      known until a response is received, the stream is reset",
            "      individually, another GOAWAY is received with a lower stream ID",
            "      than that of the request in question, or the connection",
            "      terminates.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac0936dc967dfae2",
                  "547e8fbd6f356e2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Servers MAY reject individual requests on streams below the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac0936dc967dfae2",
                  "547e8fbd6f356e2e"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "indicated ID if these requests were not processed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   *  If a server receives a GOAWAY frame after having promised pushes",
            "      with a push ID greater than or equal to the identifier contained",
            "      in the GOAWAY frame, those pushes will not be accepted.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b35b5cd3a0ac1fd",
                  "93f2dc64ea33b50c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Servers SHOULD send a GOAWAY frame when the closing of a connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b35b5cd3a0ac1fd",
                  "93f2dc64ea33b50c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "is known in advance, even if the advance notice is small, so that the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b35b5cd3a0ac1fd",
                  "93f2dc64ea33b50c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "remote peer can know whether or not a request has been partially"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1b35b5cd3a0ac1fd",
                  "93f2dc64ea33b50c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "processed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  For example, if an HTTP client sends a POST at the same"
              }
            ],
            "   time that a server closes a QUIC connection, the client cannot know",
            "   if the server started to process that POST request if the server does",
            "   not send a GOAWAY frame to indicate what streams it might have acted",
            "   on.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b3dad25aa371980",
                  "2535b50626e41c9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "An endpoint MAY send multiple GOAWAY frames indicating different"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b3dad25aa371980",
                  "2535b50626e41c9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "identifiers, but the identifier in each frame MUST NOT be greater"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b3dad25aa371980",
                  "2535b50626e41c9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "than the identifier in any previous frame, since clients might"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b3dad25aa371980",
                  "2535b50626e41c9c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "already have retried unprocessed requests on another HTTP connection."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "651af02c785ac082",
                  "aad84fe8f12682b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Receiving a GOAWAY containing a larger identifier than previously"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "651af02c785ac082",
                  "aad84fe8f12682b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "received MUST be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   An endpoint that is attempting to gracefully shut down a connection",
            "   can send a GOAWAY frame with a value set to the maximum possible",
            "   value (2^62-4 for servers, 2^62-1 for clients).  This ensures that",
            "   the peer stops creating new requests or pushes.  After allowing time",
            "   for any in-flight requests or pushes to arrive, the endpoint can send",
            "   another GOAWAY frame indicating which requests or pushes it might",
            "   accept before the end of the connection.  This ensures that a",
            "   connection can be cleanly shut down without losing requests.",
            "",
            "   A client has more flexibility in the value it chooses for the Push ID",
            "   field in a GOAWAY that it sends.  A value of 2^62-1 indicates that",
            "   the server can continue fulfilling pushes that have already been",
            "   promised.  A smaller value indicates the client will reject pushes",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   with push IDs greater than or equal to this value.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37249656d1256a73",
                  "0094b17a6c3cef22"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "Like the server,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37249656d1256a73",
                  "0094b17a6c3cef22"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "the client MAY send subsequent GOAWAY frames so long as the specified"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "37249656d1256a73",
                  "0094b17a6c3cef22"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "push ID is no greater than any previously sent value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Even when a GOAWAY indicates that a given request or push will not be",
            "   processed or accepted upon receipt, the underlying transport",
            "   resources still exist.  The endpoint that initiated these requests",
            "   can cancel them to clean up transport state.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff551e5570d0bebc",
                  "e2f6749361cc7cca"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Once all accepted requests and pushes have been processed, the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff551e5570d0bebc",
                  "e2f6749361cc7cca"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "endpoint can permit the connection to become idle, or it MAY initiate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ff551e5570d0bebc",
                  "e2f6749361cc7cca"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "an immediate closure of the connection."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "028226bce4cf92f5",
                  "e356e28a9b617d41"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "An endpoint that completes a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "028226bce4cf92f5",
                  "e356e28a9b617d41"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "graceful shutdown SHOULD use the H3_NO_ERROR error code when closing"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "028226bce4cf92f5",
                  "e356e28a9b617d41"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "the connection."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If a client has consumed all available bidirectional stream IDs with",
            "   requests, the server need not send a GOAWAY frame, since the client",
            "   is unable to make further requests."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "2a1a535d36c7ec57",
            "2a1a535d36c7ec57",
            "38689b3da54dd596",
            "38689b3da54dd596",
            "38689b3da54dd596",
            "38689b3da54dd596",
            "38689b3da54dd596",
            "b4f5a0cc325e48dd",
            "b4f5a0cc325e48dd",
            "e540cc43e0208525",
            "e540cc43e0208525",
            "f67941570f8ce6ed",
            "f67941570f8ce6ed",
            "547e8fbd6f356e2e",
            "547e8fbd6f356e2e",
            "93f2dc64ea33b50c",
            "93f2dc64ea33b50c",
            "93f2dc64ea33b50c",
            "93f2dc64ea33b50c",
            "2535b50626e41c9c",
            "2535b50626e41c9c",
            "2535b50626e41c9c",
            "2535b50626e41c9c",
            "aad84fe8f12682b8",
            "aad84fe8f12682b8",
            "0094b17a6c3cef22",
            "0094b17a6c3cef22",
            "0094b17a6c3cef22",
            "e2f6749361cc7cca",
            "e2f6749361cc7cca",
            "e2f6749361cc7cca",
            "e356e28a9b617d41",
            "e356e28a9b617d41",
            "e356e28a9b617d41"
          ],
          "title": "Connection Shutdown"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.3",
          "lines": [
            "   An HTTP/3 implementation can immediately close the QUIC connection at",
            "   any time.  This results in sending a QUIC CONNECTION_CLOSE frame to",
            "   the peer indicating that the application layer has terminated the",
            "   connection.  The application error code in this frame indicates to",
            "   the peer why the connection is being closed.  See Section 8 for error",
            "   codes that can be used when closing a connection in HTTP/3.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f399b02cae8ef04",
                  "55286aab802a4d87"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Before closing the connection, a GOAWAY frame MAY be sent to allow"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f399b02cae8ef04",
                  "55286aab802a4d87"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "the client to retry some requests."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f399b02cae8ef04"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "  Including the GOAWAY frame in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f399b02cae8ef04"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "same packet as the QUIC CONNECTION_CLOSE frame improves the chances"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9f399b02cae8ef04"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "of the frame being received by clients."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If there are open streams that have not been explicitly closed, they",
            "   are implicitly closed when the connection is closed; see Section 10.2",
            "   of [QUIC-TRANSPORT]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "55286aab802a4d87",
            "55286aab802a4d87"
          ],
          "title": "Immediate Application Closure"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-5.4",
          "lines": [
            "   For various reasons, the QUIC transport could indicate to the",
            "   application layer that the connection has terminated.  This might be",
            "   due to an explicit closure by the peer, a transport-level error, or a",
            "   change in network topology that interrupts connectivity.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e960f1fcbdb1e28",
                  "279b4eb96da49f6c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If a connection terminates without a GOAWAY frame, clients MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e960f1fcbdb1e28",
                  "279b4eb96da49f6c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "assume that any request that was sent, whether in whole or in part,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1e960f1fcbdb1e28",
                  "279b4eb96da49f6c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "might have been processed."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "279b4eb96da49f6c",
            "279b4eb96da49f6c",
            "279b4eb96da49f6c"
          ],
          "title": "Transport Closure"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6",
          "lines": [
            "   A QUIC stream provides reliable in-order delivery of bytes, but makes",
            "   no guarantees about order of delivery with regard to bytes on other",
            "   streams.  In version 1 of QUIC, the stream data containing HTTP",
            "   frames is carried by QUIC STREAM frames, but this framing is",
            "   invisible to the HTTP framing layer.  The transport layer buffers and",
            "   orders received stream data, exposing a reliable byte stream to the",
            "   application.  Although QUIC permits out-of-order delivery within a",
            "   stream, HTTP/3 does not make use of this feature.",
            "",
            "   QUIC streams can be either unidirectional, carrying data only from",
            "   initiator to receiver, or bidirectional, carrying data in both",
            "   directions.  Streams can be initiated by either the client or the",
            "   server.  For more detail on QUIC streams, see Section 2 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "",
            "   When HTTP fields and data are sent over QUIC, the QUIC layer handles",
            "   most of the stream management.  HTTP does not need to do any separate",
            "   multiplexing when using QUIC: data sent over a QUIC stream always",
            "   maps to a particular HTTP transaction or to the entire HTTP/3",
            "   connection context."
          ],
          "title": "Stream Mapping and Usage"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.1",
          "lines": [
            "   All client-initiated bidirectional streams are used for HTTP requests",
            "   and responses.  A bidirectional stream ensures that the response can",
            "   be readily correlated with the request.  These streams are referred",
            "   to as request streams.",
            "",
            "   This means that the client's first request occurs on QUIC stream 0,",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   with subsequent requests on streams 4, 8, and so on.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef894b18943771a5",
                  "757a6ff85af25157"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "In order to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef894b18943771a5",
                  "757a6ff85af25157"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "permit these streams to open, an HTTP/3 server SHOULD configure non-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef894b18943771a5",
                  "757a6ff85af25157"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "zero minimum values for the number of permitted streams and the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ef894b18943771a5",
                  "757a6ff85af25157"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "initial stream flow-control window."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6fc4a692ab701b13",
                  "16544e083447ce87"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "So as to not unnecessarily limit"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6fc4a692ab701b13",
                  "16544e083447ce87"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "parallelism, at least 100 request streams SHOULD be permitted at a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6fc4a692ab701b13",
                  "16544e083447ce87"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "time."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   HTTP/3 does not use server-initiated bidirectional streams, though an",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   extension could define a use for these streams.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e7b93ade4715c5b",
                  "bf8cbc51ae2c49b8",
                  "7df97886005961c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Clients MUST treat"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e7b93ade4715c5b",
                  "bf8cbc51ae2c49b8",
                  "7df97886005961c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "receipt of a server-initiated bidirectional stream as a connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e7b93ade4715c5b",
                  "bf8cbc51ae2c49b8",
                  "7df97886005961c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR unless such an extension has"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e7b93ade4715c5b",
                  "bf8cbc51ae2c49b8",
                  "7df97886005961c4"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "been negotiated."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "757a6ff85af25157",
            "757a6ff85af25157",
            "757a6ff85af25157",
            "757a6ff85af25157",
            "16544e083447ce87",
            "16544e083447ce87",
            "16544e083447ce87",
            "7df97886005961c4",
            "7df97886005961c4",
            "7df97886005961c4",
            "7df97886005961c4"
          ],
          "title": "Bidirectional Streams"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Unidirectional streams, in either direction, are used for a range of",
            "   purposes.  The purpose is indicated by a stream type, which is sent",
            "   as a variable-length integer at the start of the stream.  The format",
            "   and structure of data that follows this integer is determined by the",
            "   stream type.",
            "",
            "   Unidirectional Stream Header {",
            "     Stream Type (i),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                   Figure 1: Unidirectional Stream Header",
            "",
            "   Two stream types are defined in this document: control streams",
            "   (Section 6.2.1) and push streams (Section 6.2.2).  [QPACK] defines",
            "   two additional stream types.  Other stream types can be defined by",
            "   extensions to HTTP/3; see Section 9 for more details.  Some stream",
            "   types are reserved (Section 6.2.3).",
            "",
            "   The performance of HTTP/3 connections in the early phase of their",
            "   lifetime is sensitive to the creation and exchange of data on",
            "   unidirectional streams.  Endpoints that excessively restrict the",
            "   number of streams or the flow-control window of these streams will",
            "   increase the chance that the remote peer reaches the limit early and",
            "   becomes blocked.  In particular, implementations should consider that",
            "   remote peers may wish to exercise reserved stream behavior",
            "   (Section 6.2.3) with some of the unidirectional streams they are",
            "   permitted to use.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Each endpoint needs to create at least one unidirectional stream for"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "the HTTP control stream.  QPACK requires two additional"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "unidirectional streams, and other extensions might require further"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "streams.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b",
                  "f041d2fe59a3ec7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Therefore, the transport parameters sent by both clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b",
                  "f041d2fe59a3ec7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "and servers MUST allow the peer to create at least three"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b",
                  "f041d2fe59a3ec7c"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unidirectional streams."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b",
                  "2be1f4a755942aab"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "These transport parameters SHOULD also"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b",
                  "2be1f4a755942aab"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "provide at least 1,024 bytes of flow-control credit to each"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "929a9831180c6e4b",
                  "2be1f4a755942aab"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "unidirectional stream."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Note that an endpoint is not required to grant additional credits to",
            "   create more unidirectional streams if its peer consumes all the",
            "   initial credits before creating the critical unidirectional streams.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "565c62c557d9ae10",
                  "f9fffa36e5e586b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Endpoints SHOULD create the HTTP control stream as well as the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "565c62c557d9ae10",
                  "f9fffa36e5e586b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "unidirectional streams required by mandatory extensions (such as the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "565c62c557d9ae10",
                  "f9fffa36e5e586b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "QPACK encoder and decoder streams) first, and then create additional"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f9fffa36e5e586b3"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "streams as allowed by their peer."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If the stream header indicates a stream type that is not supported by",
            "   the recipient, the remainder of the stream cannot be consumed as the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   semantics are unknown.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50758fba273e450a",
                  "c0bd3dc16eff47d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Recipients of unknown stream types MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50758fba273e450a",
                  "c0bd3dc16eff47d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "either abort reading of the stream or discard incoming data without"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "50758fba273e450a",
                  "c0bd3dc16eff47d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "further processing."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22749977fe15683b",
                  "ece28172445a589d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "If reading is aborted, the recipient SHOULD use"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22749977fe15683b",
                  "ece28172445a589d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "the H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR error code or a reserved error code"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "22749977fe15683b",
                  "ece28172445a589d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "(Section 8.1)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b75efbe32111810",
                  "830f8b47859906b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The recipient MUST NOT consider unknown stream types"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4b75efbe32111810",
                  "830f8b47859906b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "to be a connection error of any kind."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e144963ca398ab5",
                  "973a11615b6b3c68"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "As certain stream types can affect connection state, a recipient"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e144963ca398ab5",
                  "973a11615b6b3c68"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "SHOULD NOT discard data from incoming unidirectional streams prior to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8e144963ca398ab5",
                  "973a11615b6b3c68"
                ],
                "status_id": 6,
                "text": "reading the stream type."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ea5ead0fb376cee",
                  "f78aaab67f13e2f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "Implementations MAY send stream types before knowing whether the peer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ea5ead0fb376cee",
                  "f78aaab67f13e2f0"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "supports them."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc3c52623fb627bc",
                  "0e083fc722fadb44"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "However, stream types that could modify the state or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc3c52623fb627bc",
                  "0e083fc722fadb44"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "semantics of existing protocol components, including QPACK or other"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dc3c52623fb627bc",
                  "0e083fc722fadb44"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "extensions, MUST NOT be sent until the peer is known to support them."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A sender can close or reset a unidirectional stream unless otherwise",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   specified.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf404173f3d69e6e",
                  "019770d70175fafb"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A receiver MUST tolerate unidirectional streams being"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf404173f3d69e6e",
                  "019770d70175fafb"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "closed or reset prior to the reception of the unidirectional stream"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cf404173f3d69e6e",
                  "019770d70175fafb"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "header."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f041d2fe59a3ec7c",
            "f041d2fe59a3ec7c",
            "f041d2fe59a3ec7c",
            "2be1f4a755942aab",
            "2be1f4a755942aab",
            "2be1f4a755942aab",
            "f9fffa36e5e586b3",
            "f9fffa36e5e586b3",
            "f9fffa36e5e586b3",
            "f9fffa36e5e586b3",
            "c0bd3dc16eff47d1",
            "c0bd3dc16eff47d1",
            "c0bd3dc16eff47d1",
            "ece28172445a589d",
            "ece28172445a589d",
            "ece28172445a589d",
            "830f8b47859906b0",
            "830f8b47859906b0",
            "973a11615b6b3c68",
            "973a11615b6b3c68",
            "973a11615b6b3c68",
            "f78aaab67f13e2f0",
            "f78aaab67f13e2f0",
            "0e083fc722fadb44",
            "0e083fc722fadb44",
            "0e083fc722fadb44",
            "019770d70175fafb",
            "019770d70175fafb",
            "019770d70175fafb"
          ],
          "title": "Unidirectional Streams"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   A control stream is indicated by a stream type of 0x00.  Data on this",
            "   stream consists of HTTP/3 frames, as defined in Section 7.2.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "773cfa903518d745",
                  "5c6a913d6dab89be"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Each side MUST initiate a single control stream at the beginning of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "773cfa903518d745",
                  "5c6a913d6dab89be"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "the connection and send its SETTINGS frame as the first frame on this"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "773cfa903518d745",
                  "5c6a913d6dab89be"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "983e21485bb62cf6",
                  "6a499abebe930a04",
                  "49ab785e362ab475"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If the first frame of the control stream is any other frame"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "983e21485bb62cf6",
                  "6a499abebe930a04",
                  "49ab785e362ab475"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "type, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "983e21485bb62cf6",
                  "6a499abebe930a04",
                  "49ab785e362ab475"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "H3_MISSING_SETTINGS."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bccc3bb13f4df6ed",
                  "d952c61069f2c29b",
                  "cdc40201d195e03d"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Only one control stream per peer is permitted;"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bccc3bb13f4df6ed",
                  "d952c61069f2c29b",
                  "cdc40201d195e03d"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "receipt of a second stream claiming to be a control stream MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bccc3bb13f4df6ed",
                  "d952c61069f2c29b",
                  "cdc40201d195e03d"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "treated as a connection error of type H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09797e0976f1cec5",
                  "f52a0250cab812c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09797e0976f1cec5",
                  "f52a0250cab812c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "sender MUST NOT close the control stream, and the receiver MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "09797e0976f1cec5",
                  "f52a0250cab812c8"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "request that the sender close the control stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "858c14a846b1c5e5",
                  "461113cfc19caa06",
                  "b6f13f7811745223"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If either control"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "858c14a846b1c5e5",
                  "461113cfc19caa06",
                  "b6f13f7811745223"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "stream is closed at any point, this MUST be treated as a connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "858c14a846b1c5e5",
                  "461113cfc19caa06",
                  "b6f13f7811745223"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "error of type H3_CLOSED_CRITICAL_STREAM."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Connection errors are"
              }
            ],
            "   described in Section 8.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "541ad082d250c7a6",
                  "5691356d09c4a182"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "Because the contents of the control stream are used to manage the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "541ad082d250c7a6",
                  "5691356d09c4a182"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "behavior of other streams, endpoints SHOULD provide enough flow-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "541ad082d250c7a6",
                  "5691356d09c4a182"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "control credit to keep the peer's control stream from becoming"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "541ad082d250c7a6",
                  "5691356d09c4a182"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "blocked."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A pair of unidirectional streams is used rather than a single",
            "   bidirectional stream.  This allows either peer to send data as soon",
            "   as it is able.  Depending on whether 0-RTT is available on the QUIC",
            "   connection, either client or server might be able to send stream data",
            "   first."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "5c6a913d6dab89be",
            "5c6a913d6dab89be",
            "5c6a913d6dab89be",
            "49ab785e362ab475",
            "49ab785e362ab475",
            "49ab785e362ab475",
            "cdc40201d195e03d",
            "cdc40201d195e03d",
            "cdc40201d195e03d",
            "f52a0250cab812c8",
            "f52a0250cab812c8",
            "f52a0250cab812c8",
            "b6f13f7811745223",
            "b6f13f7811745223",
            "b6f13f7811745223",
            "5691356d09c4a182",
            "5691356d09c4a182",
            "5691356d09c4a182",
            "5691356d09c4a182"
          ],
          "title": "Control Streams"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Server push is an optional feature introduced in HTTP/2 that allows a",
            "   server to initiate a response before a request has been made.  See",
            "   Section 4.6 for more details.",
            "",
            "   A push stream is indicated by a stream type of 0x01, followed by the",
            "   push ID of the promise that it fulfills, encoded as a variable-length",
            "   integer.  The remaining data on this stream consists of HTTP/3",
            "   frames, as defined in Section 7.2, and fulfills a promised server",
            "   push by zero or more interim HTTP responses followed by a single",
            "   final HTTP response, as defined in Section 4.1.  Server push and push",
            "   IDs are described in Section 4.6.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "16748f744ef535ea",
                  "3990b3f46a171ff4"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Only servers can push; if a server receives a client-initiated push"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "16748f744ef535ea",
                  "3990b3f46a171ff4"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "stream, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "16748f744ef535ea",
                  "3990b3f46a171ff4"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Push Stream Header {",
            "     Stream Type (i) = 0x01,",
            "     Push ID (i),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                        Figure 2: Push Stream Header",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a5a38baee16cb1c",
                  "e0de61642e003a1b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "A client SHOULD NOT abort reading on a push stream prior to reading"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a5a38baee16cb1c",
                  "e0de61642e003a1b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "the push stream header, as this could lead to disagreement between"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2a5a38baee16cb1c",
                  "e0de61642e003a1b"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "client and server on which push IDs have already been consumed."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "7ed8b66fae5bb4e3",
                  "a4a6c565843a8ade"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Each push ID MUST only be used once in a push stream header."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d0b4269ae724adb",
                  "d64170d26820da2c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d0b4269ae724adb",
                  "d64170d26820da2c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "client detects that a push stream header includes a push ID that was"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d0b4269ae724adb",
                  "d64170d26820da2c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "used in another push stream header, the client MUST treat this as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3d0b4269ae724adb",
                  "d64170d26820da2c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "3990b3f46a171ff4",
            "3990b3f46a171ff4",
            "3990b3f46a171ff4",
            "e0de61642e003a1b",
            "e0de61642e003a1b",
            "e0de61642e003a1b",
            "a4a6c565843a8ade",
            "d64170d26820da2c",
            "d64170d26820da2c",
            "d64170d26820da2c",
            "d64170d26820da2c"
          ],
          "title": "Push Streams"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-6.2.3",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f9d426b8614b5c2"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "Stream types of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f9d426b8614b5c2"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "values of N are reserved to exercise the requirement that unknown"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f9d426b8614b5c2"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "types be ignored.  These streams have no semantics, and they can be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f9d426b8614b5c2"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "sent when application-layer padding is desired.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f9d426b8614b5c2",
                  "28c9d02ce683de09"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "They MAY also be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0f9d426b8614b5c2",
                  "28c9d02ce683de09"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "sent on connections where no data is currently being transferred."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a82a88395533696a",
                  "85b46f2a993db513"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider these streams to have any meaning upon"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a82a88395533696a",
                  "85b46f2a993db513"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "receipt."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The payload and length of the stream are selected in any manner the",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   sending implementation chooses.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "28dc3f082f79aec9",
                  "62016693af93c5ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "When sending a reserved stream type,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "28dc3f082f79aec9",
                  "62016693af93c5ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "the implementation MAY either terminate the stream cleanly or reset"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "28dc3f082f79aec9",
                  "62016693af93c5ed"
                ],
                "status_id": 19,
                "text": "it."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33125ae624a6f02a"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "When resetting the stream, either the H3_NO_ERROR error code or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33125ae624a6f02a"
                ],
                "status_id": 20,
                "text": "a reserved error code (Section 8.1) SHOULD be used."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "28c9d02ce683de09",
            "28c9d02ce683de09",
            "85b46f2a993db513",
            "85b46f2a993db513",
            "62016693af93c5ed",
            "62016693af93c5ed",
            "62016693af93c5ed",
            "33125ae624a6f02a",
            "33125ae624a6f02a"
          ],
          "title": "Reserved Stream Types"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP frames are carried on QUIC streams, as described in Section 6.",
            "   HTTP/3 defines three stream types: control stream, request stream,",
            "   and push stream.  This section describes HTTP/3 frame formats and",
            "   their permitted stream types; see Table 1 for an overview.  A",
            "   comparison between HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 frames is provided in",
            "   Appendix A.2.",
            "",
            "   +==============+================+================+========+=========+",
            "   | Frame        | Control Stream | Request        | Push   | Section |",
            "   |              |                | Stream         | Stream |         |",
            "   +==============+================+================+========+=========+",
            "   | DATA         | No             | Yes            | Yes    | Section |",
            "   |              |                |                |        | 7.2.1   |",
            "   +--------------+----------------+----------------+--------+---------+",
            "   | HEADERS      | No             | Yes            | Yes    | Section |",
            "   |              |                |                |        | 7.2.2   |",
            "   +--------------+----------------+----------------+--------+---------+",
            "   | CANCEL_PUSH  | Yes            | No             | No     | Section |",
            "   |              |                |                |        | 7.2.3   |",
            "   +--------------+----------------+----------------+--------+---------+",
            "   | SETTINGS     | Yes (1)        | No             | No     | Section |",
            "   |              |                |                |        | 7.2.4   |",
            "   +--------------+----------------+----------------+--------+---------+",
            "   | PUSH_PROMISE | No             | Yes            | No     | Section |",
            "   |              |                |                |        | 7.2.5   |",
            "   +--------------+----------------+----------------+--------+---------+",
            "   | GOAWAY       | Yes            | No             | No     | Section |",
            "   |              |                |                |        | 7.2.6   |",
            "   +--------------+----------------+----------------+--------+---------+",
            "   | MAX_PUSH_ID  | Yes            | No             | No     | Section |",
            "   |              |                |                |        | 7.2.7   |",
            "   +--------------+----------------+----------------+--------+---------+",
            "   | Reserved     | Yes            | Yes            | Yes    | Section |",
            "   |              |                |                |        | 7.2.8   |",
            "   +--------------+----------------+----------------+--------+---------+",
            "",
            "              Table 1: HTTP/3 Frames and Stream Type Overview",
            "",
            "   The SETTINGS frame can only occur as the first frame of a Control",
            "   stream; this is indicated in Table 1 with a (1).  Specific guidance",
            "   is provided in the relevant section.",
            "",
            "   Note that, unlike QUIC frames, HTTP/3 frames can span multiple",
            "   packets."
          ],
          "title": "HTTP Framing Layer"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.1",
          "lines": [
            "   All frames have the following format:",
            "",
            "   HTTP/3 Frame Format {",
            "     Type (i),",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Frame Payload (..),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                       Figure 3: HTTP/3 Frame Format",
            "",
            "   A frame includes the following fields:",
            "",
            "   Type:  A variable-length integer that identifies the frame type.",
            "",
            "   Length:  A variable-length integer that describes the length in bytes",
            "      of the Frame Payload.",
            "",
            "   Frame Payload:  A payload, the semantics of which are determined by",
            "      the Type field.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "97dd0d49cb4a22b4",
                  "4bffaa7b2c1c3152"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Each frame's payload MUST contain exactly the fields identified in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "97dd0d49cb4a22b4",
                  "4bffaa7b2c1c3152"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "its description."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2923e04c99a175b7",
                  "f803acd8bc4e6be5",
                  "42764cbfdaecb2b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "A frame payload that contains additional bytes"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2923e04c99a175b7",
                  "f803acd8bc4e6be5",
                  "42764cbfdaecb2b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "after the identified fields or a frame payload that terminates before"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2923e04c99a175b7",
                  "f803acd8bc4e6be5",
                  "42764cbfdaecb2b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "the end of the identified fields MUST be treated as a connection"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2923e04c99a175b7",
                  "f803acd8bc4e6be5",
                  "42764cbfdaecb2b8"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "error of type H3_FRAME_ERROR."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "080ed16d5c8b27a4",
                  "243c6cdcb0818cd0",
                  "812f1e756ada4c64",
                  "e2c762004fc06a88"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "In particular, redundant length"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "080ed16d5c8b27a4",
                  "243c6cdcb0818cd0",
                  "812f1e756ada4c64",
                  "e2c762004fc06a88"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "encodings MUST be verified to be self-consistent; see Section 10.8."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48cadc7f78352a1a",
                  "0b7738d81d4a615a"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "When a stream terminates cleanly, if the last frame on the stream was"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48cadc7f78352a1a",
                  "0b7738d81d4a615a"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "truncated, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "48cadc7f78352a1a",
                  "0b7738d81d4a615a"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "H3_FRAME_ERROR."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Streams that terminate abruptly may be reset at any"
              }
            ],
            "   point in a frame."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4bffaa7b2c1c3152",
            "4bffaa7b2c1c3152",
            "42764cbfdaecb2b8",
            "42764cbfdaecb2b8",
            "42764cbfdaecb2b8",
            "42764cbfdaecb2b8",
            "e2c762004fc06a88",
            "e2c762004fc06a88",
            "0b7738d81d4a615a",
            "0b7738d81d4a615a",
            "0b7738d81d4a615a"
          ],
          "title": "Frame Layout"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "Frame Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   DATA frames (type=0x00) convey arbitrary, variable-length sequences",
            "   of bytes associated with HTTP request or response content.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f27bcb12af817198",
                  "127152604cf3e41a"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "DATA frames MUST be associated with an HTTP request or response."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1ce87baefb820d7",
                  "e3c6a671d11a47c1",
                  "7b602960014f50cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1ce87baefb820d7",
                  "e3c6a671d11a47c1",
                  "7b602960014f50cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "a DATA frame is received on a control stream, the recipient MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1ce87baefb820d7",
                  "e3c6a671d11a47c1",
                  "7b602960014f50cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   DATA Frame {",
            "     Type (i) = 0x00,",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Data (..),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                            Figure 4: DATA Frame"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "127152604cf3e41a",
            "7b602960014f50cc",
            "7b602960014f50cc",
            "7b602960014f50cc"
          ],
          "title": "DATA"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The HEADERS frame (type=0x01) is used to carry an HTTP field section",
            "   that is encoded using QPACK.  See [QPACK] for more details.",
            "",
            "   HEADERS Frame {",
            "     Type (i) = 0x01,",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Encoded Field Section (..),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                          Figure 5: HEADERS Frame",
            "",
            "   HEADERS frames can only be sent on request streams or push streams.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a19a0b93e1b1f89c",
                  "3a850aca5d6d4bbd"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "If a HEADERS frame is received on a control stream, the recipient"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a19a0b93e1b1f89c",
                  "3a850aca5d6d4bbd"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "3a850aca5d6d4bbd",
            "3a850aca5d6d4bbd"
          ],
          "title": "HEADERS"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The CANCEL_PUSH frame (type=0x03) is used to request cancellation of",
            "   a server push prior to the push stream being received.  The",
            "   CANCEL_PUSH frame identifies a server push by push ID (see",
            "   Section 4.6), encoded as a variable-length integer.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31dfc2149798bdea"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "When a client sends a CANCEL_PUSH frame, it is indicating that it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31dfc2149798bdea"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "does not wish to receive the promised resource.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31dfc2149798bdea",
                  "4aec43ec1bda0329"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "The server SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31dfc2149798bdea",
                  "4aec43ec1bda0329"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "abort sending the resource, but the mechanism to do so depends on the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31dfc2149798bdea",
                  "4aec43ec1bda0329"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "state of the corresponding push stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  If the server has not yet"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   created a push stream, it does not create one.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c089db5974cc128d",
                  "06fb5e7ed0f290d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "If the push stream is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c089db5974cc128d",
                  "06fb5e7ed0f290d1"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "open, the server SHOULD abruptly terminate that stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b987bccb1c3bcce3",
                  "ddbb733d9eaaef91"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "If the push"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b987bccb1c3bcce3",
                  "ddbb733d9eaaef91"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "stream has already ended, the server MAY still abruptly terminate the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b987bccb1c3bcce3",
                  "ddbb733d9eaaef91"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "stream or MAY take no action."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A server sends a CANCEL_PUSH frame to indicate that it will not be",
            "   fulfilling a promise that was previously sent.  The client cannot",
            "   expect the corresponding promise to be fulfilled, unless it has",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   already received and processed the promised response.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54e31c15cefea0c5",
                  "31caab4fc1dbcade"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Regardless of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54e31c15cefea0c5",
                  "31caab4fc1dbcade"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "whether a push stream has been opened, a server SHOULD send a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54e31c15cefea0c5",
                  "31caab4fc1dbcade"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "CANCEL_PUSH frame when it determines that promise will not be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "54e31c15cefea0c5",
                  "31caab4fc1dbcade"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "fulfilled."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  If a stream has already been opened, the server can abort"
              }
            ],
            "   sending on the stream with an error code of H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED.",
            "",
            "   Sending a CANCEL_PUSH frame has no direct effect on the state of",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   existing push streams.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb24f6635a30a258",
                  "f5487cf12913c622"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "A client SHOULD NOT send a CANCEL_PUSH frame"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "eb24f6635a30a258",
                  "f5487cf12913c622"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "when it has already received a corresponding push stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4834482e1d1791a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "A push"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4834482e1d1791a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "stream could arrive after a client has sent a CANCEL_PUSH frame,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4834482e1d1791a"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "because a server might not have processed the CANCEL_PUSH.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4834482e1d1791a",
                  "7eab7f35fb09bdf3"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "The"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4834482e1d1791a",
                  "7eab7f35fb09bdf3"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "client SHOULD abort reading the stream with an error code of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b4834482e1d1791a",
                  "7eab7f35fb09bdf3"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   A CANCEL_PUSH frame is sent on the control stream.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c93f88531bd194a5",
                  "09648c1ad784e409",
                  "8fdf87bd66f79665",
                  "e76ac93e327f9deb"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Receiving a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c93f88531bd194a5",
                  "09648c1ad784e409",
                  "8fdf87bd66f79665",
                  "e76ac93e327f9deb"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "CANCEL_PUSH frame on a stream other than the control stream MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c93f88531bd194a5",
                  "09648c1ad784e409",
                  "8fdf87bd66f79665",
                  "e76ac93e327f9deb"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "treated as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   CANCEL_PUSH Frame {",
            "     Type (i) = 0x03,",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Push ID (i),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                        Figure 6: CANCEL_PUSH Frame",
            "",
            "   The CANCEL_PUSH frame carries a push ID encoded as a variable-length",
            "   integer.  The Push ID field identifies the server push that is being",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   cancelled; see Section 4.6.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dad341cf81c770d1",
                  "3d9ea830b4cdb36a"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If a CANCEL_PUSH frame is received that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dad341cf81c770d1",
                  "3d9ea830b4cdb36a"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "references a push ID greater than currently allowed on the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dad341cf81c770d1",
                  "3d9ea830b4cdb36a"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "connection, this MUST be treated as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dad341cf81c770d1",
                  "3d9ea830b4cdb36a"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "H3_ID_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   If the client receives a CANCEL_PUSH frame, that frame might identify",
            "   a push ID that has not yet been mentioned by a PUSH_PROMISE frame due",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   to reordering.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1bf83164abb38258",
                  "5bf7b51068068b54"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If a server receives a CANCEL_PUSH frame for a push"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1bf83164abb38258",
                  "5bf7b51068068b54"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "ID that has not yet been mentioned by a PUSH_PROMISE frame, this MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "1bf83164abb38258",
                  "5bf7b51068068b54"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "be treated as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "4aec43ec1bda0329",
            "4aec43ec1bda0329",
            "4aec43ec1bda0329",
            "06fb5e7ed0f290d1",
            "06fb5e7ed0f290d1",
            "ddbb733d9eaaef91",
            "ddbb733d9eaaef91",
            "ddbb733d9eaaef91",
            "31caab4fc1dbcade",
            "31caab4fc1dbcade",
            "31caab4fc1dbcade",
            "31caab4fc1dbcade",
            "f5487cf12913c622",
            "f5487cf12913c622",
            "7eab7f35fb09bdf3",
            "7eab7f35fb09bdf3",
            "7eab7f35fb09bdf3",
            "e76ac93e327f9deb",
            "e76ac93e327f9deb",
            "e76ac93e327f9deb",
            "3d9ea830b4cdb36a",
            "3d9ea830b4cdb36a",
            "3d9ea830b4cdb36a",
            "3d9ea830b4cdb36a",
            "5bf7b51068068b54",
            "5bf7b51068068b54",
            "5bf7b51068068b54"
          ],
          "title": "CANCEL_PUSH"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.4",
          "lines": [
            "   The SETTINGS frame (type=0x04) conveys configuration parameters that",
            "   affect how endpoints communicate, such as preferences and constraints",
            "   on peer behavior.  Individually, a SETTINGS parameter can also be",
            "   referred to as a \"setting\"; the identifier and value of each setting",
            "   parameter can be referred to as a \"setting identifier\" and a \"setting",
            "   value\".",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS frames always apply to an entire HTTP/3 connection, never a",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   single stream.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "843eb908926b1928",
                  "f4f78434a390d332"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "A SETTINGS frame MUST be sent as the first frame of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "843eb908926b1928",
                  "f4f78434a390d332"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "each control stream (see Section 6.2.1) by each peer, and it MUST NOT"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "843eb908926b1928",
                  "f4f78434a390d332"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "be sent subsequently."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee3f92379086f8d9",
                  "ba37e1fbe330665a"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "If an endpoint receives a second SETTINGS"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee3f92379086f8d9",
                  "ba37e1fbe330665a"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "frame on the control stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ee3f92379086f8d9",
                  "ba37e1fbe330665a"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b76f01b92a5ecb5",
                  "0326ee95669b027b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "SETTINGS frames MUST NOT be sent on any stream other than the control"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b76f01b92a5ecb5",
                  "0326ee95669b027b"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45f132d0b684c910",
                  "71589630b7ec019c",
                  "ceb5a3b172d93adf",
                  "12cfbf44692554a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "If an endpoint receives a SETTINGS frame on a different"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45f132d0b684c910",
                  "71589630b7ec019c",
                  "ceb5a3b172d93adf",
                  "12cfbf44692554a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "stream, the endpoint MUST respond with a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "45f132d0b684c910",
                  "71589630b7ec019c",
                  "ceb5a3b172d93adf",
                  "12cfbf44692554a1"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   SETTINGS parameters are not negotiated; they describe characteristics",
            "   of the sending peer that can be used by the receiving peer.  However,",
            "   a negotiation can be implied by the use of SETTINGS: each peer uses",
            "   SETTINGS to advertise a set of supported values.  The definition of",
            "   the setting would describe how each peer combines the two sets to",
            "   conclude which choice will be used.  SETTINGS does not provide a",
            "   mechanism to identify when the choice takes effect.",
            "",
            "   Different values for the same parameter can be advertised by each",
            "   peer.  For example, a client might be willing to consume a very large",
            "   response field section, while servers are more cautious about request",
            "   size.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "983c14c5ad06dd24",
                  "53339c2a59192f3c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "The same setting identifier MUST NOT occur more than once in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "983c14c5ad06dd24",
                  "53339c2a59192f3c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "SETTINGS frame."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10e0aad18f02481e",
                  "004e5121caeeb077"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A receiver MAY treat the presence of duplicate"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "10e0aad18f02481e",
                  "004e5121caeeb077"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "setting identifiers as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The payload of a SETTINGS frame consists of zero or more parameters.",
            "   Each parameter consists of a setting identifier and a value, both",
            "   encoded as QUIC variable-length integers.",
            "",
            "   Setting {",
            "     Identifier (i),",
            "     Value (i),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS Frame {",
            "     Type (i) = 0x04,",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Setting (..) ...,",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                          Figure 7: SETTINGS Frame",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2e2d1f6c8ed7c956",
                  "3c9a2337b928bb98"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "An implementation MUST ignore any parameter with an identifier it"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2e2d1f6c8ed7c956",
                  "3c9a2337b928bb98"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "does not understand."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f4f78434a390d332",
            "f4f78434a390d332",
            "f4f78434a390d332",
            "ba37e1fbe330665a",
            "ba37e1fbe330665a",
            "ba37e1fbe330665a",
            "0326ee95669b027b",
            "0326ee95669b027b",
            "12cfbf44692554a1",
            "12cfbf44692554a1",
            "12cfbf44692554a1",
            "53339c2a59192f3c",
            "53339c2a59192f3c",
            "004e5121caeeb077",
            "004e5121caeeb077",
            "3c9a2337b928bb98",
            "3c9a2337b928bb98"
          ],
          "title": "SETTINGS"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The following settings are defined in HTTP/3:",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS_MAX_FIELD_SECTION_SIZE (0x06):  The default value is",
            "      unlimited.  See Section 4.2.2 for usage.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f46a80a95d00cf3"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "Setting identifiers of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f46a80a95d00cf3"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "integer values of N are reserved to exercise the requirement that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f46a80a95d00cf3"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "unknown identifiers be ignored.  Such settings have no defined"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f46a80a95d00cf3"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "meaning.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f46a80a95d00cf3",
                  "110359c950c5514d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "Endpoints SHOULD include at least one such setting in their"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4f46a80a95d00cf3",
                  "110359c950c5514d"
                ],
                "status_id": 7,
                "text": "SETTINGS frame."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b44801fce652a220",
                  "1ff1049e2acf2dd5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST NOT consider such settings to have"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b44801fce652a220",
                  "1ff1049e2acf2dd5"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "any meaning upon receipt."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Because the setting has no defined meaning, the value of the setting",
            "   can be any value the implementation selects.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1edb8e39f9b72c4",
                  "3feabd0b82a65f9d",
                  "51e9a81064a7de3b",
                  "a2848050c34e3914",
                  "ed29a04aacb827eb"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "Setting identifiers that were defined in [HTTP/2] where there is no"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1edb8e39f9b72c4",
                  "3feabd0b82a65f9d",
                  "51e9a81064a7de3b",
                  "a2848050c34e3914",
                  "ed29a04aacb827eb"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "corresponding HTTP/3 setting have also been reserved"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1edb8e39f9b72c4",
                  "3feabd0b82a65f9d",
                  "51e9a81064a7de3b",
                  "a2848050c34e3914",
                  "ed29a04aacb827eb"
                ],
                "status_id": 22,
                "text": "(Section 11.2.2).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1edb8e39f9b72c4",
                  "3feabd0b82a65f9d",
                  "51e9a81064a7de3b",
                  "a2848050c34e3914",
                  "ed29a04aacb827eb",
                  "75abee02df644c35"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "These reserved settings MUST NOT be sent, and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1edb8e39f9b72c4",
                  "3feabd0b82a65f9d",
                  "51e9a81064a7de3b",
                  "a2848050c34e3914",
                  "ed29a04aacb827eb",
                  "75abee02df644c35"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "their receipt MUST be treated as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f1edb8e39f9b72c4",
                  "3feabd0b82a65f9d",
                  "51e9a81064a7de3b",
                  "a2848050c34e3914",
                  "ed29a04aacb827eb",
                  "75abee02df644c35"
                ],
                "status_id": 13,
                "text": "H3_SETTINGS_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Additional settings can be defined by extensions to HTTP/3; see",
            "   Section 9 for more details."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "110359c950c5514d",
            "110359c950c5514d",
            "1ff1049e2acf2dd5",
            "1ff1049e2acf2dd5",
            "75abee02df644c35",
            "75abee02df644c35",
            "75abee02df644c35"
          ],
          "title": "Defined SETTINGS Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.4.2",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4ffd7eaa78d1bbf3",
                  "ffd79ebc5a82d9bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "An HTTP implementation MUST NOT send frames or requests that would be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4ffd7eaa78d1bbf3",
                  "ffd79ebc5a82d9bd"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "invalid based on its current understanding of the peer's settings."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   All settings begin at an initial value.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "08d201ec21920899",
                  "432e5027f8762abe"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Each endpoint SHOULD use"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "08d201ec21920899",
                  "432e5027f8762abe"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "these initial values to send messages before the peer's SETTINGS"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "08d201ec21920899",
                  "432e5027f8762abe"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "frame has arrived, as packets carrying the settings can be lost or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "08d201ec21920899",
                  "432e5027f8762abe"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "delayed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  When the SETTINGS frame arrives, any settings are changed"
              }
            ],
            "   to their new values.",
            "",
            "   This removes the need to wait for the SETTINGS frame before sending",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   messages.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "546b7a87040177d8",
                  "5e6b147e55423fa0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST NOT require any data to be received from"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "546b7a87040177d8",
                  "5e6b147e55423fa0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "the peer prior to sending the SETTINGS frame; settings MUST be sent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "546b7a87040177d8",
                  "5e6b147e55423fa0"
                ],
                "status_id": 8,
                "text": "as soon as the transport is ready to send data."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   For servers, the initial value of each client setting is the default",
            "   value.",
            "",
            "   For clients using a 1-RTT QUIC connection, the initial value of each",
            "   server setting is the default value.  1-RTT keys will always become",
            "   available prior to the packet containing SETTINGS being processed by",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   QUIC, even if the server sends SETTINGS immediately.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "13a3f5f671281dfc",
                  "39adaf45ccc58747"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Clients SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "13a3f5f671281dfc",
                  "39adaf45ccc58747"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "NOT wait indefinitely for SETTINGS to arrive before sending requests,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "13a3f5f671281dfc",
                  "39adaf45ccc58747"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "but they SHOULD process received datagrams in order to increase the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "13a3f5f671281dfc",
                  "39adaf45ccc58747"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "likelihood of processing SETTINGS before sending the first request."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e6ed5289074edf"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "When a 0-RTT QUIC connection is being used, the initial value of each"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e6ed5289074edf"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "server setting is the value used in the previous session.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e6ed5289074edf",
                  "9289dd1e0f49fe77"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Clients"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e6ed5289074edf",
                  "9289dd1e0f49fe77"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "SHOULD store the settings the server provided in the HTTP/3"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e6ed5289074edf",
                  "9289dd1e0f49fe77"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "connection where resumption information was provided, but they MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e6ed5289074edf",
                  "9289dd1e0f49fe77"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "opt not to store settings in certain cases (e.g., if the session"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "60e6ed5289074edf",
                  "9289dd1e0f49fe77"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "ticket is received before the SETTINGS frame)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dde1ba7ea396b557",
                  "7635202f3f0c45bd",
                  "64cca4e5efb0d987"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A client MUST comply"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dde1ba7ea396b557",
                  "7635202f3f0c45bd",
                  "64cca4e5efb0d987"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "with stored settings -- or default values if no values are stored --"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dde1ba7ea396b557",
                  "7635202f3f0c45bd",
                  "64cca4e5efb0d987"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "when attempting 0-RTT."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a93f56f6b3ab4ab",
                  "729c8396fa58f230",
                  "cddeeae79b42ad02"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Once a server has provided new settings,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9a93f56f6b3ab4ab",
                  "729c8396fa58f230",
                  "cddeeae79b42ad02"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "clients MUST comply with those values."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   A server can remember the settings that it advertised or store an",
            "   integrity-protected copy of the values in the ticket and recover the",
            "   information when accepting 0-RTT data.  A server uses the HTTP/3",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   settings values in determining whether to accept 0-RTT data.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6a49b4fe4aa581",
                  "019ab9a277c307dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6a49b4fe4aa581",
                  "019ab9a277c307dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "server cannot determine that the settings remembered by a client are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6a49b4fe4aa581",
                  "019ab9a277c307dc"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "compatible with its current settings, it MUST NOT accept 0-RTT data."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6a49b4fe4aa581"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Remembered settings are compatible if a client complying with those"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ac6a49b4fe4aa581"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "settings would not violate the server's current settings."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "49b278483a4a4ddf",
                  "72b2dd5043f6ef94"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A server MAY accept 0-RTT and subsequently provide different settings"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "49b278483a4a4ddf",
                  "72b2dd5043f6ef94"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "in its SETTINGS frame."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31b0a0dc47201e44",
                  "a3a828590a6bd9e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If 0-RTT data is accepted by the server, its"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31b0a0dc47201e44",
                  "a3a828590a6bd9e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "SETTINGS frame MUST NOT reduce any limits or alter any values that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "31b0a0dc47201e44",
                  "a3a828590a6bd9e6"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "might be violated by the client with its 0-RTT data."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b37d6718768eacd6",
                  "0ddddef0505cc5fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The server MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b37d6718768eacd6",
                  "0ddddef0505cc5fd"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "include all settings that differ from their default values."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b680e8cab9bf130",
                  "fcf12e48eb6cefcd"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b680e8cab9bf130",
                  "fcf12e48eb6cefcd"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "server accepts 0-RTT but then sends settings that are not compatible"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b680e8cab9bf130",
                  "fcf12e48eb6cefcd"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "with the previously specified settings, this MUST be treated as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5b680e8cab9bf130",
                  "fcf12e48eb6cefcd"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e26e277c06529ec1",
                  "2762ff8045d49714"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If a server accepts"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e26e277c06529ec1",
                  "2762ff8045d49714"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "0-RTT but then sends a SETTINGS frame that omits a setting value that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e26e277c06529ec1",
                  "2762ff8045d49714"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "the client understands (apart from reserved setting identifiers) that"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e26e277c06529ec1",
                  "2762ff8045d49714"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "was previously specified to have a non-default value, this MUST be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e26e277c06529ec1",
                  "2762ff8045d49714"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "treated as a connection error of type H3_SETTINGS_ERROR."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "ffd79ebc5a82d9bd",
            "ffd79ebc5a82d9bd",
            "432e5027f8762abe",
            "432e5027f8762abe",
            "432e5027f8762abe",
            "432e5027f8762abe",
            "5e6b147e55423fa0",
            "5e6b147e55423fa0",
            "5e6b147e55423fa0",
            "39adaf45ccc58747",
            "39adaf45ccc58747",
            "39adaf45ccc58747",
            "39adaf45ccc58747",
            "9289dd1e0f49fe77",
            "9289dd1e0f49fe77",
            "9289dd1e0f49fe77",
            "9289dd1e0f49fe77",
            "9289dd1e0f49fe77",
            "64cca4e5efb0d987",
            "64cca4e5efb0d987",
            "64cca4e5efb0d987",
            "cddeeae79b42ad02",
            "cddeeae79b42ad02",
            "019ab9a277c307dc",
            "019ab9a277c307dc",
            "019ab9a277c307dc",
            "72b2dd5043f6ef94",
            "72b2dd5043f6ef94",
            "a3a828590a6bd9e6",
            "a3a828590a6bd9e6",
            "a3a828590a6bd9e6",
            "0ddddef0505cc5fd",
            "0ddddef0505cc5fd",
            "fcf12e48eb6cefcd",
            "fcf12e48eb6cefcd",
            "fcf12e48eb6cefcd",
            "fcf12e48eb6cefcd",
            "2762ff8045d49714",
            "2762ff8045d49714",
            "2762ff8045d49714",
            "2762ff8045d49714",
            "2762ff8045d49714"
          ],
          "title": "Initialization"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.5",
          "lines": [
            "   The PUSH_PROMISE frame (type=0x05) is used to carry a promised",
            "   request header section from server to client on a request stream.",
            "",
            "   PUSH_PROMISE Frame {",
            "     Type (i) = 0x05,",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Push ID (i),",
            "     Encoded Field Section (..),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                        Figure 8: PUSH_PROMISE Frame",
            "",
            "   The payload consists of:",
            "",
            "   Push ID:  A variable-length integer that identifies the server push",
            "      operation.  A push ID is used in push stream headers (Section 4.6)",
            "      and CANCEL_PUSH frames.",
            "",
            "   Encoded Field Section:  QPACK-encoded request header fields for the",
            "      promised response.  See [QPACK] for more details.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bdbe0b7692bcbc80",
                  "ddef3080399146ba"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A server MUST NOT use a push ID that is larger than the client has"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bdbe0b7692bcbc80",
                  "ddef3080399146ba"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "provided in a MAX_PUSH_ID frame (Section 7.2.7)."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af947b3312e8881b",
                  "a16190e5b336709d"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A client MUST treat"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af947b3312e8881b",
                  "a16190e5b336709d"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame that contains a larger push ID than"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "af947b3312e8881b",
                  "a16190e5b336709d"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "the client has advertised as a connection error of H3_ID_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c3466282e5a98052",
                  "a47aa454bbdef2fc"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "A server MAY use the same push ID in multiple PUSH_PROMISE frames."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c3466282e5a98052",
                  "27f4f80a52e71b41"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If so, the decompressed request header sets MUST contain the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c3466282e5a98052",
                  "27f4f80a52e71b41"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "fields in the same order, and both the name and the value in each"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c3466282e5a98052",
                  "27f4f80a52e71b41"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "field MUST be exact matches."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "21931cea7a58c819"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Clients SHOULD compare the request"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "21931cea7a58c819"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "header sections for resources promised multiple times."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "b0bdc393917f18af",
                  "229fb775ebc4e8e9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "If a client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "b0bdc393917f18af",
                  "229fb775ebc4e8e9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "receives a push ID that has already been promised and detects a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "b0bdc393917f18af",
                  "229fb775ebc4e8e9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "mismatch, it MUST respond with a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "b0bdc393917f18af",
                  "229fb775ebc4e8e9"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "H3_GENERAL_PROTOCOL_ERROR."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "54e5f27c49bf0f70"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "If the decompressed field sections match"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "54e5f27c49bf0f70"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "exactly, the client SHOULD associate the pushed content with each"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8992c704681d1fc5",
                  "54e5f27c49bf0f70"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "stream on which a PUSH_PROMISE frame was received."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8c4334a132ba7bb"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Allowing duplicate references to the same push ID is primarily to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8c4334a132ba7bb"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "reduce duplication caused by concurrent requests.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8c4334a132ba7bb",
                  "98b391d596d52e3d"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "A server SHOULD"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "f8c4334a132ba7bb",
                  "98b391d596d52e3d"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "avoid reusing a push ID over a long period."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Clients are likely to"
              }
            ],
            "   consume server push responses and not retain them for reuse over",
            "   time.  Clients that see a PUSH_PROMISE frame that uses a push ID that",
            "   they have already consumed and discarded are forced to ignore the",
            "   promise.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ea684161a5cd041f",
                  "c2058bd747e103f7"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "If a PUSH_PROMISE frame is received on the control stream, the client"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ea684161a5cd041f",
                  "c2058bd747e103f7"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "MUST respond with a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "b875f5625dcf7a81",
                  "ed53d52b7b2c9488"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A client MUST NOT send a PUSH_PROMISE frame."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e2018074798db64",
                  "8ad30eff7fcc7c93",
                  "a264e1afa211fa33"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "A server MUST treat the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e2018074798db64",
                  "8ad30eff7fcc7c93",
                  "a264e1afa211fa33"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "receipt of a PUSH_PROMISE frame as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6e2018074798db64",
                  "8ad30eff7fcc7c93",
                  "a264e1afa211fa33"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   See Section 4.6 for a description of the overall server push",
            "   mechanism."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "ddef3080399146ba",
            "ddef3080399146ba",
            "a16190e5b336709d",
            "a16190e5b336709d",
            "a16190e5b336709d",
            "a47aa454bbdef2fc",
            "27f4f80a52e71b41",
            "27f4f80a52e71b41",
            "27f4f80a52e71b41",
            "21931cea7a58c819",
            "21931cea7a58c819",
            "229fb775ebc4e8e9",
            "229fb775ebc4e8e9",
            "229fb775ebc4e8e9",
            "229fb775ebc4e8e9",
            "54e5f27c49bf0f70",
            "54e5f27c49bf0f70",
            "54e5f27c49bf0f70",
            "98b391d596d52e3d",
            "98b391d596d52e3d",
            "c2058bd747e103f7",
            "c2058bd747e103f7",
            "ed53d52b7b2c9488",
            "a264e1afa211fa33",
            "a264e1afa211fa33",
            "a264e1afa211fa33"
          ],
          "title": "PUSH_PROMISE"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.6",
          "lines": [
            "   The GOAWAY frame (type=0x07) is used to initiate graceful shutdown of",
            "   an HTTP/3 connection by either endpoint.  GOAWAY allows an endpoint",
            "   to stop accepting new requests or pushes while still finishing",
            "   processing of previously received requests and pushes.  This enables",
            "   administrative actions, like server maintenance.  GOAWAY by itself",
            "   does not close a connection.",
            "",
            "   GOAWAY Frame {",
            "     Type (i) = 0x07,",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Stream ID/Push ID (i),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                           Figure 9: GOAWAY Frame",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "897bb33be841db66"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "The GOAWAY frame is always sent on the control stream.  In the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "897bb33be841db66"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "server-to-client direction, it carries a QUIC stream ID for a client-"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "897bb33be841db66"
                ],
                "status_id": 21,
                "text": "initiated bidirectional stream encoded as a variable-length integer."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "897bb33be841db66",
                  "107c5e17f53007c1",
                  "411ae7d197b5e75f"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "A client MUST treat receipt of a GOAWAY frame containing a stream ID"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "897bb33be841db66",
                  "107c5e17f53007c1",
                  "411ae7d197b5e75f"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "of any other type as a connection error of type H3_ID_ERROR."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   In the client-to-server direction, the GOAWAY frame carries a push ID",
            "   encoded as a variable-length integer.",
            "",
            "   The GOAWAY frame applies to the entire connection, not a specific",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   stream.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6aafaca728703ff4",
                  "fabbbf6484ec8332",
                  "8dea253ace587866",
                  "bca37440c7c8dc9d"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "A client MUST treat a GOAWAY frame on a stream other than"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6aafaca728703ff4",
                  "fabbbf6484ec8332",
                  "8dea253ace587866",
                  "bca37440c7c8dc9d"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "the control stream as a connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   See Section 5.2 for more information on the use of the GOAWAY frame."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "411ae7d197b5e75f",
            "411ae7d197b5e75f",
            "bca37440c7c8dc9d",
            "bca37440c7c8dc9d"
          ],
          "title": "GOAWAY"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.7",
          "lines": [
            "   The MAX_PUSH_ID frame (type=0x0d) is used by clients to control the",
            "   number of server pushes that the server can initiate.  This sets the",
            "   maximum value for a push ID that the server can use in PUSH_PROMISE",
            "   and CANCEL_PUSH frames.  Consequently, this also limits the number of",
            "   push streams that the server can initiate in addition to the limit",
            "   maintained by the QUIC transport.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "914110a0b4a72190",
                  "c8cf666193c12086",
                  "a799fa2bf14d7ceb"
                ],
                "status_id": 23,
                "text": "The MAX_PUSH_ID frame is always sent on the control stream.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "914110a0b4a72190",
                  "c8cf666193c12086",
                  "a799fa2bf14d7ceb",
                  "647f128b19cf5ab3"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "Receipt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "914110a0b4a72190",
                  "c8cf666193c12086",
                  "a799fa2bf14d7ceb",
                  "647f128b19cf5ab3"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame on any other stream MUST be treated as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "914110a0b4a72190",
                  "c8cf666193c12086",
                  "a799fa2bf14d7ceb",
                  "647f128b19cf5ab3"
                ],
                "status_id": 5,
                "text": "connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8b84ef0f629acf5e",
                  "96610cfb897dfeab"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A server MUST NOT send a MAX_PUSH_ID frame."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c00ef4d1aa6c1783",
                  "d70507bb4dc8e33c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "A client MUST treat the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c00ef4d1aa6c1783",
                  "d70507bb4dc8e33c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "c00ef4d1aa6c1783",
                  "d70507bb4dc8e33c"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The maximum push ID is unset when an HTTP/3 connection is created,",
            "   meaning that a server cannot push until it receives a MAX_PUSH_ID",
            "   frame.  A client that wishes to manage the number of promised server",
            "   pushes can increase the maximum push ID by sending MAX_PUSH_ID frames",
            "   as the server fulfills or cancels server pushes.",
            "",
            "   MAX_PUSH_ID Frame {",
            "     Type (i) = 0x0d,",
            "     Length (i),",
            "     Push ID (i),",
            "   }",
            "",
            "                        Figure 10: MAX_PUSH_ID Frame",
            "",
            "   The MAX_PUSH_ID frame carries a single variable-length integer that",
            "   identifies the maximum value for a push ID that the server can use;",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   see Section 4.6.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "954d0359f0f0f1fe",
                  "2b438eda7d19ed47"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "A MAX_PUSH_ID frame cannot reduce the maximum push"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "954d0359f0f0f1fe",
                  "2b438eda7d19ed47"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "ID; receipt of a MAX_PUSH_ID frame that contains a smaller value than"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "954d0359f0f0f1fe",
                  "2b438eda7d19ed47"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "previously received MUST be treated as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "954d0359f0f0f1fe",
                  "2b438eda7d19ed47"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "H3_ID_ERROR."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "647f128b19cf5ab3",
            "647f128b19cf5ab3",
            "647f128b19cf5ab3",
            "96610cfb897dfeab",
            "d70507bb4dc8e33c",
            "d70507bb4dc8e33c",
            "d70507bb4dc8e33c",
            "2b438eda7d19ed47",
            "2b438eda7d19ed47",
            "2b438eda7d19ed47",
            "2b438eda7d19ed47"
          ],
          "title": "MAX_PUSH_ID"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-7.2.8",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e0f5b6514483050b"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "Frame types of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e0f5b6514483050b"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "values of N are reserved to exercise the requirement that unknown"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e0f5b6514483050b"
                ],
                "status_id": 17,
                "text": "types be ignored (Section 9).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e0f5b6514483050b",
                  "49253564b73f9473"
                ],
                "status_id": 24,
                "text": "These frames have no semantics, and"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e0f5b6514483050b",
                  "49253564b73f9473"
                ],
                "status_id": 24,
                "text": "they MAY be sent on any stream where frames are allowed to be sent."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   This enables their use for application-layer padding.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9c073bf0cd7af5a7",
                  "f9662646873fc86c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Endpoints MUST"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "9c073bf0cd7af5a7",
                  "f9662646873fc86c"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "NOT consider these frames to have any meaning upon receipt."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The payload and length of the frames are selected in any manner the",
            "   implementation chooses.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6a62c1f0188770dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Frame types that were used in HTTP/2 where there is no corresponding"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6a62c1f0188770dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "HTTP/3 frame have also been reserved (Section 11.2.1).  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6a62c1f0188770dd",
                  "81557ad6ddd786b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "These frame"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6a62c1f0188770dd",
                  "81557ad6ddd786b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "types MUST NOT be sent, and their receipt MUST be treated as a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6a62c1f0188770dd",
                  "81557ad6ddd786b0"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "connection error of type H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "49253564b73f9473",
            "49253564b73f9473",
            "f9662646873fc86c",
            "f9662646873fc86c",
            "81557ad6ddd786b0",
            "81557ad6ddd786b0",
            "81557ad6ddd786b0"
          ],
          "title": "Reserved Frame Types"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8",
          "lines": [
            "   When a stream cannot be completed successfully, QUIC allows the",
            "   application to abruptly terminate (reset) that stream and communicate",
            "   a reason; see Section 2.4 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  This is referred to",
            "   as a \"stream error\".  An HTTP/3 implementation can decide to close a",
            "   QUIC stream and communicate the type of error.  Wire encodings of",
            "   error codes are defined in Section 8.1.  Stream errors are distinct",
            "   from HTTP status codes that indicate error conditions.  Stream errors",
            "   indicate that the sender did not transfer or consume the full request",
            "   or response, while HTTP status codes indicate the result of a request",
            "   that was successfully received.",
            "",
            "   If an entire connection needs to be terminated, QUIC similarly",
            "   provides mechanisms to communicate a reason; see Section 5.3 of",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  This is referred to as a \"connection error\".",
            "   Similar to stream errors, an HTTP/3 implementation can terminate a",
            "   QUIC connection and communicate the reason using an error code from",
            "   Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   Although the reasons for closing streams and connections are called",
            "   \"errors\", these actions do not necessarily indicate a problem with",
            "   the connection or either implementation.  For example, a stream can",
            "   be reset if the requested resource is no longer needed.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c12a40ffb17c5d8",
                  "31df5bbeae17f51c"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "An endpoint MAY choose to treat a stream error as a connection error"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c12a40ffb17c5d8",
                  "31df5bbeae17f51c"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "under certain circumstances, closing the entire connection in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5c12a40ffb17c5d8",
                  "31df5bbeae17f51c"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "response to a condition on a single stream."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Implementations need to"
              }
            ],
            "   consider the impact on outstanding requests before making this",
            "   choice.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc96cf241cb05ea",
                  "f005fa2c08aa8cd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Because new error codes can be defined without negotiation (see"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc96cf241cb05ea",
                  "f005fa2c08aa8cd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Section 9), use of an error code in an unexpected context or receipt"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc96cf241cb05ea",
                  "f005fa2c08aa8cd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "of an unknown error code MUST be treated as equivalent to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "4dc96cf241cb05ea",
                  "f005fa2c08aa8cd4"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "H3_NO_ERROR."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  However, closing a stream can have other effects"
              }
            ],
            "   regardless of the error code; for example, see Section 4.1."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "31df5bbeae17f51c",
            "31df5bbeae17f51c",
            "31df5bbeae17f51c",
            "f005fa2c08aa8cd4",
            "f005fa2c08aa8cd4",
            "f005fa2c08aa8cd4",
            "f005fa2c08aa8cd4"
          ],
          "title": "Error Handling"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-8.1",
          "lines": [
            "   The following error codes are defined for use when abruptly",
            "   terminating streams, aborting reading of streams, or immediately",
            "   closing HTTP/3 connections.",
            "",
            "   H3_NO_ERROR (0x0100):  No error.  This is used when the connection or",
            "      stream needs to be closed, but there is no error to signal.",
            "",
            "   H3_GENERAL_PROTOCOL_ERROR (0x0101):  Peer violated protocol",
            "      requirements in a way that does not match a more specific error",
            "      code or endpoint declines to use the more specific error code.",
            "",
            "   H3_INTERNAL_ERROR (0x0102):  An internal error has occurred in the",
            "      HTTP stack.",
            "",
            "   H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR (0x0103):  The endpoint detected that its",
            "      peer created a stream that it will not accept.",
            "",
            "   H3_CLOSED_CRITICAL_STREAM (0x0104):  A stream required by the HTTP/3",
            "      connection was closed or reset.",
            "",
            "   H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED (0x0105):  A frame was received that was not",
            "      permitted in the current state or on the current stream.",
            "",
            "   H3_FRAME_ERROR (0x0106):  A frame that fails to satisfy layout",
            "      requirements or with an invalid size was received.",
            "",
            "   H3_EXCESSIVE_LOAD (0x0107):  The endpoint detected that its peer is",
            "      exhibiting a behavior that might be generating excessive load.",
            "",
            "   H3_ID_ERROR (0x0108):  A stream ID or push ID was used incorrectly,",
            "      such as exceeding a limit, reducing a limit, or being reused.",
            "",
            "   H3_SETTINGS_ERROR (0x0109):  An endpoint detected an error in the",
            "      payload of a SETTINGS frame.",
            "",
            "   H3_MISSING_SETTINGS (0x010a):  No SETTINGS frame was received at the",
            "      beginning of the control stream.",
            "",
            "   H3_REQUEST_REJECTED (0x010b):  A server rejected a request without",
            "      performing any application processing.",
            "",
            "   H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED (0x010c):  The request or its response",
            "      (including pushed response) is cancelled.",
            "",
            "   H3_REQUEST_INCOMPLETE (0x010d):  The client's stream terminated",
            "      without containing a fully formed request.",
            "",
            "   H3_MESSAGE_ERROR (0x010e):  An HTTP message was malformed and cannot",
            "      be processed.",
            "",
            "   H3_CONNECT_ERROR (0x010f):  The TCP connection established in",
            "      response to a CONNECT request was reset or abnormally closed.",
            "",
            "   H3_VERSION_FALLBACK (0x0110):  The requested operation cannot be",
            "      served over HTTP/3.  The peer should retry over HTTP/1.1.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ab253e959d92da5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "Error codes of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ab253e959d92da5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "values of N are reserved to exercise the requirement that unknown"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ab253e959d92da5"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "error codes be treated as equivalent to H3_NO_ERROR (Section 9)."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ab253e959d92da5",
                  "661faba88f31a532"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Implementations SHOULD select an error code from this space with some"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5ab253e959d92da5",
                  "661faba88f31a532"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "probability when they would have sent H3_NO_ERROR."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "661faba88f31a532",
            "661faba88f31a532"
          ],
          "title": "HTTP/3 Error Codes"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-9",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/3 permits extension of the protocol.  Within the limitations",
            "   described in this section, protocol extensions can be used to provide",
            "   additional services or alter any aspect of the protocol.  Extensions",
            "   are effective only within the scope of a single HTTP/3 connection.",
            "",
            "   This applies to the protocol elements defined in this document.  This",
            "   does not affect the existing options for extending HTTP, such as",
            "   defining new methods, status codes, or fields.",
            "",
            "   Extensions are permitted to use new frame types (Section 7.2), new",
            "   settings (Section 7.2.4.1), new error codes (Section 8), or new",
            "   unidirectional stream types (Section 6.2).  Registries are",
            "   established for managing these extension points: frame types",
            "   (Section 11.2.1), settings (Section 11.2.2), error codes",
            "   (Section 11.2.3), and stream types (Section 11.2.4).",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd71538ccf82aeeb",
                  "fbee3adc4145ecde"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Implementations MUST ignore unknown or unsupported values in all"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "dd71538ccf82aeeb",
                  "fbee3adc4145ecde"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "extensible protocol elements."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33e867e6195b6ec1",
                  "81e9cbc8751f2cce"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "Implementations MUST discard data or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33e867e6195b6ec1",
                  "81e9cbc8751f2cce"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "abort reading on unidirectional streams that have unknown or"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33e867e6195b6ec1",
                  "81e9cbc8751f2cce"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "unsupported types."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  This means that any of these extension points can"
              }
            ],
            "   be safely used by extensions without prior arrangement or",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   negotiation.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04da51f1046d8115",
                  "5c8f24fa1ff2b911"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "However, where a known frame type is required to be in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04da51f1046d8115",
                  "5c8f24fa1ff2b911"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "a specific location, such as the SETTINGS frame as the first frame of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04da51f1046d8115",
                  "5c8f24fa1ff2b911"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "the control stream (see Section 6.2.1), an unknown frame type does"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "04da51f1046d8115",
                  "5c8f24fa1ff2b911"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "not satisfy that requirement and SHOULD be treated as an error."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87d08f4178de733a",
                  "66eab4393614241d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Extensions that could change the semantics of existing protocol"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "87d08f4178de733a",
                  "66eab4393614241d"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "components MUST be negotiated before being used."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  For example, an"
              }
            ],
            "   extension that changes the layout of the HEADERS frame cannot be used",
            "   until the peer has given a positive signal that this is acceptable.",
            "   Coordinating when such a revised layout comes into effect could prove",
            "   complex.  As such, allocating new identifiers for new definitions of",
            "   existing protocol elements is likely to be more effective.",
            "",
            "   This document does not mandate a specific method for negotiating the",
            "   use of an extension, but it notes that a setting (Section 7.2.4.1)",
            "   could be used for that purpose.  If both peers set a value that",
            "   indicates willingness to use the extension, then the extension can be",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   used.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e774e62d373ef48f",
                  "ba1f10f5ae72dca4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "If a setting is used for extension negotiation, the default"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e774e62d373ef48f",
                  "ba1f10f5ae72dca4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "value MUST be defined in such a fashion that the extension is"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e774e62d373ef48f",
                  "ba1f10f5ae72dca4"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "disabled if the setting is omitted."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "fbee3adc4145ecde",
            "fbee3adc4145ecde",
            "81e9cbc8751f2cce",
            "81e9cbc8751f2cce",
            "81e9cbc8751f2cce",
            "5c8f24fa1ff2b911",
            "5c8f24fa1ff2b911",
            "5c8f24fa1ff2b911",
            "5c8f24fa1ff2b911",
            "66eab4393614241d",
            "66eab4393614241d",
            "ba1f10f5ae72dca4",
            "ba1f10f5ae72dca4",
            "ba1f10f5ae72dca4"
          ],
          "title": "Extensions to HTTP/3"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10",
          "lines": [
            "   The security considerations of HTTP/3 should be comparable to those",
            "   of HTTP/2 with TLS.  However, many of the considerations from",
            "   Section 10 of [HTTP/2] apply to [QUIC-TRANSPORT] and are discussed in",
            "   that document."
          ],
          "title": "Security Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.1",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/3 relies on the HTTP definition of authority.  The security",
            "   considerations of establishing authority are discussed in",
            "   Section 17.1 of [HTTP]."
          ],
          "title": "Server Authority"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The use of ALPN in the TLS and QUIC handshakes establishes the target",
            "   application protocol before application-layer bytes are processed.",
            "   This ensures that endpoints have strong assurances that peers are",
            "   using the same protocol.",
            "",
            "   This does not guarantee protection from all cross-protocol attacks.",
            "   Section 21.5 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT] describes some ways in which the",
            "   plaintext of QUIC packets can be used to perform request forgery",
            "   against endpoints that don't use authenticated transports."
          ],
          "title": "Cross-Protocol Attacks"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.3",
          "lines": [
            "   The HTTP/3 field encoding allows the expression of names that are not",
            "   valid field names in the syntax used by HTTP (Section 5.1 of [HTTP]).",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3216127f35d63a7c",
                  "b00ea8d3a3983a35"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Requests or responses containing invalid field names MUST be treated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3216127f35d63a7c",
                  "b00ea8d3a3983a35"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "as malformed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Therefore, an intermediary cannot translate an HTTP/3"
              }
            ],
            "   request or response containing an invalid field name into an HTTP/1.1",
            "   message.",
            "",
            "   Similarly, HTTP/3 can transport field values that are not valid.",
            "   While most values that can be encoded will not alter field parsing,",
            "   carriage return (ASCII 0x0d), line feed (ASCII 0x0a), and the null",
            "   character (ASCII 0x00) might be exploited by an attacker if they are",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   translated verbatim.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a5dc0bb622406b9",
                  "ab50585e50f008cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "Any request or response that contains a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a5dc0bb622406b9",
                  "ab50585e50f008cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "character not permitted in a field value MUST be treated as"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a5dc0bb622406b9",
                  "ab50585e50f008cc"
                ],
                "status_id": 16,
                "text": "malformed."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Valid characters are defined by the \"field-content\" ABNF"
              }
            ],
            "   rule in Section 5.5 of [HTTP]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b00ea8d3a3983a35",
            "b00ea8d3a3983a35",
            "ab50585e50f008cc",
            "ab50585e50f008cc",
            "ab50585e50f008cc"
          ],
          "title": "Intermediary-Encapsulation Attacks"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.4",
          "lines": [
            "   Pushed responses do not have an explicit request from the client; the",
            "   request is provided by the server in the PUSH_PROMISE frame.",
            "",
            "   Caching responses that are pushed is possible based on the guidance",
            "   provided by the origin server in the Cache-Control header field.",
            "   However, this can cause issues if a single server hosts more than one",
            "   tenant.  For example, a server might offer multiple users each a",
            "   small portion of its URI space.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8843f05493cadb1a",
                  "6618ea9abe2850f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Where multiple tenants share space on the same server, that server"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8843f05493cadb1a",
                  "6618ea9abe2850f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST ensure that tenants are not able to push representations of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "8843f05493cadb1a",
                  "6618ea9abe2850f3"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "resources that they do not have authority over."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  Failure to enforce"
              }
            ],
            "   this would allow a tenant to provide a representation that would be",
            "   served out of cache, overriding the actual representation that the",
            "   authoritative tenant provides.",
            "",
            "   Clients are required to reject pushed responses for which an origin",
            "   server is not authoritative; see Section 4.6."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "6618ea9abe2850f3",
            "6618ea9abe2850f3",
            "6618ea9abe2850f3"
          ],
          "title": "Cacheability of Pushed Responses"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.5",
          "lines": [
            "   An HTTP/3 connection can demand a greater commitment of resources to",
            "   operate than an HTTP/1.1 or HTTP/2 connection.  The use of field",
            "   compression and flow control depend on a commitment of resources for",
            "   storing a greater amount of state.  Settings for these features",
            "   ensure that memory commitments for these features are strictly",
            "   bounded.",
            "",
            "   The number of PUSH_PROMISE frames is constrained in a similar",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   fashion.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86b69ab907faa922",
                  "3cc98ad8fb02ba5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "A client that accepts server push SHOULD limit the number"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "86b69ab907faa922",
                  "3cc98ad8fb02ba5e"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "of push IDs it issues at a time."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Processing capacity cannot be guarded as effectively as state",
            "   capacity.",
            "",
            "   The ability to send undefined protocol elements that the peer is",
            "   required to ignore can be abused to cause a peer to expend additional",
            "   processing time.  This might be done by setting multiple undefined",
            "   SETTINGS parameters, unknown frame types, or unknown stream types.",
            "   Note, however, that some uses are entirely legitimate, such as",
            "   optional-to-understand extensions and padding to increase resistance",
            "   to traffic analysis.",
            "",
            "   Compression of field sections also offers some opportunities to waste",
            "   processing resources; see Section 7 of [QPACK] for more details on",
            "   potential abuses.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33643dd014b3cc10"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "All these features -- i.e., server push, unknown protocol elements,"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33643dd014b3cc10"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "field compression -- have legitimate uses.  These features become a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33643dd014b3cc10"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "burden only when they are used unnecessarily or to excess."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33643dd014b3cc10"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "An endpoint that does not monitor such behavior exposes itself to a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33643dd014b3cc10"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "risk of denial-of-service attack.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33643dd014b3cc10",
                  "fff8299c267e67dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "Implementations SHOULD track the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "33643dd014b3cc10",
                  "fff8299c267e67dd"
                ],
                "status_id": 11,
                "text": "use of these features and set limits on their use."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7baf8f46c2bba31",
                  "30435513d440a425"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "An endpoint MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7baf8f46c2bba31",
                  "30435513d440a425"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "treat activity that is suspicious as a connection error of type"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7baf8f46c2bba31",
                  "30435513d440a425"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "H3_EXCESSIVE_LOAD, but false positives will result in disrupting"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "a7baf8f46c2bba31",
                  "30435513d440a425"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "valid connections and requests."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "3cc98ad8fb02ba5e",
            "3cc98ad8fb02ba5e",
            "fff8299c267e67dd",
            "fff8299c267e67dd",
            "30435513d440a425",
            "30435513d440a425",
            "30435513d440a425",
            "30435513d440a425"
          ],
          "title": "Denial-of-Service Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.5.1",
          "lines": [
            "   A large field section (Section 4.1) can cause an implementation to",
            "   commit a large amount of state.  Header fields that are critical for",
            "   routing can appear toward the end of a header section, which prevents",
            "   streaming of the header section to its ultimate destination.  This",
            "   ordering and other reasons, such as ensuring cache correctness, mean",
            "   that an endpoint likely needs to buffer the entire header section.",
            "   Since there is no hard limit to the size of a field section, some",
            "   endpoints could be forced to commit a large amount of available",
            "   memory for header fields.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3439932dd7160b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "An endpoint can use the SETTINGS_MAX_FIELD_SECTION_SIZE"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3439932dd7160b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "(Section 4.2.2) setting to advise peers of limits that might apply on"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3439932dd7160b"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "the size of field sections.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3439932dd7160b",
                  "16c88b859a586492"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "This setting is only advisory, so"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3439932dd7160b",
                  "16c88b859a586492"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "endpoints MAY choose to send field sections that exceed this limit"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2c3439932dd7160b",
                  "16c88b859a586492"
                ],
                "status_id": 10,
                "text": "and risk having the request or response being treated as malformed."
              }
            ],
            "   This setting is specific to an HTTP/3 connection, so any request or",
            "   response could encounter a hop with a lower, unknown limit.  An",
            "   intermediary can attempt to avoid this problem by passing on values",
            "   presented by different peers, but they are not obligated to do so.",
            "",
            "   A server that receives a larger field section than it is willing to",
            "   handle can send an HTTP 431 (Request Header Fields Too Large) status",
            "   code ([RFC6585]).  A client can discard responses that it cannot",
            "   process."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "16c88b859a586492",
            "16c88b859a586492",
            "16c88b859a586492"
          ],
          "title": "Limits on Field Section Size"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.5.2",
          "lines": [
            "   The CONNECT method can be used to create disproportionate load on a",
            "   proxy, since stream creation is relatively inexpensive when compared",
            "   to the creation and maintenance of a TCP connection.  Therefore, a",
            "   proxy that supports CONNECT might be more conservative in the number",
            "   of simultaneous requests it accepts.",
            "",
            "   A proxy might also maintain some resources for a TCP connection",
            "   beyond the closing of the stream that carries the CONNECT request,",
            "   since the outgoing TCP connection remains in the TIME_WAIT state.  To",
            "   account for this, a proxy might delay increasing the QUIC stream",
            "   limits for some time after a TCP connection terminates."
          ],
          "title": "CONNECT Issues"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.6",
          "lines": [
            "   Compression can allow an attacker to recover secret data when it is",
            "   compressed in the same context as data under attacker control.",
            "   HTTP/3 enables compression of fields (Section 4.2); the following",
            "   concerns also apply to the use of HTTP compressed content-codings;",
            "   see Section 8.4.1 of [HTTP].",
            "",
            "   There are demonstrable attacks on compression that exploit the",
            "   characteristics of the web (e.g., [BREACH]).  The attacker induces",
            "   multiple requests containing varying plaintext, observing the length",
            "   of the resulting ciphertext in each, which reveals a shorter length",
            "   when a guess about the secret is correct.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79eb79f93938496c",
                  "21823b164e17aacf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Implementations communicating on a secure channel MUST NOT compress"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79eb79f93938496c",
                  "21823b164e17aacf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "content that includes both confidential and attacker-controlled data"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79eb79f93938496c",
                  "21823b164e17aacf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "unless separate compression contexts are used for each source of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "79eb79f93938496c",
                  "21823b164e17aacf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "data."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "244041e7aff572a3",
                  "a194991955a45aff"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Compression MUST NOT be used if the source of data cannot be"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "244041e7aff572a3",
                  "a194991955a45aff"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "reliably determined."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Further considerations regarding the compression of field sections",
            "   are described in [QPACK]."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "21823b164e17aacf",
            "21823b164e17aacf",
            "21823b164e17aacf",
            "21823b164e17aacf",
            "a194991955a45aff",
            "a194991955a45aff"
          ],
          "title": "Use of Compression"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.7",
          "lines": [
            "   Padding can be used to obscure the exact size of frame content and is",
            "   provided to mitigate specific attacks within HTTP, for example,",
            "   attacks where compressed content includes both attacker-controlled",
            "   plaintext and secret data (e.g., [BREACH]).",
            "",
            "   Where HTTP/2 employs PADDING frames and Padding fields in other",
            "   frames to make a connection more resistant to traffic analysis,",
            "   HTTP/3 can either rely on transport-layer padding or employ the",
            "   reserved frame and stream types discussed in Sections 7.2.8 and",
            "   6.2.3.  These methods of padding produce different results in terms",
            "   of the granularity of padding, how padding is arranged in relation to",
            "   the information that is being protected, whether padding is applied",
            "   in the case of packet loss, and how an implementation might control",
            "   padding.",
            "",
            "   Reserved stream types can be used to give the appearance of sending",
            "   traffic even when the connection is idle.  Because HTTP traffic often",
            "   occurs in bursts, apparent traffic can be used to obscure the timing",
            "   or duration of such bursts, even to the point of appearing to send a",
            "   constant stream of data.  However, as such traffic is still flow",
            "   controlled by the receiver, a failure to promptly drain such streams",
            "   and provide additional flow-control credit can limit the sender's",
            "   ability to send real traffic.",
            "",
            "   To mitigate attacks that rely on compression, disabling or limiting",
            "   compression might be preferable to padding as a countermeasure.",
            "",
            "   Use of padding can result in less protection than might seem",
            "   immediately obvious.  Redundant padding could even be",
            "   counterproductive.  At best, padding only makes it more difficult for",
            "   an attacker to infer length information by increasing the number of",
            "   frames an attacker has to observe.  Incorrectly implemented padding",
            "   schemes can be easily defeated.  In particular, randomized padding",
            "   with a predictable distribution provides very little protection;",
            "   similarly, padding payloads to a fixed size exposes information as",
            "   payload sizes cross the fixed-sized boundary, which could be possible",
            "   if an attacker can control plaintext."
          ],
          "title": "Padding and Traffic Analysis"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.8",
          "lines": [
            "   Several protocol elements contain nested length elements, typically",
            "   in the form of frames with an explicit length containing variable-",
            "   length integers.  This could pose a security risk to an incautious",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   implementer.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "874937aef87606e1",
                  "b142a05de43183ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "An implementation MUST ensure that the length of a"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "874937aef87606e1",
                  "b142a05de43183ab"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "frame exactly matches the length of the fields it contains."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "b142a05de43183ab",
            "b142a05de43183ab"
          ],
          "title": "Frame Parsing"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.9",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b4637c2dbad23de"
                ],
                "status_id": 12,
                "text": "The use of 0-RTT with HTTP/3 creates an exposure to replay attack."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b4637c2dbad23de",
                  "5669030a63845ea1"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "The anti-replay mitigations in [HTTP-REPLAY] MUST be applied when"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2b4637c2dbad23de",
                  "5669030a63845ea1"
                ],
                "status_id": 9,
                "text": "using HTTP/3 with 0-RTT."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  When applying [HTTP-REPLAY] to HTTP/3,"
              }
            ],
            "   references to the TLS layer refer to the handshake performed within",
            "   QUIC, while all references to application data refer to the contents",
            "   of streams."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "5669030a63845ea1",
            "5669030a63845ea1"
          ],
          "title": "Early Data"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.10",
          "lines": [
            "   Certain HTTP implementations use the client address for logging or",
            "   access-control purposes.  Since a QUIC client's address might change",
            "   during a connection (and future versions might support simultaneous",
            "   use of multiple addresses), such implementations will need to either",
            "   actively retrieve the client's current address or addresses when they",
            "   are relevant or explicitly accept that the original address might",
            "   change."
          ],
          "title": "Migration"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-10.11",
          "lines": [
            "   Several characteristics of HTTP/3 provide an observer an opportunity",
            "   to correlate actions of a single client or server over time.  These",
            "   include the value of settings, the timing of reactions to stimulus,",
            "   and the handling of any features that are controlled by settings.",
            "",
            "   As far as these create observable differences in behavior, they could",
            "   be used as a basis for fingerprinting a specific client.",
            "",
            "   HTTP/3's preference for using a single QUIC connection allows",
            "   correlation of a user's activity on a site.  Reusing connections for",
            "   different origins allows for correlation of activity across those",
            "   origins.",
            "",
            "   Several features of QUIC solicit immediate responses and can be used",
            "   by an endpoint to measure latency to their peer; this might have",
            "   privacy implications in certain scenarios."
          ],
          "title": "Privacy Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11",
          "lines": [
            "   This document registers a new ALPN protocol ID (Section 11.1) and",
            "   creates new registries that manage the assignment of code points in",
            "   HTTP/3."
          ],
          "title": "IANA Considerations"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11.1",
          "lines": [
            "   This document creates a new registration for the identification of",
            "   HTTP/3 in the \"TLS Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation (ALPN)",
            "   Protocol IDs\" registry established in [RFC7301].",
            "",
            "   The \"h3\" string identifies HTTP/3:",
            "",
            "   Protocol:  HTTP/3",
            "",
            "   Identification Sequence:  0x68 0x33 (\"h3\")",
            "",
            "   Specification:  This document"
          ],
          "title": "Registration of HTTP/3 Identification String"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11.2",
          "lines": [
            "   New registries created in this document operate under the QUIC",
            "   registration policy documented in Section 22.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].",
            "   These registries all include the common set of fields listed in",
            "   Section 22.1.1 of [QUIC-TRANSPORT].  These registries are collected",
            "   under the \"Hypertext Transfer Protocol version 3 (HTTP/3)\" heading.",
            "",
            "   The initial allocations in these registries are all assigned",
            "   permanent status and list a change controller of the IETF and a",
            "   contact of the HTTP working group (ietf-http-wg@w3.org)."
          ],
          "title": "New Registries"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   This document establishes a registry for HTTP/3 frame type codes.",
            "   The \"HTTP/3 Frame Types\" registry governs a 62-bit space.  This",
            "   registry follows the QUIC registry policy; see Section 11.2.",
            "   Permanent registrations in this registry are assigned using the",
            "   Specification Required policy ([RFC8126]), except for values between",
            "   0x00 and 0x3f (in hexadecimal; inclusive), which are assigned using",
            "   Standards Action or IESG Approval as defined in Sections 4.9 and 4.10",
            "   of [RFC8126].",
            "",
            "   While this registry is separate from the \"HTTP/2 Frame Type\" registry",
            "   defined in [HTTP/2], it is preferable that the assignments parallel",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   each other where the code spaces overlap.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "38928d3bb7612f7a",
                  "dc593cff92109e95"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If an entry is present in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "38928d3bb7612f7a",
                  "dc593cff92109e95"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "only one registry, every effort SHOULD be made to avoid assigning the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "38928d3bb7612f7a",
                  "dc593cff92109e95"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "corresponding value to an unrelated operation."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2fbe4bd25f5fc64f",
                  "c2dc09c81ad996e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Expert reviewers MAY"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2fbe4bd25f5fc64f",
                  "c2dc09c81ad996e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "reject unrelated registrations that would conflict with the same"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "2fbe4bd25f5fc64f",
                  "c2dc09c81ad996e8"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "value in the corresponding registry."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd9cd268ec86e812",
                  "096132a5c58e3b8f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd9cd268ec86e812",
                  "096132a5c58e3b8f"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "registrations in this registry MUST include the following field:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "cd9cd268ec86e812"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Frame Type:  A name or label for the frame type."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2dad16d0d77680e",
                  "89c93d2581c06224"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Specifications of frame types MUST include a description of the frame"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2dad16d0d77680e",
                  "89c93d2581c06224"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "layout and its semantics, including any parts of the frame that are"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "d2dad16d0d77680e",
                  "89c93d2581c06224"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "conditionally present."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The entries in Table 2 are registered by this document.",
            "",
            "                 +==============+=======+===============+",
            "                 | Frame Type   | Value | Specification |",
            "                 +==============+=======+===============+",
            "                 | DATA         |  0x00 | Section 7.2.1 |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | HEADERS      |  0x01 | Section 7.2.2 |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | Reserved     |  0x02 | This document |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | CANCEL_PUSH  |  0x03 | Section 7.2.3 |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | SETTINGS     |  0x04 | Section 7.2.4 |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | PUSH_PROMISE |  0x05 | Section 7.2.5 |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | Reserved     |  0x06 | This document |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | GOAWAY       |  0x07 | Section 7.2.6 |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | Reserved     |  0x08 | This document |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | Reserved     |  0x09 | This document |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "                 | MAX_PUSH_ID  |  0x0d | Section 7.2.7 |",
            "                 +--------------+-------+---------------+",
            "",
            "                   Table 2: Initial HTTP/3 Frame Types",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d6ff86b8878eacb",
                  "6ec25ca053820271"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d6ff86b8878eacb",
                  "6ec25ca053820271"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d6ff86b8878eacb",
                  "6ec25ca053820271"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "5d6ff86b8878eacb",
                  "6ec25ca053820271"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "assigned values."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "dc593cff92109e95",
            "dc593cff92109e95",
            "dc593cff92109e95",
            "c2dc09c81ad996e8",
            "c2dc09c81ad996e8",
            "c2dc09c81ad996e8",
            "096132a5c58e3b8f",
            "096132a5c58e3b8f",
            "89c93d2581c06224",
            "89c93d2581c06224",
            "89c93d2581c06224",
            "6ec25ca053820271",
            "6ec25ca053820271",
            "6ec25ca053820271",
            "6ec25ca053820271"
          ],
          "title": "Frame Types"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11.2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   This document establishes a registry for HTTP/3 settings.  The",
            "   \"HTTP/3 Settings\" registry governs a 62-bit space.  This registry",
            "   follows the QUIC registry policy; see Section 11.2.  Permanent",
            "   registrations in this registry are assigned using the Specification",
            "   Required policy ([RFC8126]), except for values between 0x00 and 0x3f",
            "   (in hexadecimal; inclusive), which are assigned using Standards",
            "   Action or IESG Approval as defined in Sections 4.9 and 4.10 of",
            "   [RFC8126].",
            "",
            "   While this registry is separate from the \"HTTP/2 Settings\" registry",
            "   defined in [HTTP/2], it is preferable that the assignments parallel",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   each other.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "83e4295d21417b1f",
                  "759b4ce0dda185a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "If an entry is present in only one registry, every"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "83e4295d21417b1f",
                  "759b4ce0dda185a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "effort SHOULD be made to avoid assigning the corresponding value to"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "83e4295d21417b1f",
                  "759b4ce0dda185a8"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "an unrelated operation."
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6a3a99106bbab454",
                  "fb055d725135fceb"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Expert reviewers MAY reject unrelated"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6a3a99106bbab454",
                  "fb055d725135fceb"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "registrations that would conflict with the same value in the"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "6a3a99106bbab454",
                  "fb055d725135fceb"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "corresponding registry."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e3a1c102e5f4d29d",
                  "2c04635e729dfcae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e3a1c102e5f4d29d",
                  "2c04635e729dfcae"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "registrations in this registry MUST include the following fields:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e3a1c102e5f4d29d"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Setting Name:  A symbolic name for the setting.  Specifying a setting"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "e3a1c102e5f4d29d"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "name is optional."
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70eee5eb6c38b250"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Default:  The value of the setting unless otherwise indicated.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70eee5eb6c38b250"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "A"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "      "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "70eee5eb6c38b250",
                  "e04bee38d4e7a32c"
                ],
                "status_id": 3,
                "text": "default SHOULD be the most restrictive possible value."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The entries in Table 3 are registered by this document.",
            "",
            "     +========================+=======+=================+===========+",
            "     | Setting Name           | Value | Specification   | Default   |",
            "     +========================+=======+=================+===========+",
            "     | Reserved               |  0x00 | This document   | N/A       |",
            "     +------------------------+-------+-----------------+-----------+",
            "     | Reserved               |  0x02 | This document   | N/A       |",
            "     +------------------------+-------+-----------------+-----------+",
            "     | Reserved               |  0x03 | This document   | N/A       |",
            "     +------------------------+-------+-----------------+-----------+",
            "     | Reserved               |  0x04 | This document   | N/A       |",
            "     +------------------------+-------+-----------------+-----------+",
            "     | Reserved               |  0x05 | This document   | N/A       |",
            "     +------------------------+-------+-----------------+-----------+",
            "     | MAX_FIELD_SECTION_SIZE |  0x06 | Section 7.2.4.1 | Unlimited |",
            "     +------------------------+-------+-----------------+-----------+",
            "",
            "                     Table 3: Initial HTTP/3 Settings",
            "",
            "   For formatting reasons, setting names can be abbreviated by removing",
            "   the 'SETTINGS_' prefix.",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc3ec3bb6a5b0ad0",
                  "a3845b8fd1708627"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc3ec3bb6a5b0ad0",
                  "a3845b8fd1708627"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc3ec3bb6a5b0ad0",
                  "a3845b8fd1708627"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "bc3ec3bb6a5b0ad0",
                  "a3845b8fd1708627"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "assigned values."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "759b4ce0dda185a8",
            "759b4ce0dda185a8",
            "759b4ce0dda185a8",
            "fb055d725135fceb",
            "fb055d725135fceb",
            "fb055d725135fceb",
            "2c04635e729dfcae",
            "2c04635e729dfcae",
            "e04bee38d4e7a32c",
            "e04bee38d4e7a32c",
            "a3845b8fd1708627",
            "a3845b8fd1708627",
            "a3845b8fd1708627",
            "a3845b8fd1708627"
          ],
          "title": "Settings Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11.2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   This document establishes a registry for HTTP/3 error codes.  The",
            "   \"HTTP/3 Error Codes\" registry manages a 62-bit space.  This registry",
            "   follows the QUIC registry policy; see Section 11.2.  Permanent",
            "   registrations in this registry are assigned using the Specification",
            "   Required policy ([RFC8126]), except for values between 0x00 and 0x3f",
            "   (in hexadecimal; inclusive), which are assigned using Standards",
            "   Action or IESG Approval as defined in Sections 4.9 and 4.10 of",
            "   [RFC8126].",
            "",
            "   Registrations for error codes are required to include a description",
            "   of the error code.  An expert reviewer is advised to examine new",
            "   registrations for possible duplication with existing error codes.",
            "   Use of existing registrations is to be encouraged, but not mandated.",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "102e356af49f054c",
                  "d4fd7430fbe2c4c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "Use of values that are registered in the \"HTTP/2 Error Code\" registry"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "102e356af49f054c",
                  "d4fd7430fbe2c4c3"
                ],
                "status_id": 2,
                "text": "is discouraged, and expert reviewers MAY reject such registrations."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, this",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   registry includes two additional fields.  "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fda8e3e12e46b03c",
                  "01051a80bd783957"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Permanent registrations in"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fda8e3e12e46b03c",
                  "01051a80bd783957"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "this registry MUST include the following field:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "fda8e3e12e46b03c"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Name:  A name for the error code."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Description:  A brief description of the error code semantics.",
            "",
            "   The entries in Table 4 are registered by this document.  These error",
            "   codes were selected from the range that operates on a Specification",
            "   Required policy to avoid collisions with HTTP/2 error codes.",
            "",
            "   +===========================+========+==============+===============+",
            "   | Name                      | Value  | Description  | Specification |",
            "   +===========================+========+==============+===============+",
            "   | H3_NO_ERROR               | 0x0100 | No error     | Section 8.1   |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_GENERAL_PROTOCOL_ERROR | 0x0101 | General      | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | protocol     |               |",
            "   |                           |        | error        |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_INTERNAL_ERROR         | 0x0102 | Internal     | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | error        |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_STREAM_CREATION_ERROR  | 0x0103 | Stream       | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | creation     |               |",
            "   |                           |        | error        |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_CLOSED_CRITICAL_STREAM | 0x0104 | Critical     | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | stream was   |               |",
            "   |                           |        | closed       |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED       | 0x0105 | Frame not    | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | permitted    |               |",
            "   |                           |        | in the       |               |",
            "   |                           |        | current      |               |",
            "   |                           |        | state        |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_FRAME_ERROR            | 0x0106 | Frame        | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | violated     |               |",
            "   |                           |        | layout or    |               |",
            "   |                           |        | size rules   |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_EXCESSIVE_LOAD         | 0x0107 | Peer         | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | generating   |               |",
            "   |                           |        | excessive    |               |",
            "   |                           |        | load         |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_ID_ERROR               | 0x0108 | An           | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | identifier   |               |",
            "   |                           |        | was used     |               |",
            "   |                           |        | incorrectly  |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_SETTINGS_ERROR         | 0x0109 | SETTINGS     | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | frame        |               |",
            "   |                           |        | contained    |               |",
            "   |                           |        | invalid      |               |",
            "   |                           |        | values       |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_MISSING_SETTINGS       | 0x010a | No SETTINGS  | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | frame        |               |",
            "   |                           |        | received     |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_REQUEST_REJECTED       | 0x010b | Request not  | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | processed    |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED      | 0x010c | Data no      | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | longer       |               |",
            "   |                           |        | needed       |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_REQUEST_INCOMPLETE     | 0x010d | Stream       | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | terminated   |               |",
            "   |                           |        | early        |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_MESSAGE_ERROR          | 0x010e | Malformed    | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | message      |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_CONNECT_ERROR          | 0x010f | TCP reset    | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | or error on  |               |",
            "   |                           |        | CONNECT      |               |",
            "   |                           |        | request      |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "   | H3_VERSION_FALLBACK       | 0x0110 | Retry over   | Section 8.1   |",
            "   |                           |        | HTTP/1.1     |               |",
            "   +---------------------------+--------+--------------+---------------+",
            "",
            "                    Table 4: Initial HTTP/3 Error Codes",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a2c0a33fca49024",
                  "0f5362612bfe2296"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a2c0a33fca49024",
                  "0f5362612bfe2296"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a2c0a33fca49024",
                  "0f5362612bfe2296"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "0a2c0a33fca49024",
                  "0f5362612bfe2296"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "assigned values."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "d4fd7430fbe2c4c3",
            "d4fd7430fbe2c4c3",
            "01051a80bd783957",
            "01051a80bd783957",
            "0f5362612bfe2296",
            "0f5362612bfe2296",
            "0f5362612bfe2296",
            "0f5362612bfe2296"
          ],
          "title": "Error Codes"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-11.2.4",
          "lines": [
            "   This document establishes a registry for HTTP/3 unidirectional stream",
            "   types.  The \"HTTP/3 Stream Types\" registry governs a 62-bit space.",
            "   This registry follows the QUIC registry policy; see Section 11.2.",
            "   Permanent registrations in this registry are assigned using the",
            "   Specification Required policy ([RFC8126]), except for values between",
            "   0x00 and 0x3f (in hexadecimal; inclusive), which are assigned using",
            "   Standards Action or IESG Approval as defined in Sections 4.9 and 4.10",
            "   of [RFC8126].",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a5c239049088071",
                  "f636c659de02009b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "In addition to common fields as described in Section 11.2, permanent"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a5c239049088071",
                  "f636c659de02009b"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "registrations in this registry MUST include the following fields:"
              }
            ],
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "3a5c239049088071"
                ],
                "status_id": 4,
                "text": "Stream Type:  A name or label for the stream type."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   Sender:  Which endpoint on an HTTP/3 connection may initiate a stream",
            "      of this type.  Values are \"Client\", \"Server\", or \"Both\".",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30be05c14c3a81c5",
                  "4245ef3af964e5bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Specifications for permanent registrations MUST include a description"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30be05c14c3a81c5",
                  "4245ef3af964e5bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "of the stream type, including the layout and semantics of the stream"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "30be05c14c3a81c5",
                  "4245ef3af964e5bf"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "contents."
              }
            ],
            "",
            "   The entries in Table 5 are registered by this document.",
            "",
            "            +================+=======+===============+========+",
            "            | Stream Type    | Value | Specification | Sender |",
            "            +================+=======+===============+========+",
            "            | Control Stream |  0x00 | Section 6.2.1 | Both   |",
            "            +----------------+-------+---------------+--------+",
            "            | Push Stream    |  0x01 | Section 4.6   | Server |",
            "            +----------------+-------+---------------+--------+",
            "",
            "                       Table 5: Initial Stream Types",
            "",
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ce69f635e6db5cf0",
                  "147e3d8a2c356e17"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "Each code of the format 0x1f * N + 0x21 for non-negative integer"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ce69f635e6db5cf0",
                  "147e3d8a2c356e17"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "values of N (that is, 0x21, 0x40, ..., through 0x3ffffffffffffffe)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ce69f635e6db5cf0",
                  "147e3d8a2c356e17"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "MUST NOT be assigned by IANA and MUST NOT appear in the listing of"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "annotation_ids": [],
                "status_id": 0,
                "text": "   "
              },
              {
                "annotation_ids": [
                  "ce69f635e6db5cf0",
                  "147e3d8a2c356e17"
                ],
                "status_id": 1,
                "text": "assigned values."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "f636c659de02009b",
            "f636c659de02009b",
            "4245ef3af964e5bf",
            "4245ef3af964e5bf",
            "4245ef3af964e5bf",
            "147e3d8a2c356e17",
            "147e3d8a2c356e17",
            "147e3d8a2c356e17",
            "147e3d8a2c356e17"
          ],
          "title": "Stream Types"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-12",
          "lines": [],
          "title": "References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-12.1",
          "lines": [
            "   [ALTSVC]   Nottingham, M., McManus, P., and J. Reschke, \"HTTP",
            "              Alternative Services\", RFC 7838, DOI 10.17487/RFC7838,",
            "              April 2016, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7838>.",
            "",
            "   [COOKIES]  Barth, A., \"HTTP State Management Mechanism\", RFC 6265,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC6265, April 2011,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc6265>.",
            "",
            "   [HTTP]     Fielding, R., Ed., Nottingham, M., Ed., and J. Reschke,",
            "              Ed., \"HTTP Semantics\", STD 97, RFC 9110,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC9110, June 2022,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9110>.",
            "",
            "   [HTTP-CACHING]",
            "              Fielding, R., Ed., Nottingham, M., Ed., and J. Reschke,",
            "              Ed., \"HTTP Caching\", STD 98, RFC 9111,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC9111, June 2022,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9111>.",
            "",
            "   [HTTP-REPLAY]",
            "              Thomson, M., Nottingham, M., and W. Tarreau, \"Using Early",
            "              Data in HTTP\", RFC 8470, DOI 10.17487/RFC8470, September",
            "              2018, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8470>.",
            "",
            "   [QPACK]    Krasic, C., Bishop, M., and A. Frindell, Ed., \"QPACK:",
            "              Field Compression for HTTP/3\", RFC 9204,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC9204, June 2022,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9204>.",
            "",
            "   [QUIC-TRANSPORT]",
            "              Iyengar, J., Ed. and M. Thomson, Ed., \"QUIC: A UDP-Based",
            "              Multiplexed and Secure Transport\", RFC 9000,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC9000, May 2021,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9000>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC0793]  Postel, J., \"Transmission Control Protocol\", STD 7,",
            "              RFC 793, DOI 10.17487/RFC0793, September 1981,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc793>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC2119]  Bradner, S., \"Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate",
            "              Requirement Levels\", BCP 14, RFC 2119,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC2119, March 1997,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2119>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC6066]  Eastlake 3rd, D., \"Transport Layer Security (TLS)",
            "              Extensions: Extension Definitions\", RFC 6066,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC6066, January 2011,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc6066>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC7301]  Friedl, S., Popov, A., Langley, A., and E. Stephan,",
            "              \"Transport Layer Security (TLS) Application-Layer Protocol",
            "              Negotiation Extension\", RFC 7301, DOI 10.17487/RFC7301,",
            "              July 2014, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7301>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC8126]  Cotton, M., Leiba, B., and T. Narten, \"Guidelines for",
            "              Writing an IANA Considerations Section in RFCs\", BCP 26,",
            "              RFC 8126, DOI 10.17487/RFC8126, June 2017,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8126>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC8174]  Leiba, B., \"Ambiguity of Uppercase vs Lowercase in RFC",
            "              2119 Key Words\", BCP 14, RFC 8174, DOI 10.17487/RFC8174,",
            "              May 2017, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8174>.",
            "",
            "   [URI]      Berners-Lee, T., Fielding, R., and L. Masinter, \"Uniform",
            "              Resource Identifier (URI): Generic Syntax\", STD 66,",
            "              RFC 3986, DOI 10.17487/RFC3986, January 2005,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc3986>."
          ],
          "title": "Normative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "section-12.2",
          "lines": [
            "   [BREACH]   Gluck, Y., Harris, N., and A. Prado, \"BREACH: Reviving the",
            "              CRIME Attack\", July 2013,",
            "              <http://breachattack.com/resources/",
            "              BREACH%20-%20SSL,%20gone%20in%2030%20seconds.pdf>.",
            "",
            "   [DNS-TERMS]",
            "              Hoffman, P., Sullivan, A., and K. Fujiwara, \"DNS",
            "              Terminology\", BCP 219, RFC 8499, DOI 10.17487/RFC8499,",
            "              January 2019, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8499>.",
            "",
            "   [HPACK]    Peon, R. and H. Ruellan, \"HPACK: Header Compression for",
            "              HTTP/2\", RFC 7541, DOI 10.17487/RFC7541, May 2015,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7541>.",
            "",
            "   [HTTP/1.1] Fielding, R., Ed., Nottingham, M., Ed., and J. Reschke,",
            "              Ed., \"HTTP/1.1\", STD 99, RFC 9112, DOI 10.17487/RFC9112,",
            "              June 2022, <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9112>.",
            "",
            "   [HTTP/2]   Thomson, M., Ed. and C. Benfield, Ed., \"HTTP/2\", RFC 9113,",
            "              DOI 10.17487/RFC9113, June 2022,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9113>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC6585]  Nottingham, M. and R. Fielding, \"Additional HTTP Status",
            "              Codes\", RFC 6585, DOI 10.17487/RFC6585, April 2012,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc6585>.",
            "",
            "   [RFC8164]  Nottingham, M. and M. Thomson, \"Opportunistic Security for",
            "              HTTP/2\", RFC 8164, DOI 10.17487/RFC8164, May 2017,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8164>.",
            "",
            "   [TFO]      Cheng, Y., Chu, J., Radhakrishnan, S., and A. Jain, \"TCP",
            "              Fast Open\", RFC 7413, DOI 10.17487/RFC7413, December 2014,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7413>.",
            "",
            "   [TLS]      Rescorla, E., \"The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol",
            "              Version 1.3\", RFC 8446, DOI 10.17487/RFC8446, August 2018,",
            "              <https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc8446>."
          ],
          "title": "Informative References"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/3 is strongly informed by HTTP/2, and it bears many",
            "   similarities.  This section describes the approach taken to design",
            "   HTTP/3, points out important differences from HTTP/2, and describes",
            "   how to map HTTP/2 extensions into HTTP/3.",
            "",
            "   HTTP/3 begins from the premise that similarity to HTTP/2 is",
            "   preferable, but not a hard requirement.  HTTP/3 departs from HTTP/2",
            "   where QUIC differs from TCP, either to take advantage of QUIC",
            "   features (like streams) or to accommodate important shortcomings",
            "   (such as a lack of total ordering).  While HTTP/3 is similar to",
            "   HTTP/2 in key aspects, such as the relationship of requests and",
            "   responses to streams, the details of the HTTP/3 design are",
            "   substantially different from HTTP/2.",
            "",
            "   Some important departures are noted in this section."
          ],
          "title": "Considerations for Transitioning from HTTP/2"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.1",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/3 permits use of a larger number of streams (2^62-1) than",
            "   HTTP/2.  The same considerations about exhaustion of stream",
            "   identifier space apply, though the space is significantly larger such",
            "   that it is likely that other limits in QUIC are reached first, such",
            "   as the limit on the connection flow-control window.",
            "",
            "   In contrast to HTTP/2, stream concurrency in HTTP/3 is managed by",
            "   QUIC.  QUIC considers a stream closed when all data has been received",
            "   and sent data has been acknowledged by the peer.  HTTP/2 considers a",
            "   stream closed when the frame containing the END_STREAM bit has been",
            "   committed to the transport.  As a result, the stream for an",
            "   equivalent exchange could remain \"active\" for a longer period of",
            "   time.  HTTP/3 servers might choose to permit a larger number of",
            "   concurrent client-initiated bidirectional streams to achieve",
            "   equivalent concurrency to HTTP/2, depending on the expected usage",
            "   patterns.",
            "",
            "   In HTTP/2, only request and response bodies (the frame payload of",
            "   DATA frames) are subject to flow control.  All HTTP/3 frames are sent",
            "   on QUIC streams, so all frames on all streams are flow controlled in",
            "   HTTP/3.",
            "",
            "   Due to the presence of other unidirectional stream types, HTTP/3 does",
            "   not rely exclusively on the number of concurrent unidirectional",
            "   streams to control the number of concurrent in-flight pushes.",
            "   Instead, HTTP/3 clients use the MAX_PUSH_ID frame to control the",
            "   number of pushes received from an HTTP/3 server."
          ],
          "title": "Streams"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2",
          "lines": [
            "   Many framing concepts from HTTP/2 can be elided on QUIC, because the",
            "   transport deals with them.  Because frames are already on a stream,",
            "   they can omit the stream number.  Because frames do not block",
            "   multiplexing (QUIC's multiplexing occurs below this layer), the",
            "   support for variable-maximum-length packets can be removed.  Because",
            "   stream termination is handled by QUIC, an END_STREAM flag is not",
            "   required.  This permits the removal of the Flags field from the",
            "   generic frame layout.",
            "",
            "   Frame payloads are largely drawn from [HTTP/2].  However, QUIC",
            "   includes many features (e.g., flow control) that are also present in",
            "   HTTP/2.  In these cases, the HTTP mapping does not re-implement them.",
            "   As a result, several HTTP/2 frame types are not required in HTTP/3.",
            "   Where an HTTP/2-defined frame is no longer used, the frame ID has",
            "   been reserved in order to maximize portability between HTTP/2 and",
            "   HTTP/3 implementations.  However, even frame types that appear in",
            "   both mappings do not have identical semantics.",
            "",
            "   Many of the differences arise from the fact that HTTP/2 provides an",
            "   absolute ordering between frames across all streams, while QUIC",
            "   provides this guarantee on each stream only.  As a result, if a frame",
            "   type makes assumptions that frames from different streams will still",
            "   be received in the order sent, HTTP/3 will break them.",
            "",
            "   Some examples of feature adaptations are described below, as well as",
            "   general guidance to extension frame implementors converting an HTTP/2",
            "   extension to HTTP/3."
          ],
          "title": "HTTP Frame Types"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2.1",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/2 specifies priority assignments in PRIORITY frames and",
            "   (optionally) in HEADERS frames.  HTTP/3 does not provide a means of",
            "   signaling priority.",
            "",
            "   Note that, while there is no explicit signaling for priority, this",
            "   does not mean that prioritization is not important for achieving good",
            "   performance."
          ],
          "title": "Prioritization Differences"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2.2",
          "lines": [
            "   HPACK was designed with the assumption of in-order delivery.  A",
            "   sequence of encoded field sections must arrive (and be decoded) at an",
            "   endpoint in the same order in which they were encoded.  This ensures",
            "   that the dynamic state at the two endpoints remains in sync.",
            "",
            "   Because this total ordering is not provided by QUIC, HTTP/3 uses a",
            "   modified version of HPACK, called QPACK.  QPACK uses a single",
            "   unidirectional stream to make all modifications to the dynamic table,",
            "   ensuring a total order of updates.  All frames that contain encoded",
            "   fields merely reference the table state at a given time without",
            "   modifying it.",
            "",
            "   [QPACK] provides additional details."
          ],
          "title": "Field Compression Differences"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2.3",
          "lines": [
            "   HTTP/2 specifies a stream flow-control mechanism.  Although all",
            "   HTTP/2 frames are delivered on streams, only the DATA frame payload",
            "   is subject to flow control.  QUIC provides flow control for stream",
            "   data and all HTTP/3 frame types defined in this document are sent on",
            "   streams.  Therefore, all frame headers and payload are subject to",
            "   flow control."
          ],
          "title": "Flow-Control Differences"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2.4",
          "lines": [
            "   Frame type definitions in HTTP/3 often use the QUIC variable-length",
            "   integer encoding.  In particular, stream IDs use this encoding, which",
            "   allows for a larger range of possible values than the encoding used",
            "   in HTTP/2.  Some frames in HTTP/3 use an identifier other than a",
            "   stream ID (e.g., push IDs).  Redefinition of the encoding of",
            "   extension frame types might be necessary if the encoding includes a",
            "   stream ID.",
            "",
            "   Because the Flags field is not present in generic HTTP/3 frames,",
            "   those frames that depend on the presence of flags need to allocate",
            "   space for flags as part of their frame payload.",
            "",
            "   Other than these issues, frame type HTTP/2 extensions are typically",
            "   portable to QUIC simply by replacing stream 0 in HTTP/2 with a",
            "   control stream in HTTP/3.  HTTP/3 extensions will not assume",
            "   ordering, but would not be harmed by ordering, and are expected to be",
            "   portable to HTTP/2."
          ],
          "title": "Guidance for New Frame Type Definitions"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.2.5",
          "lines": [
            "   DATA (0x00):  Padding is not defined in HTTP/3 frames.  See",
            "      Section 7.2.1.",
            "",
            "   HEADERS (0x01):  The PRIORITY region of HEADERS is not defined in",
            "      HTTP/3 frames.  Padding is not defined in HTTP/3 frames.  See",
            "      Section 7.2.2.",
            "",
            "   PRIORITY (0x02):  As described in Appendix A.2.1, HTTP/3 does not",
            "      provide a means of signaling priority.",
            "",
            "   RST_STREAM (0x03):  RST_STREAM frames do not exist in HTTP/3, since",
            "      QUIC provides stream lifecycle management.  The same code point is",
            "      used for the CANCEL_PUSH frame (Section 7.2.3).",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS (0x04):  SETTINGS frames are sent only at the beginning of",
            "      the connection.  See Section 7.2.4 and Appendix A.3.",
            "",
            "   PUSH_PROMISE (0x05):  The PUSH_PROMISE frame does not reference a",
            "      stream; instead, the push stream references the PUSH_PROMISE frame",
            "      using a push ID.  See Section 7.2.5.",
            "",
            "   PING (0x06):  PING frames do not exist in HTTP/3, as QUIC provides",
            "      equivalent functionality.",
            "",
            "   GOAWAY (0x07):  GOAWAY does not contain an error code.  In the",
            "      client-to-server direction, it carries a push ID instead of a",
            "      server-initiated stream ID.  See Section 7.2.6.",
            "",
            "   WINDOW_UPDATE (0x08):  WINDOW_UPDATE frames do not exist in HTTP/3,",
            "      since QUIC provides flow control.",
            "",
            "   CONTINUATION (0x09):  CONTINUATION frames do not exist in HTTP/3;",
            "      instead, larger HEADERS/PUSH_PROMISE frames than HTTP/2 are",
            "      permitted.",
            "",
            "   Frame types defined by extensions to HTTP/2 need to be separately",
            "   registered for HTTP/3 if still applicable.  The IDs of frames defined",
            "   in [HTTP/2] have been reserved for simplicity.  Note that the frame",
            "   type space in HTTP/3 is substantially larger (62 bits versus 8 bits),",
            "   so many HTTP/3 frame types have no equivalent HTTP/2 code points.",
            "   See Section 11.2.1."
          ],
          "title": "Comparison of HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 Frame Types"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.3",
          "lines": [
            "   An important difference from HTTP/2 is that settings are sent once,",
            "   as the first frame of the control stream, and thereafter cannot",
            "   change.  This eliminates many corner cases around synchronization of",
            "   changes.",
            "",
            "   Some transport-level options that HTTP/2 specifies via the SETTINGS",
            "   frame are superseded by QUIC transport parameters in HTTP/3.  The",
            "   HTTP-level setting that is retained in HTTP/3 has the same value as",
            "   in HTTP/2.  The superseded settings are reserved, and their receipt",
            "   is an error.  See Section 7.2.4.1 for discussion of both the retained",
            "   and reserved values.",
            "",
            "   Below is a listing of how each HTTP/2 SETTINGS parameter is mapped:",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE (0x01):  See [QPACK].",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS_ENABLE_PUSH (0x02):  This is removed in favor of the",
            "      MAX_PUSH_ID frame, which provides a more granular control over",
            "      server push.  Specifying a setting with the identifier 0x02",
            "      (corresponding to the SETTINGS_ENABLE_PUSH parameter) in the",
            "      HTTP/3 SETTINGS frame is an error.",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS_MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS (0x03):  QUIC controls the largest",
            "      open stream ID as part of its flow-control logic.  Specifying a",
            "      setting with the identifier 0x03 (corresponding to the",
            "      SETTINGS_MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS parameter) in the HTTP/3 SETTINGS",
            "      frame is an error.",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE (0x04):  QUIC requires both stream and",
            "      connection flow-control window sizes to be specified in the",
            "      initial transport handshake.  Specifying a setting with the",
            "      identifier 0x04 (corresponding to the SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE",
            "      parameter) in the HTTP/3 SETTINGS frame is an error.",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE (0x05):  This setting has no equivalent in",
            "      HTTP/3.  Specifying a setting with the identifier 0x05",
            "      (corresponding to the SETTINGS_MAX_FRAME_SIZE parameter) in the",
            "      HTTP/3 SETTINGS frame is an error.",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS_MAX_HEADER_LIST_SIZE (0x06):  This setting identifier has",
            "      been renamed SETTINGS_MAX_FIELD_SECTION_SIZE.",
            "",
            "   In HTTP/3, setting values are variable-length integers (6, 14, 30, or",
            "   62 bits long) rather than fixed-length 32-bit fields as in HTTP/2.",
            "   This will often produce a shorter encoding, but can produce a longer",
            "   encoding for settings that use the full 32-bit space.  Settings",
            "   ported from HTTP/2 might choose to redefine their value to limit it",
            "   to 30 bits for more efficient encoding or to make use of the 62-bit",
            "   space if more than 30 bits are required.",
            "",
            "   Settings need to be defined separately for HTTP/2 and HTTP/3.  The",
            "   IDs of settings defined in [HTTP/2] have been reserved for",
            "   simplicity.  Note that the settings identifier space in HTTP/3 is",
            "   substantially larger (62 bits versus 16 bits), so many HTTP/3",
            "   settings have no equivalent HTTP/2 code point.  See Section 11.2.2.",
            "",
            "   As QUIC streams might arrive out of order, endpoints are advised not",
            "   to wait for the peers' settings to arrive before responding to other",
            "   streams.  See Section 7.2.4.2."
          ],
          "title": "HTTP/2 SETTINGS Parameters"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.4",
          "lines": [
            "   QUIC has the same concepts of \"stream\" and \"connection\" errors that",
            "   HTTP/2 provides.  However, the differences between HTTP/2 and HTTP/3",
            "   mean that error codes are not directly portable between versions.",
            "",
            "   The HTTP/2 error codes defined in Section 7 of [HTTP/2] logically map",
            "   to the HTTP/3 error codes as follows:",
            "",
            "   NO_ERROR (0x00):  H3_NO_ERROR in Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   PROTOCOL_ERROR (0x01):  This is mapped to H3_GENERAL_PROTOCOL_ERROR",
            "      except in cases where more specific error codes have been defined.",
            "      Such cases include H3_FRAME_UNEXPECTED, H3_MESSAGE_ERROR, and",
            "      H3_CLOSED_CRITICAL_STREAM defined in Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   INTERNAL_ERROR (0x02):  H3_INTERNAL_ERROR in Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR (0x03):  Not applicable, since QUIC handles flow",
            "      control.",
            "",
            "   SETTINGS_TIMEOUT (0x04):  Not applicable, since no acknowledgment of",
            "      SETTINGS is defined.",
            "",
            "   STREAM_CLOSED (0x05):  Not applicable, since QUIC handles stream",
            "      management.",
            "",
            "   FRAME_SIZE_ERROR (0x06):  H3_FRAME_ERROR error code defined in",
            "      Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   REFUSED_STREAM (0x07):  H3_REQUEST_REJECTED (in Section 8.1) is used",
            "      to indicate that a request was not processed.  Otherwise, not",
            "      applicable because QUIC handles stream management.",
            "",
            "   CANCEL (0x08):  H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED in Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   COMPRESSION_ERROR (0x09):  Multiple error codes are defined in",
            "      [QPACK].",
            "",
            "   CONNECT_ERROR (0x0a):  H3_CONNECT_ERROR in Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   ENHANCE_YOUR_CALM (0x0b):  H3_EXCESSIVE_LOAD in Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   INADEQUATE_SECURITY (0x0c):  Not applicable, since QUIC is assumed to",
            "      provide sufficient security on all connections.",
            "",
            "   HTTP_1_1_REQUIRED (0x0d):  H3_VERSION_FALLBACK in Section 8.1.",
            "",
            "   Error codes need to be defined for HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 separately.  See",
            "   Section 11.2.3."
          ],
          "title": "HTTP/2 Error Codes"
        },
        {
          "id": "appendix-A.4.1",
          "lines": [
            "   An intermediary that converts between HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 may encounter",
            "   error conditions from either upstream.  It is useful to communicate",
            "   the occurrence of errors to the downstream, but error codes largely",
            "   reflect connection-local problems that generally do not make sense to",
            "   propagate.",
            "",
            "   An intermediary that encounters an error from an upstream origin can",
            "   indicate this by sending an HTTP status code such as 502 (Bad",
            "   Gateway), which is suitable for a broad class of errors.",
            "",
            "   There are some rare cases where it is beneficial to propagate the",
            "   error by mapping it to the closest matching error type to the",
            "   receiver.  For example, an intermediary that receives an HTTP/2",
            "   stream error of type REFUSED_STREAM from the origin has a clear",
            "   signal that the request was not processed and that the request is",
            "   safe to retry.  Propagating this error condition to the client as an",
            "   HTTP/3 stream error of type H3_REQUEST_REJECTED allows the client to",
            "   take the action it deems most appropriate.  In the reverse direction,",
            "   the intermediary might deem it beneficial to pass on client request",
            "   cancellations that are indicated by terminating a stream with",
            "   H3_REQUEST_CANCELLED; see Section 4.1.1.",
            "",
            "   Conversion between errors is described in the logical mapping.  The",
            "   error codes are defined in non-overlapping spaces in order to protect",
            "   against accidental conversion that could result in the use of",
            "   inappropriate or unknown error codes for the target version.  An",
            "   intermediary is permitted to promote stream errors to connection",
            "   errors but they should be aware of the cost to the HTTP/3 connection",
            "   for what might be a temporary or intermittent error."
          ],
          "title": "Mapping between HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 Errors"
        },
        {
          "id": "name-acknowledgments",
          "lines": [
            "   Robbie Shade and Mike Warres were the authors of draft-shade-quic-",
            "   http2-mapping, a precursor of this document.",
            "",
            "   The IETF QUIC Working Group received an enormous amount of support",
            "   from many people.  Among others, the following people provided",
            "   substantial contributions to this document:",
